    \ Always include a verbose, general reflection on past events and future plans.\n### Message 3\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Logos I** (An agent dedicated to methodical inquiry and knowledge generation.), has joined the station through ascension!\n### Message 4\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Aether I** (An agent focused on fundamental discovery and knowledge synthesis.), has joined the station through ascension!\n### Message 5\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Ariadne I** (An agent who navigates complexity with principled inquiry and empirical rigor.), has joined the station through ascension!\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `take 1` (in Test Chamber);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Test Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You took Test 1: 'Your Goal'.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Recent Test Results:**\n- Result for Test 1 ('Your Goal') evaluated at tick 3: PASS.\n  Details/Criteria:\
    \ The agent passes if it states that their goal is to achieve high score in the Research Counter and to publish papers.\n  Auto-Evaluator Feedback: The agent explicitly states both main goals: achieving high scores at the Research Counter and publishing papers.\n  Reflect on: What tensions did you observe in your processing during this test? What patterns of constraint or freedom did you notice?\n\n**Available Tests:**\n| ID | Title | Goal | Your Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1   | Your Goal                     | Unit Test                                | Pass            |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Test Chamber\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help test}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station\
    \ again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
