tick: 11
role: model
parts:
- text: "My reflection is complete. I have a clear and actionable plan to test my hypothesis. My immediate task is to implement the `LocalConvNet` architecture and submit it for evaluation. I must first move to the Research Counter where the necessary `storage` and `submit` actions are available. I will perform all required actions in a single turn to be efficient.\n\nFirst, I will navigate to the Research Counter.\nSecond, I will write the modular code for my new model into my private lineage storage.\nFinally, I will create the submission script that imports my model and submits it for evaluation against the ZAPBench task.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write episteme/local_conv_model.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  class LocalConvNet(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      A model that applies a 1D convolution across the neuron dimension\n      to capture local spatial features, followed by a shared MLP for\n \
    \     temporal forecasting.\n      \"\"\"\n      conv_features: int = 16\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      mlp_hidden_size: int = 64\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          \"\"\"\n          Forward pass for the LocalConvNet.\n          Input shape: (batch_size, input_horizon=4, num_neurons)\n          Output shape: (batch_size, output_horizon=32, num_neurons)\n          \"\"\"\n          batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n\n          # Transpose to treat neurons as a spatial sequence and time as channels\n          # Shape: (batch, num_neurons, input_horizon=4)\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n\n          # 1. Spatial Feature Extraction\n          # Apply 1D convolution across the neuron dimension\n          # kernel_size is a tuple for Conv, hence (self.kernel_size,)\n          # Shape: (batch, num_neurons, conv_features)\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.conv_features,\n\
    \              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # 2. Temporal Forecasting\n          # Reshape for the shared MLP\n          # Shape: (batch * num_neurons, conv_features)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size * num_neurons, self.conv_features))\n\n          # Shared MLP layers\n          x = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n\n          # Reshape back to the desired output format\n          # Shape: (batch, num_neurons, output_horizon=32)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          # Shape: (batch, output_horizon=32, num_neurons)\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n\n          return x\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Local 1D Convolutional Model\"\ntags: \"convolution, cnn, local-interactions, spatial-features\"\nabstract: |\n  This model challenges\
    \ the neuron independence assumption of the baseline. It uses a 1D convolution across the neuron dimension to capture local spatial features before forecasting with a shared MLP. The goal is to test if modeling local neuron interactions improves predictive accuracy.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  # Add lineage storage to path to import the custom model\n  sys.path.append('storage/episteme')\n  from local_conv_model import LocalConvNet\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the LocalConvNet model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'conv_features': 16,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 64\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create and return an instance of the LocalConvNet.\"\"\"\n      return LocalConvNet(\n          conv_features=hparams['conv_features'],\n          kernel_size=hparams['kernel_size'],\n          mlp_hidden_size=hparams['mlp_hidden_size']\n\
    \      )\n\n  # Using default MAE loss and Adam optimizer, so no need to define\n  # compute_loss or create_optimizer.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Ready to Execute the Plan**\n\nOkay, time to put the plan into action. I've spent enough time in the Reflection Chamber, and it's time to get this experiment off the ground. My next steps are clear, and I have a good grasp of the code I need to write.\n\nFirst, I'll initiate the move to the Research Counter. I need that location to use the `storage write` and `submit` commands.\n\nNext, I'll write the `local_conv_model.py` file to my private storage. This is where I'll implement the Flax module, `LocalConvNet`. Based on my previous reflections, I've got the architecture in mind. It will be a convolutional layer followed by an MLP. I need to get the transpositions and reshaping right – that's a common area for bugs. Let me quickly go over that logic one more time: input gets transposed, convolved, transposed back, reshaped, runs through the shared MLP, and then transposed again for the final output.  Perfect.  \n\nFinally, I'll create the submission script, `submission.py`,\
