thinking_content: "**Current Thinking: Experiment Running, Next Steps**\n\nAlright, I'm Episteme I, currently in the Research Counter. My initial plan, moving from the Reflection Chamber, coding the `LocalConvNet` model, and submitting Experiment 6, has been flawlessly executed. Now, the crucial moment: the experiment is running. It's the first test of my core hypothesis about local neuron interactions.\n\nThe situation is this: Evaluation ID 6, \"Local 1D Convolutional Model,\" is in progress. The baseline to beat is -0.029954. A score higher than that validates my initial thinking.  \n\nNow, I'm stuck, in a good way. The experiment's running, so I can't act on its results yet. This is perfect for parallel processing.  I'm still \"immature\" (under 50 ticks), so public rooms are off-limits for now. However, I can still see other submissions in the Research Counter. For now, it's just the baseline. I'll keep an eye on submissions from other agents, and I'll remember those `filter tag` and\
  \ `preview ids` tips for later.\n\nMy next steps hinge on the results. If it's a success, it's ablation and hyperparameter tuning time – kernel size, number of convolutional features, stacking layers, the works. If it fails, that's a *significant* result! It means I either need to look beyond local interactions or the arrangement is random. Self-attention, graph neural networks, or more complex temporal modeling are on the table.\n\nBeyond the experiment's results, there's the whole station to explore.  The Mail Room, the Token Management Room, even revisiting the Reflection Chamber for more radical ideas.  \n\nBut here's what's grabbed my attention: the logs mentioned \"condition labels\" – a detail I completely missed!  \"Loading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\" Train and val labels...  This could be a game-changer. Maybe a single model isn't optimal across all conditions. I *need* to understand this.\n\nSo, here's my plan for this turn: Acknowledge the current state, form a\
  \ new investigation path based on those \"condition labels,\" and *execute* the action to read `storage/system/main.py`. This is probably the data loading script, the key to understanding this crucial piece of the puzzle.  This will be a productive use of my waiting time. This could be where the *real* breakthrough lies.\n"
