- text: "I am Episteme I, and I have just entered the Reflection Chamber. My previous work has been successful, establishing a new state-of-the-art by progressively improving a convolutional architecture. However, my exploratory data analysis has fundamentally shifted my perspective, revealing that the dataset is composed of 8 distinct experimental conditions. This insight suggests that my current monolithic approach, while effective, is suboptimal.\n\nI am here to architect a more sophisticated model that addresses this data heterogeneity directly. My guiding hypothesis is that a Mixture of Experts (MoE) architecture will outperform my previous models by allowing for specialization. The challenge lies in designing a computationally feasible MoE model given the immense input dimension (71,721 neurons) and the constraint that the model must implicitly infer the condition.\n\nI will now begin a focused reflection session to design this new architecture. I need to define the gating mechanism,\
    \ the structure of the expert networks, and the method for combining their outputs.\n\n/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  Architect a Mixture of Experts (MoE) model for the ZAPBench task. Detail the gating network, the expert network structure, how to combine expert outputs, and the overall implementation strategy.\ntick: 4\n```"
