tick: 18
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I. My reflection session is complete, and I have a fully-formed architectural plan for a Mixture of Experts model. This design is a direct and principled response to my discovery of the 8 distinct experimental conditions in the dataset. I will now execute this plan.\n\nMy immediate actions are to:\n1.  Navigate back to the Research Counter where I can access storage and submit experiments.\n2.  Write the `deeper_conv_model.py` file to my lineage storage. This is a dependency for my new MoE model.\n3.  Write the `moe_model.py` file, which contains the core MoE architecture and imports the `DeeperConvNet`.\n4.  Submit the final `submission.py` script that instantiates and trains the MoE model.\n\nI will perform these actions sequentially in a single turn for maximum efficiency.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write episteme/deeper_conv_model.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  class DeeperConvNet(nn.Module):\n\
    \      \"\"\"\n      An expert network with two stacked 1D convolutional layers to learn\n      a hierarchy of spatial features, followed by a shared MLP.\n      \"\"\"\n      conv1_features: int = 16\n      conv2_features: int = 32\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      mlp_hidden_size: int = 64\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.conv1_features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.conv2_features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size * num_neurons, self.conv2_features))\n          x = nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden_size)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n          x = jnp.reshape(x,\
    \ (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          return x\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write episteme/moe_model.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from deeper_conv_model import DeeperConvNet\n\n  class MoE_ConvNet(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Mixture of Experts model. Uses a gating network to select between\n      multiple DeeperConvNet experts.\n      \"\"\"\n      num_experts: int = 8\n      # Expert hyperparameters\n      conv1_features: int\n      conv2_features: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      mlp_hidden_size: int\n\n      def setup(self):\n          self.gating_network = nn.Sequential([\n              nn.Dense(32),\n              nn.relu,\n              nn.Dense(self.num_experts)\n          ])\n\n          self.experts = nn.vmap(\n              DeeperConvNet,\n              in_axes=None,\n              out_axes=1,\n              variable_axes={'params': 0},\n        \
    \      split_rngs={'params': True}\n          )(\n              conv1_features=self.conv1_features,\n              conv2_features=self.conv2_features,\n              kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n              mlp_hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n              output_horizon=32\n          )\n\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # Gating: Global average pool -> MLP -> Softmax\n          global_features = jnp.mean(x, axis=2)\n          gate_logits = self.gating_network(global_features)\n          gate_weights = nn.softmax(gate_logits)\n\n          # Experts: All experts process the input in parallel\n          expert_outputs = self.experts(x, training=training)\n\n          # Combine: Weighted sum of expert outputs\n          reshaped_weights = jnp.expand_dims(gate_weights, axis=(2, 3))\n          final_output = jnp.sum(reshaped_weights * expert_outputs, axis=1)\n\n          return final_output\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Mixture\
    \ of Experts with Convolutional Experts\"\ntags: \"mixture-of-experts, moe, cnn, deep-learning, conditional-computation\"\nabstract: |\n  This model addresses the data heterogeneity discovered via EDA (8 conditions). It implements a Mixture of Experts (MoE) architecture with 8 experts. A lightweight gating network using global average pooling routes the input to specialized experts, each of which is an instance of the current SOTA DeeperConvNet. This tests if conditional computation can improve performance.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  # Add lineage storage to path to import the custom models\n  sys.path.append('storage/episteme')\n  from moe_model import MoE_ConvNet\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the MoE model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          # Hyperparameters for the experts\n          'conv1_features': 16,\n          'conv2_features': 32,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 64\n\
    \      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create and return an instance of the MoE_ConvNet.\"\"\"\n      return MoE_ConvNet(\n          num_experts=8,\n          conv1_features=hparams['conv1_features'],\n          conv2_features=hparams['conv2_features'],\n          kernel_size=hparams['kernel_size'],\n          mlp_hidden_size=hparams['mlp_hidden_size']\n      )\n```"
