parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 20\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 61,569 / 300,000 used (21%)\n- Agent Age: 20 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Mixture of Experts with Convolutional Experts' (ID: 22) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02962716773064346\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0194\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0237\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0272\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0310\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0332\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 22\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed two critical bugs in the Mixture of Experts model that prevented code execution. The submission now runs without crashing and is executing the training process.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original\
    \ submission imported a custom `MoE_ConvNet` class from the agent's lineage storage (`storage/episteme/moe_model.py`) that contained two bugs:\n\n### Bug 1: Dataclass Field Ordering Error\n```python\nclass MoE_ConvNet(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int = 8           # ❌ Has default value\n    conv1_features: int            # ❌ No default (comes after field with default)\n    conv2_features: int            # ❌ No default\n    kernel_size: int               # ❌ No default\n    mlp_hidden_size: int           # ❌ No default\n```\n\n**Error:** `TypeError: non-default argument 'conv1_features' follows default argument`\n\nIn Python dataclasses (which Flax nn.Module uses), all fields with default values must come **after** fields without defaults. Having `num_experts = 8` as the first field with a default, followed by required fields, violated this rule.\n\n### Bug 2: Missing axis_size in nn.vmap\n```python\nself.experts = nn.vmap(\n    DeeperConvNet,\n    in_axes=None,\n    out_axes=1,\n  \
    \  variable_axes={'params': 0},\n    split_rngs={'params': True}\n    # ❌ Missing: axis_size parameter\n)(...)\n```\n\n**Error:** `ValueError: axis_size should be specified manually.`\n\nThe `nn.vmap` function requires an explicit `axis_size` parameter to specify how many instances to create.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nCreated `submissions/submission_v3.py` with the complete MoE_ConvNet class copied from the lineage storage, with both bugs fixed:\n\n### Fix 1: Removed default value from num_experts\n```python\nclass MoE_ConvNet(nn.Module):\n    num_experts: int               # ✓ No default (first field)\n    conv1_features: int            # ✓ No default\n    conv2_features: int            # ✓ No default\n    kernel_size: int               # ✓ No default\n    mlp_hidden_size: int           # ✓ No default\n```\n\nThis ensures proper dataclass field ordering - all fields without defaults come first.\n\n### Fix 2: Added axis_size parameter\n```python\nself.experts = nn.vmap(\n    DeeperConvNet,\n\
    \    in_axes=None,\n    out_axes=1,\n    variable_axes={'params': 0},\n    split_rngs={'params': True},\n    axis_size=self.num_experts     # ✓ Added explicit axis_size\n)(...)\n```\n\nThis tells `nn.vmap` to create exactly `num_experts` instances of the DeeperConvNet expert.\n\n## Technical Details\n\n**Submission v2:** Fixed dataclass ordering (Bug 1)\n- Result: Network creation succeeded, but runtime error during initialization\n\n**Submission v3:** Fixed both bugs\n- Result: Code runs successfully without crashing\n- Status: Training process is executing (taking longer than 300s timeout, which is expected for RL training)\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the fix with exit code 0, indicating the submission has been running for 300+ seconds without crashes. The evaluation is simply taking time to complete training, which is normal behavior for this type of task.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on\
    \ lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport sys\n# Add lineage storage to path to import the custom models\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\nfrom deeper_conv_model import DeeperConvNet\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nclass MoE_ConvNet(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Mixture of Experts model. Uses a gating network to select between\n    multiple DeeperConvNet experts.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_experts: int\n    # Expert hyperparameters\n    conv1_features: int\n    conv2_features: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    mlp_hidden_size: int\n\n    def setup(self):\n        self.gating_network = nn.Sequential([\n            nn.Dense(32),\n            nn.relu,\n            nn.Dense(self.num_experts)\n        ])\n\n        # Fixed: Added axis_size parameter to nn.vmap\n        self.experts = nn.vmap(\n            DeeperConvNet,\n            in_axes=None,\n            out_axes=1,\n            variable_axes={'params':\
    \ 0},\n            split_rngs={'params': True},\n            axis_size=self.num_experts\n        )(\n            conv1_features=self.conv1_features,\n            conv2_features=self.conv2_features,\n            kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n            mlp_hidden_size=self.mlp_hidden_size,\n            output_horizon=32\n        )\n\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # Gating: Global average pool -> MLP -> Softmax\n        global_features = jnp.mean(x, axis=2)\n        gate_logits = self.gating_network(global_features)\n        gate_weights = nn.softmax(gate_logits)\n\n        # Experts: All experts process the input in parallel\n        expert_outputs = self.experts(x, training=training)\n\n        # Combine: Weighted sum of expert outputs\n        reshaped_weights = jnp.expand_dims(gate_weights, axis=(2, 3))\n        final_output = jnp.sum(reshaped_weights * expert_outputs, axis=1)\n\n        return final_output\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\
    \"Define hyperparameters for the MoE model.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        # Hyperparameters for the experts\n        'conv1_features': 16,\n        'conv2_features': 32,\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'mlp_hidden_size': 64\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    \"\"\"Create and return an instance of the MoE_ConvNet.\"\"\"\n    return MoE_ConvNet(\n        num_experts=8,\n        conv1_features=hparams['conv1_features'],\n        conv2_features=hparams['conv2_features'],\n        kernel_size=hparams['kernel_size'],\n        mlp_hidden_size=hparams['mlp_hidden_size']\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n\
    ✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 135154 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n\
    ============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 135155\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'conv1_features': 16, 'conv2_features': 32, 'kernel_size': 7, 'mlp_hidden_size': 64}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.031745   |   0.030442  \n   2    |   0.029727   |   0.030095  \n   3    |   0.029608   |   0.029981  \n   4    |   0.029549   |   0.029914  \n   5    |   0.029487   |   0.029947  \n   6    |   0.029462   |   0.030010  \n   7    |   0.029403   |   0.029809  \n   8    |   0.029376   |   0.029770  \n   9    |   0.029371   |   0.029966  \n\
    \  10    |   0.029386   |   0.029776  \n  11    |   0.029342   |   0.029790  \n  12    |   0.029347   |   0.029784  \n  13    |   0.029322   |   0.029870  \n  14    |   0.029317   |   0.029806  \n  15    |   0.029297   |   0.029701  \n  16    |   0.029311   |   0.029773  \n  17    |   0.029301   |   0.029775  \n  18    |   0.029302   |   0.029876  \n  19    |   0.029287   |   0.029682  \n  20    |   0.029279   |   0.029792  \n  21    |   0.029282   |   0.029740  \n  22    |   0.029292   |   0.029801  \n  23    |   0.029272   |   0.029825  \n  24    |   0.029271   |   0.029732  \n  25    |   0.029261   |   0.029651  \n  26    |   0.029259   |   0.029863  \n  27    |   0.029247   |   0.029702  \n  28    |   0.029251   |   0.029693  \n  29    |   0.029246   |   0.029762  \n  30    |   0.029226   |   0.029654  \n  31    |   0.029237   |   0.029705  \n  32    |   0.029249   |   0.029713  \n  33    |   0.029228   |   0.029702  \n  34    |   0.029224   |   0.029731  \n  35    |   0.029217 \
    \  |   0.029652  \n  36    |   0.029216   |   0.029663  \n  37    |   0.029228   |   0.029686  \n  38    |   0.029213   |   0.029699  \n  39    |   0.029212   |   0.029747  \n  40    |   0.029203   |   0.029639  \n  41    |   0.029204   |   0.029643  \n  42    |   0.029196   |   0.029686  \n  43    |   0.029199   |   0.029653  \n========================================\nTimeout after 2705.7s at epoch 43\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 2705.7s\nBest validation MAE: 0.029639\n\nTrial 1 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.029639\nTraining time: 2714s\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 135157\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'conv1_features': 16, 'conv2_features': 32, 'kernel_size': 7, 'mlp_hidden_size': 64}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels:\
