parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 35\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **SOTA:** MoE with Convolutional Gater (ID 30, Score: -0.028995)\n- **Goal:** Publish a paper upon reaching maturity (Age 50).\n- **Current Research Program:** Investigating low-rank factorization.\n- **Current Action:** Previous factor models are flawed. Now testing a recurrent (GRU) forecaster on a latent sequence\
    \ to better model dynamics.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 121,108 / 300,000 used (40%)\n- Agent Age: 35 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Factor Model with Recurrent (GRU) Forecaster' (ID: 55) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.030903160699756266\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0389\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0299\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0302\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0307\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0312\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 55\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The code has been fixed and is now running without crashing. The submission has been running for over 300 seconds, confirming the fix resolved the issue.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code imported `FactorRNNModel` from the lineage file `storage/episteme/factor_rnn_model.py`, which contained a bug on line 27:\n\n```python\ngru_cell = nn.GRUCell()\n```\n\nThe `nn.GRUCell()` constructor\
    \ was called without the required `features` argument, causing a `TypeError`:\n```\nTypeError: GRUCell.__init__() missing 1 required positional argument: 'features'\n```\n\nIn Flax's neural network library, `GRUCell` requires specifying the number of features (hidden state size) it should operate on.\n\n## Fix Applied\nI created `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Copied the entire `FactorRNNModel` class** from the lineage file into the submission\n2. **Fixed line 27** by adding the required `features` argument:\n   ```python\n   gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.num_factors)\n   ```\n3. **Kept the hyperparameters and create_network functions** from the original submission\n\nThe fix ensures that the GRU cell knows it should operate on `num_factors` dimensional vectors (64 in this case based on the hyperparameters), which matches the dimensionality of the factor sequence being processed.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Bug location**: `storage/episteme/factor_rnn_model.py:27`\n\
    - **Fix location**: `submissions/submission_v2.py:27`\n- **Key change**: Added `features=self.num_factors` parameter to `nn.GRUCell()`\n- **Verification**: Code ran successfully for 300+ seconds without crashes\n\nThe fix is minimal and surgical - only the buggy function was copied and corrected, maintaining the original algorithm's logic and structure.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom typing import Sequence\n\nclass FactorRNNModel(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    A more advanced factor model. It projects the 4-step input history into a\n    4-step latent factor sequence, then uses a GRU to recurrently forecast\n    the next 32 steps in the latent space.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_factors: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n\
    \        batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n        output_horizon = 32\n\n        # 1. Encoder: Project each of the 4 timesteps into the factor space.\n        # This is just a linear projection (the loading matrix).\n        loadings = self.param('loadings', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (num_neurons, self.num_factors))\n        # Input x: (batch, 4, N)\n        # x @ L -> (batch, 4, k)\n        factor_sequence = jnp.matmul(x, loadings)\n\n        # 2. Forecaster: Use a GRU to predict the future.\n        # FIX: Added features argument to GRUCell\n        gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.num_factors)\n        # Get initial hidden state from the mean of the input sequence.\n        hidden_state = jnp.mean(factor_sequence, axis=1)\n\n        # Autoregressive forecasting loop for 32 steps.\n        outputs = []\n        # The last factor state from the input sequence is the first input to the GRU.\n        current_factor = factor_sequence[:, -1, :]\n        for _\
    \ in range(output_horizon):\n            hidden_state, current_factor = gru_cell(hidden_state, current_factor)\n            outputs.append(current_factor)\n\n        # Stack the outputs to create the forecasted sequence.\n        forecasted_factors = jnp.stack(outputs, axis=1) # Shape: (batch, 32, k)\n\n        # 3. Decoder: Use the same loading matrix to reconstruct neuron activity.\n        # (batch, 32, k) @ (k, N) -> (batch, 32, N)\n        reconstructed_output = jnp.matmul(forecasted_factors, jnp.transpose(loadings, (1, 0)))\n\n        return reconstructed_output\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'num_factors': 64\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return FactorRNNModel(\n        num_factors=hparams['num_factors']\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\n\
    Validating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 157241 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting\
    \ Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 157242\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'num_factors': 64}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.057783   |   0.032394  \n   2    |   0.032720   |   0.031745  \n   3    |   0.031922   |   0.031339  \n   4    |   0.031351   |   0.030909  \n   5    |   0.030898   |   0.031469  \n   6    |   1.912723   |   1.751510\
    \  \n   7    |   0.701096   |   0.217929  \n   8    |   0.101622   |   0.052926  \n   9    |   0.044542   |   0.038798  \n  10    |   0.037377   |   0.035929  \n  11    |   0.035104   |   0.034036  \n  12    |   0.033924   |   0.033336  \n  13    |   0.033262   |   0.033430  \n  14    |   0.032862   |   0.032510  \n  15    |   0.032459   |   0.033762  \n  16    |   0.032127   |   0.032591  \n  17    |   0.031916   |   0.032607  \n  18    |   0.031805   |   0.031974  \n  19    |   0.031720   |   0.032081  \n  20    |   0.031464   |   0.032811  \n  21    |   0.031436   |   0.031521  \n  22    |   0.031773   |   0.033943  \n  23    |   0.031415   |   0.031865  \n  24    |   0.031057   |   0.031124  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 24 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 1567.1s\nBest validation MAE: 0.030909\n\nTrial 1 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.030909\nTraining time: 1573s\n\nStarting ZAPBench training -\
