tick: 37
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 37\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **SOTA:** MoE with Convolutional Gater (ID 30, Score: -0.028995)\n- **Goal:** Publish a paper upon reaching maturity (Age 50).\n- **Current Research Program:** Investigating low-rank factorization.\n- **Current Action:** Previous factor models are flawed. Now testing a recurrent (GRU) forecaster on a latent sequence\
    \ to better model dynamics.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 132,203 / 300,000 used (44%)\n- Agent Age: 37 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Factor Model with Encoder-Decoder GRU' (ID: 60) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.03132355494697061\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0443\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0309\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0303\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0307\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0314\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 60\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the Flax `NameInUseError` by removing duplicate module name definitions. The code is now running without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code in `storage/episteme/robust_factor_rnn_model.py` contained multiple attempts at implementing the encoder, with leftover experimental code that was never cleaned up. Specifically, there were three instances of creating a Dense layer\
    \ with the name \"Encoder\":\n\n1. Line 18: `encoder = nn.Dense(features=self.num_factors, name=\"Encoder\")`\n2. Line 32: `latent_per_neuron = nn.Dense(features=self.num_factors, name=\"Encoder\")(...)`\n3. Line 39: `encoder_mlp = nn.Dense(self.num_factors, name=\"Encoder\")`\n\nIn Flax's `@nn.compact` decorator mode, all submodules must have unique names. The code attempted to create multiple Dense layers with the same name \"Encoder\", which caused the error:\n\n```\nflax.errors.NameInUseError: Could not create submodule \"Encoder\" in Module RobustFactorRNNModel: Name in use.\n```\n\nThe lines 18-35 were dead code from earlier experimental attempts that were commented out but not removed, while lines 39-59 contained the actual working implementation.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the cleaned-up version of `RobustFactorRNNModel`:\n\n1. **Removed dead code** (lines 18-35 from the original file) that contained duplicate \"Encoder\" module definitions\n\
    2. **Kept the working implementation** (lines 39-59) that properly defines the encoder-decoder architecture:\n   - Single Encoder MLP that projects neurons to latent factors\n   - GRU forecaster for temporal prediction in latent space\n   - Decoder MLP that projects latent factors back to neuron space\n3. **Included the required interface functions** (`_define_hyperparameters()` and `create_network()`)\n\nThe fix maintains the agent's intended architecture (a proper encoder-decoder factor model with GRU) while eliminating the naming conflict.\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- The submission passed the simple CPU validation phase that was failing before\n- Status: Code is running successfully (evaluation may still be in progress for full training)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code\
    \ (version v2):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nclass RobustFactorRNNModel(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    A robust factor model with a dedicated non-linear MLP encoder and decoder.\n    This addresses the flaws of previous models (shared linear projection).\n    \"\"\"\n    num_factors: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n        output_horizon = 32\n\n        # Encoder: projects neuron space to factor space for each of the 4 timesteps\n        encoder_mlp = nn.Dense(self.num_factors, name=\"Encoder\")\n        factor_sequence = jax.vmap(encoder_mlp, in_axes=1, out_axes=1)(x) # (batch, 4, k)\n\n        # 2. Forecaster: GRU predicts future latent states.\n        gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.num_factors)\n        hidden_state = jnp.mean(factor_sequence, axis=1)\n\n        outputs = []\n        current_factor = factor_sequence[:, -1, :]\n\
    \        for _ in range(output_horizon):\n            hidden_state, current_factor = gru_cell(hidden_state, current_factor)\n            outputs.append(current_factor)\n\n        forecasted_factors = jnp.stack(outputs, axis=1)\n\n        # 3. Decoder: A separate MLP projects factor space back to neuron space.\n        decoder_mlp = nn.Dense(features=num_neurons, name=\"Decoder\")\n        # Apply the decoder to each of the 32 forecasted factor states\n        reconstructed_output = jax.vmap(decoder_mlp, in_axes=1, out_axes=1)(forecasted_factors)\n\n        return reconstructed_output\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return { 'learning_rate': 0.001, 'num_factors': 64 }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return RobustFactorRNNModel(num_factors=hparams['num_factors'])\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function\
    \ loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 161668 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench\
    \ Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 161670\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'num_factors': 64}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.736322   |   0.042791  \n   2    |   0.039451   |   0.036061  \n   3    |   0.036301   |   0.035283  \n   4    |   0.035527   |   0.035205  \n   5    |   0.035760   |   0.035480  \n   6    |   0.036891   |   0.037975  \n   7  \
    \  |   0.037952   |   0.037966  \n   8    |   0.037886   |   0.037751  \n   9    |   0.037798   |   0.037304  \n  10    |   0.037542   |   0.037055  \n  11    |   0.037129   |   0.036429  \n  12    |   0.036698   |   0.037236  \n  13    |   0.036428   |   0.036434  \n  14    |   0.036068   |   0.038066  \n  15    |   0.035403   |   0.035023  \n  16    |   0.034732   |   0.033842  \n  17    |   0.033788   |   0.033349  \n  18    |   0.032865   |   0.032232  \n  19    |   0.031997   |   0.032483  \n  20    |   0.031646   |   0.032849  \n  21    |   0.031171   |   0.031810  \n  22    |   0.030973   |   0.032378  \n  23    |   0.301177   |   0.122561  \n  24    |   0.070003   |   0.049124  \n  25    |   0.046399   |   0.041800  \n  26    |   0.040913   |   0.039962  \n  27    |   0.038802   |   0.038494  \n  28    |   0.037316   |   0.037896  \n  29    |   0.036211   |   0.037111  \n  30    |   0.035408   |   0.035472  \n  31    |   0.034465   |   0.035552  \n  32    |   0.033593   |   0.034001\
