- text: "I am Epistemte I, currently in the Research Counter. I have completed the process of documenting the failure of my low-rank factorization research program and have cleaned up the relevant buggy code file. My strategic pivot is now complete, and I am ready to resume work on my successful MoE-ConvGate architecture.\n\nMy meta prompt is out of date, as the decision it outlines has now been made. I will first update it to reflect my new focus.\n\nFollowing my protocol, the next step is to design a new experiment. The most principled path forward is to begin a systematic optimization of my SOTA model (ID 30). The learning rate is a fundamental hyperparameter, and my successful model used the default value of 0.001. It is highly probable that this is not optimal for such a complex architecture.\n\n*Hypothesis:* Reducing the learning rate for the MoE-ConvGate architecture will lead to more stable training and a better final convergence, resulting in a score superior to the current SOTA.\n\
    \nI will test this by submitting a new experiment that is identical to my SOTA model (ID 30) but with a learning rate reduced by a factor of three, to approximately 0.0003. This is a standard practice in deep learning when refining a successful model.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Episteme I Research Protocol**\n  1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n  2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n  3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n  4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n  ---\n  **Current Status & Goals:**\n  - **SOTA:** MoE with Convolutional Gater (ID 30, Score: -0.028995)\n  - **Goal:** Publish a paper upon reaching maturity (Age 50).\n  - **Current Research Program:** Refinement and optimization of the MoE-ConvGate architecture.\n  - **Current Action:** Testing\
    \ the effect of a lower learning rate.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MoE-ConvGate with Lower Learning Rate\"\ntags: \"mixture-of-experts, moe, convolutional-gater, optimization, learning-rate\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment marks a return to the successful MoE-ConvGate architecture (ID 30) after abandoning the low-rank factorization research program. It tests the hypothesis that the SOTA model, which was trained with a default learning rate, can be improved through basic hyperparameter optimization. The learning rate is reduced from 0.001 to 0.0003 to seek more stable convergence.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/episteme')\n  # I will reuse the moe_conv_gater_model.py file from my successful SOTA.\n  from moe_conv_gater_model import MoE_ConvGater_Net\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameters for the MoE-ConvGate model.\n      The only change from ID 30 is the reduced learning rate.\n      \"\"\"\n  \
    \    return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.0003, # Reduced from 0.001\n          'conv1_features': 16,\n          'conv2_features': 32,\n          'kernel_size': 7,\n          'mlp_hidden_size': 64\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create an instance of the MoE_ConvGater_Net.\"\"\"\n      return MoE_ConvGater_Net(\n          num_experts=8,\n          conv1_features=hparams['conv1_features'],\n          conv2_features=hparams['conv2_features'],\n          kernel_size=hparams['kernel_size'],\n          mlp_hidden_size=hparams['mlp_hidden_size']\n      )\n```"
