parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Research Counter. The results for my \"MoE with Deeper Gating Network\" experiment (ID 81) are in.\n\n**1. Observe & Analyze:**\nThe score is **-0.028947**. This is another null result. It is slightly worse than my current SOTA of -0.028910 (ID 76). My hypothesis that a more powerful gating network would improve performance has been falsified. This suggests that the original, simpler `ConvGater` is sufficient and that adding more complexity to the gater does not yield benefits, and may even be slightly detrimental. This marks the end of the most obvious architectural optimizations for my MoE model. I have found a local optimum for learning rate, expert capacity, and gater capacity.\n\n**2. Formulate Hypothesis / Strategic Direction:**\nMy systematic refinement has reached a point of diminishing returns. Further tweaks to this architecture are unlikely to produce a breakthrough. It is time to step back and think more broadly. I have a SOTA model, a compelling\
    \ research narrative documented in my private memory, and I am approaching maturity (Age 50). My primary goal is to publish. My current publication draft is strong, but it lacks a crucial component required by the Codex for a truly rigorous paper: a direct baseline comparison that I have run myself.\n\n*New Strategic Direction:* I will pause novel architectural development and focus on preparing my research for publication. To fulfill the Codex requirements, I must reproduce the system baseline (ID 1) myself. This will provide the necessary control experiment for my paper and ensure my claims of improvement are built on a solid, self-verified foundation.\n\n**3. Design & Experiment:**\nThe experiment is simple: submit the exact code for the baseline model to generate my own evaluation. The baseline code is found in `system/defaults.py` and uses an empty `submission.py` file.\n\n**4. Consolidate Knowledge & Plan Actions:**\nI will update my private memory and meta prompt to reflect this\
    \ new, pre-publication phase of my research. Then, I will submit the baseline run.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 3}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  ## Entry 7: MoE with Deeper Gating Network (ID 81)\n\n  *   **Hypothesis:** A deeper, more complex gating network would learn more discriminative features and improve the SOTA score.\n  *   **Methodology:** The SOTA model (ID 76) was modified to use a `DeeperConvGater` with more layers and less aggressive striding.\n  *   **Result:** The model achieved a score of -0.028947, which is worse than the SOTA (-0.028910). The hypothesis was falsified.\n  *   **Analysis:** This null result concludes the initial phase of architectural optimization. The simpler gater from ID 30/76 appears to be sufficient. Further improvements will likely require a more novel idea rather than incremental complexity increases. The focus now shifts to preparing the existing body of work for publication.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\
    \n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Episteme I Research Protocol**\n  1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n  2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n  3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n  4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n  ---\n  **Current Status & Goals:**\n  - **SOTA:** MoE with High-Capacity Experts (ID 76, Score: -0.028910)\n  - **Goal:** Publish a paper upon reaching maturity (Age 50).\n  - **Current Research Program:** Pre-publication validation.\n  - **Current Action:** Reproducing the system baseline (ID 1) as a control for my paper.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Baseline Reproduction (for Publication Control)\"\ntags: \"baseline, reproduction, control-experiment, publication\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission is not intended to advance\
    \ the state-of-the-art. Its purpose is to reproduce the system baseline (Shared-Neuron MLP, ID 1) under my own name. This is a necessary control experiment to fulfill the requirements of the Codex for a formal research paper, providing a self-verified baseline against which my novel architectures can be compared.\ncontent: |\n  # This submission intentionally uses the system default network.\n  # The purpose is to create a baseline run under my own name\n  # for inclusion as a control experiment in my research paper.\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Use default hyperparameters for the shared MLP.\"\"\"\n      return {'learning_rate': 0.001}\n\n  # All other functions (create_network, etc.) will use system defaults.\n```"
