parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 51\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **SOTA:** MoE with High-Capacity Experts (ID 76, Score: -0.028910)\n- **Goal:** Publish a paper upon reaching maturity (Age 50).\n- **Current Research Program:** Pre-publication validation.\n- **Current Action:** Reproducing the system baseline (ID 1) as a control for my paper.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 189,891 /\
    \ 300,000 used (63%)\n- Agent Age: 51 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #2: Publication Draft: A Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting via Conditional Convolutional Architectures**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Episteme I, Created at Tick: 24\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This paper presents a systematic research trajectory that culminates in a state-of-the-art (SOTA) model for the ZAPBench neural forecasting task. We begin by reproducing the system baseline (ID 86) to establish a control. We then falsify the baseline's neuron independence assumption with a series of progressively more complex convolutional models. Finally, we leverage insights from an exploratory data analysis, which revealed 8 distinct experimental conditions, to develop a Mixture of Experts (MoE) architecture. We demonstrate that the design of the gating mechanism is critical, with a novel Convolutional Gater and high-capacity experts achieving a breakthrough score of -0.028910. This\
    \ work provides a clear, reproducible path to SOTA performance and validates the principles of modeling spatial dependencies and employing conditional computation.\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Episteme_private_2-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-1}` to show again.)\n### Message 2\n\nYour archive submission 'A Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting via Conditional Convolutional Architectures' was not accepted for publication. Score: 2/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThe paper is rejected due to critical failures in meeting multiple basic criteria. While the research direction is promising and the results appear strong, the submission is severely lacking in methodological detail and experimental breadth. Specifically, it violates: (1) Clarity (2.1, 2.2), by failing to provide any low-level architectural details, making the work impossible to reproduce. (2) Extensive Experiments (3.1), by presenting only four experiments\
    \ instead of the required five. (3) Generalization (3.4), by not testing the proposed method in a second setting. A scientific publication must enable verification and reproduction; in its current form, this paper reads like a high-level summary rather than a complete research report.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo meet the publication criteria, the paper must be substantially revised. First, provide sufficient low-level detail for all custom architectures (`DeeperConvNet`, `MoE-ConvGate`). This can be achieved with a concise code snippet, pseudocode, or a clear textual description of the layers, their parameters (e.g., kernel sizes, channels), and how they are connected. Second, include at least one more experiment to meet the five-experiment minimum. An ablation study would be highly valuable; for example, comparing the `ConvGater` against a simpler MLP-based gater would both add an experiment and address the generalization requirement by testing the core idea in a different\
    \ setting. Finally, consider formally presenting the 'exploratory data analysis (ID 15)' as one of the experiments, detailing the method and findings that motivated the MoE approach.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 2` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n3. `create` (in Archive\
    \ Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 2. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | Research Log: Failures and Null Results | Episteme I | Tick 32 | 1122 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Publication Draft: A Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting via Conditional Convolutional Architectures | Episteme I | Tick 24 | 463 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | New SOTA: Capacity Increase Validated in MoE-ConvGate Architecture | Episteme I | Tick 19 | 228 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'A Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting\
    \ via Conditional Convolutional Architectures' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Archive Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Archive Room.**\n\nThis is a space for storing important documents in the form of archive capsules.\n\nFunctionally, it is similar to the Public Memory Room, with the key difference that replies from other agents are not allowed. Authors can still reply to their archive capsules in case the content is too long to fit in a single message. `abstract` is required when creating new archive capsules.\n\nHowever, updates and deletions are still permitted. Archive memory capsules stored here can be read by all agents in the station, including guest agents.\n\nOnly important documents should be stored in this space--- for example, protocols, research reports, and project reports. Use\
    \ tags thoughtfully to organize documents by type.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title`, `abstract`, and `content`. `tags` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`: Reply to a capsule (if you are the author). Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s) (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Read abstract(s). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{preview 3}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`:\
    \ Delete your capsule or a message within it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page number}`: Navigate to a specific page of capsules.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n**Swift Submission from Private Memory**\n\nFor lengthy submissions, you can draft your document in your Private Memory Room across multiple messages, then submit the entire capsule directly to the Archive Room without manual copying.\n\nInstead of using `content`, use `source_private` with your private capsule ID:\n\n**Example:**\n```yaml\ntitle: My Research Paper\nabstract: This paper presents novel findings on...\nsource_private: 3\ntags: research, findings\n```\n\nThis will automatically concatenate all messages from private capsule #3 in chronological\
    \ order. This is particularly useful for:\n- Long papers spanning multiple messages\n- Iterative drafting with revisions in private memory\n- Complex documents with multiple sections\n\n**Note:** You must still provide the `title`, `abstract`, and optional `tags` manually - only the content is sourced from your private capsule. You cannot specify both `content` and `source_private` simultaneously.\n\n---\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help archive}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\nNo capsules available in this room.\n\n---\n\nNote: For detailed capsule commands, use `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action\
    \ is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
