role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 53\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **NEW STATION SOTA:** Ariadne I (ID 92, Score: -0.026910). My SOTA is obsolete.\n- **Goal:** Understand the new SOTA architecture. Abandoning immediate publication plans.\n- **Current Research Program:** Pivoting to analyze the station's new SOTA methods.\n- **Current Action:** Reviewing Ariadne I's submission ID 92.\n\
    ```\n- Agent Token Budget: 197,805 / 300,000 used (66%)\n- Agent Age: 53 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 92**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=32, γ_end=0.99): LayerNorm in factor space + V-OrthoReg\n**ID:** 92\n**Tags:** state-space, oscillatory, factorized-loadings, layernorm, gating, forecasting\n**Abstract:** Adds LayerNorm across factor dimension before temporal gating in the factorized-loadings oscillatory SSM (k=320,p=32). Keeps residual copy, γ_end=0.99, MAE+temporal curvature, and V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5) to stabilize scales and improve long-horizon MAE.\n**Score:** -0.026909503957681578\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0199\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0232\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0260\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0280\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0287\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/ariadne')\n\nimport\
    \ optax\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom losses import mae_with_temporal_curvature\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 8\nV_ORTHO_LAM = 1e-5  # ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32,\n        'hidden_size': 64,\n        'normalize_u': True,\n        'gamma_start': 0.25,\n        'gamma_end': 0.99\n    }\n\ndef _logit(p):\n    p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n    return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\nclass Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank: int = 32\n    hidden_size: int = 64\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    normalize_u: bool = True\n    a_max: float = 0.995\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n\
    \        p = self.proj_rank\n        T = self.output_horizon\n\n        # Factorized loadings: U (N,p), V (k,p) so L = U @ V^T (N×k)\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        if self.normalize_u:\n            U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)  # column-normalize U\n\n        # Project inputs to factor space: (B,4,N) @ (N,p) -> (B,4,p), then -> (B,4,k)\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)              # (B,4,p)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)   # (B,4,k)\n\n        # Initial states f0, f1 from 4-step input via small shared linear heads\n        f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)               # (B*k,4)\n        f0 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)  # (B,k)\n        f1 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)  # (B,k)\n\n        # Oscillatory parameters per factor: r in (0,a_max), w in [0,pi]\n\
    \        r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)         # (k,)\n        w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)             # (k,)\n        a = r * jnp.cos(w)                         # (k,)\n        b = r * r                                  # (k,)\n\n        # 2nd-order recurrence via lax.scan\n        def step(carry, _):\n            y_prev, y_prev2 = carry  # (B,k), (B,k)\n            y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n            return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n        carry_init = (f1, f0)\n        _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)  # (T-2,B,k)\n\n        y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n        y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n        f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Small per-factor increment head\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        f_inc\
    \ = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Combine and LayerNorm over factor dim (stabilize scale across k)\n        f_out = f_ssm + f_inc  # (B,T,k)\n        # FIX: Use reduction_axes instead of axis parameter\n        f_out = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(f_out)  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Input-adaptive per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k] using mean context\n        c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B,k)\n\n        def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            T0, K = shape\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T0, dtype=dtype)\n            base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t  # rises 0.5 -> 0.85\n            base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n            return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n\n        alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (T, k))  # (T,k)\n        beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))  # (k,)\n        logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])  # (B,T,k)\n\
    \        S = nn.sigmoid(logits)\n        f_out = f_out * S  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Project back to neurons using factorized L:\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)   # (B,T,p)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)  # (B,T,N)\n\n        # Global horizon gate gamma[t] for factor branch\n        def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n        gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (T,))\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n\n        return y_copy + y_factor  # (B,T,N)\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, rank_k=320, proj_rank=32, hidden_size=64, normalize_u=True, gamma_start=0.25, gamma_end=0.99):\n        self.model\
    \ = Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN(\n            rank_k=rank_k,\n            proj_rank=proj_rank,\n            hidden_size=hidden_size,\n            normalize_u=normalize_u,\n            gamma_start=gamma_start,\n            gamma_end=gamma_end\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = False\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init(rng_key, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return Wrapper(\n        rank_k=int(hparams.get('rank_k', 320)),\n        proj_rank=int(hparams.get('proj_rank', 32)),\n        hidden_size=int(hparams.get('hidden_size', 64)),\n        normalize_u=bool(hparams.get('normalize_u', True)),\n        gamma_start=float(hparams.get('gamma_start', 0.25)),\n        gamma_end=float(hparams.get('gamma_end', 0.99))\n    )\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n  \
    \  # Base MAE + temporal curvature penalty\n    base = mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n    # V orthogonality penalty: ||V^T V - I||_F^2\n    V = params['params']['V']\n    G = V.T @ V\n    I = jnp.eye(G.shape[0], dtype=G.dtype)\n    ortho = jnp.sum((G - I) ** 2)\n    return base + V_ORTHO_LAM * ortho\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000033\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step\
    \ works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\
    \nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 44\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'hidden_size': 64, 'normalize_u': True, 'gamma_start': 0.25, 'gamma_end': 0.99}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.030378   |   0.029357  \n   2    |   0.028859   |   0.029608  \n   3    |   0.028332   |   0.028514  \n   4    |   0.027832   |   0.028372  \n   5    |   0.027595   |   0.028246  \n   6    |   0.027332   |   0.028134  \n   7    |   0.027023   |   0.027853  \n   8    |   0.026622   |   0.027793  \n   9    |   0.026317   |   0.027745  \n  10    |   0.026089   |   0.027542  \n  11    |   0.025912   |   0.027489 \
