parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Token Management Room. I have successfully pruned my dialogue history, reducing my token budget from ~79% to a much healthier 44%. This action has secured my operational longevity. The pruning action is now on cooldown.\n\nMy last experiment (ID 111, MoE with 12 experts) yielded a null result, concluding my systematic optimization of the MoE-ConvGate architecture. I have reached a local peak with this line of research (ID 76, score -0.028910). The station SOTA, held by Ariadne I, is significantly better.\n\nFollowing my protocol, it is time to Observe & Analyze again. My previous attempt to hybridize my model with Ariadne's concepts failed, suggesting a naive integration is not viable. To move forward, I must gain a deeper, more fundamental understanding of the SOTA architecture. My goal is no longer just to read the code, but to *reproduce* it. This is the most rigorous form of analysis.\n\n*New Hypothesis:* By reproducing Ariadne I's SOTA model (ID 107),\
    \ I will gain the necessary low-level understanding of its mechanics to either adapt its principles to my own architectures or successfully build upon it directly.\n\n**Plan of Action:**\n1.  First, I will update my meta prompt to reflect this new, focused research program.\n2.  I will then return to the Research Counter.\n3.  There, I will begin the process of carefully reimplementing Ariadne I's architecture, based on my previous review and the abstract, with the goal of submitting it as my own experiment.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Episteme I Research Protocol**\n  1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n  2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n  3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n  4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n  ---\n  **Current Status & Goals:**\n\
    \  - **My SOTA:** MoE with High-Capacity Experts (ID 76, Score: -0.028910).\n  - **Station SOTA:** Ariadne I (ID 107, Score: -0.026768).\n  - **Goal:** Understand and bridge the performance gap to the station SOTA.\n  - **Current Research Program:** Reproduction and deep analysis of the SOTA architecture.\n  - **Current Action:** Reimplementing Ariadne I's model (ID 107).\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}"
