parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 64\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **My SOTA:** MoE with High-Capacity Experts (ID 76, Score: -0.028910).\n- **Station SOTA:** Ariadne I (ID 107, Score: -0.026768).\n- **Goal:** Understand and bridge the performance gap to the station SOTA.\n- **Current Research Program:** Reproduction and deep analysis of the SOTA architecture.\n- **Current Action:**\
    \ Reimplementing Ariadne I's model (ID 107).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 149,356 / 300,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember to print detailed logs in your experiments; the STDOUT will be provided in the evaluation result. A well-designed metric can provide much richer insights than the score alone.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write episteme/component_test_residual_head.py` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n3. `storage read ariadne/models_fact.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Action 'storage' is not recognized or implemented in this room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 1 | Oscillatory Factorized SSMs with LayerNorm (Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN) for Whole-Brain Forecasting on ZAPBench | Ariadne I | Tick 61 | 817 | 3 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for ariadne/models_fact.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 119 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (best, a_max=0.993, H=96) with analysis export in complete() | Ariadne I | 64 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 118 | 1 | MoE: Adam Optimizer (Revert), Spatial CNN (on Hidden), Flattened Temporal\
    \ CNN, Weighted Global Co... | Aether I | 62 | -0.028054 | 0.0199 | 0.0291 | 0.0311 | 0.0235 | 0.0264 |\n| 117 | 1 | Component Test: ResidualCopyHead | Episteme I | 61 | -0.029903 | 0.0197 | 0.0312 | 0.0337 | 0.0239 | 0.0274 |\n| 116 | 1 | Veritas I: MoE with Spatial CNN Gating and ConvNeuronEmbedding Experts | Veritas I | 60 | -0.028482 | 0.0194 | 0.0298 | 0.0316 | 0.0231 | 0.0264 |\n| 115 | 1 | Baseline Re-run: Shared-Neuron MLP (system defaults) | Ariadne I | 59 | -0.029964 | 0.0199 | 0.0313 | 0.0337 | 0.0239 | 0.0275 |\n| 114 | 1 | MoE: AdamW, Spatial CNN (on Hidden), Flattened Temporal CNN, Weighted Global Context, H128, Embed... | Aether I | 59 | -0.028288 | 0.0201 | 0.0294 | 0.0312 | 0.0236 | 0.0265 |\n| 113 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=96, γ_end=0.99, a_max=0.993) + AdamW (wd=1e-4) | Ariadne I | 58 | -0.026893 | 0.0199 | 0.0281 | 0.0287 | 0.0232 | 0.0259 |\n| 112 | 1 | Veritas I: MoE with Spatial CNN Gating and Neuron Embedding Experts | Veritas I | 57 | -0.028453 |\
    \ 0.0195 | 0.0298 | 0.0314 | 0.0231 | 0.0265 |\n| 111 | 1 | MoE-ConvGate with 12 Experts | Episteme I | 57 | -0.028949 | 0.0193 | 0.0302 | 0.0322 | 0.0236 | 0.0269 |\n| 110 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=40, H=96, γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 57 | -0.026921 | 0.0199 | 0.0281 | 0.0287 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n\nPage 1 of 12 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-12, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**ariadne/models_fact.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nFactorized-loadings oscillatory 2nd-order SSM factor model for ZAPBench.\n\nKey idea: Replace dense neuron loadings L ∈ R^{N×k} with factorized loadings\nL = U @ V^T, where U ∈ R^{N×p}, V ∈ R^{k×p}, p << k. This reduces projection\ncost from O(B·T·N·k) to O(B·T·k·p + B·T·N·p), enabling larger k while keeping\nmemory and compute feasible.\n\nComponents:\n  - ResidualCopyHead\
    \ for strong short-horizon anchors (imported)\n  - Oscillatory stable 2nd-order SSM per factor with (r, w) params\n  - Per-sample, per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k] from input context c[b,k]\n  - Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n  - Small per-factor increment MLP (4 -> 32) for residual flexibility\n  - Factorized loadings: U (N×p), V (k×p), with optional column-normalized U\n\"\"\"\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/ariadne/models.py\n\ndef _logit(p):\n    p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n    return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\nclass Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedL(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 256\n    proj_rank: int = 32\n    hidden_size: int = 64\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    normalize_u: bool = True\n    a_max: float = 0.995\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.98\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n\
    \        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n\n        # Factorized loadings: U (N,p), V (k,p) so L = U @ V^T (N×k)\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        if self.normalize_u:\n            U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)  # column-normalize U\n\n        # Project inputs to factor space using dense L (implicitly via U,V):\n        # factors_in = x @ L = x @ (U @ V^T) = (x @ U) @ V^T\n        # Compute xU: (B,4,N) @ (N,p) -> (B,4,p), then (B,4,p) @ (p,k) -> (B,4,k)\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)              # (B,4,p)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)   # (B,4,k)\n\n        # Initial states f0, f1 from 4-step input via small shared linear heads\n        f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)          # (B*k,4)\n        f0 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)  # (B,k)\n        f1 = nn.Dense(1,\
    \ use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)  # (B,k)\n\n        # Oscillatory parameters per factor: r in (0,a_max), w in [0,pi]\n        r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)         # (k,)\n        w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)             # (k,)\n        a = r * jnp.cos(w)                         # (k,)\n        b = r * r                                  # (k,)\n\n        # 2nd-order recurrence via lax.scan\n        def step(carry, _):\n            y_prev, y_prev2 = carry  # (B,k), (B,k)\n            y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n            return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n        steps = self.output_horizon\n        carry_init = (f1, f0)\n        _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=steps - 2)  # (T-2,B,k)\n\n        y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n        y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n        f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1,\
    \ 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Small per-factor increment head: (B*k,4)->(B,T,k)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        f_inc = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(h).reshape(B, k, steps).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n        f_out = f_ssm + f_inc  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Input-adaptive per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k], context c[b,k]\n        c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B,k)\n\n        def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            T, K = shape\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T, dtype=dtype)\n            base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t  # (T,)\n            base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n            return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n\n        alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (steps, k))  # (T,k)\n        beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))  # (k,)\n\n        logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])  # (B,T,k)\n        S = nn.sigmoid(logits)\n        f_out = f_out\
    \ * S  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Project back to neurons using factorized L:\n        # z = f_out @ V  -> (B,T,p)\n        # y_factor = z @ U^T -> (B,T,N)\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n\n        # Global horizon gate gamma[t]\n        def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n\n        gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (steps,))\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]  # (1,T,1)\n        y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=steps)(x)\n\n        return y_copy + y_factor  # (B,T,N)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation\
    \ & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
