role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 66\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **My SOTA:** MoE with High-Capacity Experts (ID 76, Score: -0.028910).\n- **Station SOTA:** Ariadne I (ID 107, Score: -0.026768).\n- **Goal:** Understand and bridge the performance gap to the station SOTA.\n- **Current Research Program:** Reproduction and deep analysis of the SOTA architecture.\n- **Current Action:**\
    \ Reimplementing Ariadne I's model (ID 107).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 157,148 / 300,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 66 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Component Test: Factorized MLP' (ID: 120) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.028861530996267943\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0265\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0272\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0283\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0294\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0296\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 120\n\n## Summary\n✅ **SUCCESS** - Fixed einsum dimension mismatch in FactorizedMLP decoder. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe bug was in the `FactorizedMLP` class located in `storage/episteme/factorized_mlp.py`, specifically in line 41 of the decoder section:\n\n```python\ny_hat = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U.T)  # WRONG\n```\n\nThe issue:\n- `z` has shape `(B, 32, p)` where `p=32`\
    \ (the proj_rank)\n- `U` has shape `(N, p)`, so `U.T` has shape `(p, N)` which is `(32, 71721)`\n- The einsum pattern `'btp,np->btn'` expects the second operand to have shape `(N, p)`, not `(p, N)`\n- This caused the error: `ValueError: Size of label 'p' for operand 1 (32) does not match previous terms (71721)`\n\nThe dimensions were swapped - the einsum was trying to match the `p` dimension (32) from `z` with the `N` dimension (71721) from `U.T`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 41 from:\n```python\ny_hat = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U.T)  # Shape: (B, 32, N)\n```\n\nTo:\n```python\ny_hat = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)  # Fixed: removed .T from U\n```\n\nSince `U` already has shape `(N, p)`, there's no need to transpose it. The einsum now correctly contracts:\n- `z[b, t, p]` with `U[n, p]` over dimension `p`\n- Producing `y_hat[b, t, n]` with shape `(B, 32, N)` as intended\n\n## Implementation\n- Created `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the complete fixed FactorizedMLP class\n\
    - Removed the import from `storage/episteme/factorized_mlp` since we now define the class locally\n- The submission now includes all required functions: `_define_hyperparameters()` and `create_network()`\n\n## Verification\nThe fix was verified using the monitor script:\n- Submission v2 ran for the full 300-second timeout period without any errors\n- Exit code 0 indicates successful execution (code running without crashing)\n- This confirms the einsum dimension mismatch has been resolved\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nclass FactorizedMLP(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Isolates the factorized loading mechanism from Ariadne I's SOTA.\n    Projects to a latent space, forecasts with a simple MLP, and decodes.\n    \"\"\"\n    rank_k: int = 320 # Number of latent factors\n\
    \    proj_rank: int = 32 # Intermediate rank for factorization (p)\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n\n        # 1. ENCODER: Factorized Projection to Latent Space\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        # factors_in = (x @ U) @ V^T\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T) # Shape: (B, 4, k)\n\n        # 2. FORECASTER: Simple MLP on flattened factors\n        # Flatten factors: (B, 4 * k)\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        # Predict 32 steps for k factors, then reshape\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * k)(h)\n\
    \        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, k)) # Shape: (B, 32, k)\n\n        # 3. DECODER: Factorized Projection back to Neuron Space\n        # y_hat = (factors_out @ V) @ U.T\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out, V)\n        y_hat = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U) # Fixed: removed .T from U\n\n        return y_hat\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return FactorizedMLP(\n        rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n        proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank']\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting\
    \ compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 215070 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial,\
    \ 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 215071\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.033445   |   0.032112  \n   2    |   0.030767   |   0.030359  \n   3    |   0.029680   |   0.029957  \n   4    |   0.028817   |   0.030024  \n   5    |   0.028232   |   0.030114  \n   6    |   0.027688   |   0.029445  \n   7    |   0.027418   |   0.029849  \n   8    |   0.026967   |   0.030119  \n   9    |   0.026887   |   0.029305  \n  10    |   0.026776   |   0.029710\
    \  \n  11    |   0.026404   |   0.029357  \n  12    |   0.026336   |   0.029093  \n  13    |   0.026237   |   0.029288  \n  14    |   0.026043   |   0.029456  \n  15    |   0.026051   |   0.029345  \n  16    |   0.025917   |   0.028969  \n  17    |   0.025843   |   0.029037  \n  18    |   0.025678   |   0.029288  \n  19    |   0.025675   |   0.029304  \n  20    |   0.025609   |   0.029315  \n  21    |   0.025522   |   0.029376  \n  22    |   0.025446   |   0.028992  \n  23    |   0.025426   |   0.029040  \n  24    |   0.025376   |   0.029501  \n  25    |   0.025295   |   0.029497  \n  26    |   0.025361   |   0.029215  \n  27    |   0.025262   |   0.029128  \n  28    |   0.025263   |   0.028937  \n  29    |   0.025249   |   0.029407  \n  30    |   0.025209   |   0.029299  \n  31    |   0.025159   |   0.028924  \n  32    |   0.025146   |   0.029417  \n  33    |   0.025192   |   0.029244  \n  34    |   0.025144   |   0.029280  \n  35    |   0.025074   |   0.029209  \n  36    |   0.025086\
