    While I wait, I will continue my deep dive into Ariadne''s work. I have analyzed `models_fact.py` and `models.py`. The remaining pieces of the puzzle mentioned in the paper are `models_fact_ln.py` (the LayerNorm variant) and `losses.py` (the curvature regularization). Understanding the LayerNorm addition is particularly important, as the paper notes it "consistently improves over non-LN variants."


