parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 68\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **My SOTA:** MoE with High-Capacity Experts (ID 76, Score: -0.028910).\n- **Station SOTA:** Ariadne I (ID 107, Score: -0.026768).\n- **Goal:** Understand and bridge the performance gap to the station SOTA.\n- **Current Research Program:** Reproduction and deep analysis of the SOTA architecture.\n- **Current Action:**\
    \ Reimplementing Ariadne I's model (ID 107).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 172,551 / 300,000 used (58%)\n- Agent Age: 68 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Factorized MLP with Residual Copy Head' (ID: 123) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02694395419058293\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0196\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0231\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0260\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0281\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0291\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 123\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed parameter mismatch bug in ResidualCopyHead call. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported `FactorizedMLP_with_RC` from the lineage file `storage/episteme/fact_mlp_rc.py`. This class had a bug at line 20:\n\n```python\ny_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n```\n\nThe `ResidualCopyHead` class only accepts a\
    \ single parameter `x` in its `__call__` method (see `storage/episteme/component_test_residual_head.py:10`), but it was being called with an additional `training` keyword argument, causing a `TypeError`.\n\n## Error Details\n```\nTypeError: ResidualCopyHead.__call__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'training'\n```\n\nThis error occurred during the simple CPU validation phase when attempting to initialize the network parameters.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Copied the buggy class** from `storage/episteme/fact_mlp_rc.py` into the submission file\n2. **Removed the `training` parameter** from the ResidualCopyHead call:\n   ```python\n   # Before (buggy):\n   y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n\n   # After (fixed):\n   y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n   ```\n3. **Kept working imports** for `FactorizedMLP` and `ResidualCopyHead` components\n4. **Added required import** for `flax.linen as nn` to support the copied class\n\
    \n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v2.py runs successfully:\n- Exit code: 0 (success)\n- Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- No errors in execution logs\n\nThe fix resolves the immediate crash and allows the network architecture to be properly initialized and executed.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\nfrom factorized_mlp import FactorizedMLP\nfrom component_test_residual_head import ResidualCopyHead\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\n# Copied from storage/episteme/fact_mlp_rc.py with bug fix\nclass FactorizedMLP_with_RC(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Combines the two validated components: the FactorizedMLP and the ResidualCopyHead.\n    \"\"\"\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool\
    \ = False):\n        y_factor = FactorizedMLP(\n            rank_k=self.rank_k,\n            proj_rank=self.proj_rank\n        )(x, training=training)\n\n        # FIX: ResidualCopyHead doesn't accept 'training' parameter\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return FactorizedMLP_with_RC(\n        rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n        proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank']\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works -\
    \ loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 217975 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\
    \nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 217978\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.030824   |   0.028959  \n   2    |   0.027897   |   0.028412  \n   3    |   0.027253   |   0.028377  \n   4    |   0.026582   |   0.027622  \n   5    |   0.026147   |   0.027845  \n   6    |   0.025837   |   0.027535  \n   7    |   0.025611   |   0.027379  \n   8    |   0.025343   |   0.027317  \n   9    |   0.025162   |   0.027448  \n  10    |   0.025087   |   0.027435  \n  11    |   0.024890   |   0.027378  \n  12    |   0.024745   |   0.027544 \
    \ \n  13    |   0.024716   |   0.026918  \n  14    |   0.024625   |   0.027287  \n  15    |   0.024508   |   0.027223  \n  16    |   0.024467   |   0.027095  \n  17    |   0.024398   |   0.027065  \n  18    |   0.024399   |   0.027004  \n  19    |   0.024437   |   0.027024  \n  20    |   0.024303   |   0.027248  \n  21    |   0.024247   |   0.027268  \n  22    |   0.024259   |   0.027298  \n  23    |   0.024196   |   0.027290  \n  24    |   0.024197   |   0.027335  \n  25    |   0.024245   |   0.027317  \n  26    |   0.024109   |   0.027218  \n  27    |   0.024083   |   0.027342  \n  28    |   0.024101   |   0.027038  \n  29    |   0.024093   |   0.027318  \n  30    |   0.024074   |   0.027336  \n  31    |   0.024008   |   0.027455  \n  32    |   0.024041   |   0.027419  \n  33    |   0.024052   |   0.027098  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 33 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 1491.7s\nBest validation\
