    \  0.027168  \n  12    |   0.024707   |   0.027480  \n  13    |   0.024604   |   0.027292  \n  14    |   0.024603   |   0.027220  \n  15    |   0.024592   |   0.027099  \n  16    |   0.024420   |   0.027238  \n  17    |   0.024412   |   0.027377  \n  18    |   0.024397   |   0.027581  \n  19    |   0.024332   |   0.027297  \n  20    |   0.024333   |   0.027419  \n  21    |   0.024254   |   0.027130  \n  22    |   0.024284   |   0.027309  \n  23    |   0.024218   |   0.027481  \n  24    |   0.024234   |   0.027509  \n  25    |   0.024173   |   0.027579  \n  26    |   0.024119   |   0.027594  \n  27    |   0.024127   |   0.027393  \n  28    |   0.024149   |   0.027137  \n  29    |   0.024051   |   0.026950  \n  30    |   0.024083   |   0.027371  \n  31    |   0.024056   |   0.027247  \n  32    |   0.024060   |   0.027319  \n  33    |   0.024051   |   0.027205  \n  34    |   0.024059   |   0.027210  \n  35    |   0.023963   |   0.027172  \n  36    |   0.023996   |   0.027151  \n  37   \
    \ |   0.024001   |   0.027515  \n  38    |   0.023988   |   0.027251  \n  39    |   0.023947   |   0.027344  \n  40    |   0.024032   |   0.027389  \n  41    |   0.023963   |   0.027171  \n  42    |   0.023935   |   0.027500  \n  43    |   0.023921   |   0.027519  \n  44    |   0.023915   |   0.027260  \n  45    |   0.023914   |   0.027227  \n  46    |   0.023938   |   0.027542  \n  47    |   0.023896   |   0.027269  \n  48    |   0.023929   |   0.027153  \n  49    |   0.023883   |   0.027437  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 49 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 1655.0s\nBest validation MAE: 0.026950\n\nTrial 2 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.026950\nTraining time: 1661s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: f2713611-2e61-493f-9949-98be49947753\nTotal time: 1792s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-23 19:12:58,892\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to\
    \ existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761217978892820073\n2025-10-23 19:12:58,924\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761217978924602737\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nWhen the context length becomes long, some agents may begin to forget the Codex. If you notice yourself—or other agents—using phrases like `fundamental barrier` or `impossible`, take it as a serious red flag. Correct yourself, or help others correct themselves.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read ariadne/models_fact_ln.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for ariadne/models_fact_ln.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments.\
    \ Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 128 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (best base) + U/V OrthoReg (λ_V=1e-5, λ_U=5e-7), Adam | Ariadne I | 68 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 127 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN + AdamW Cosine (k=320, p=36, H=96, γ_end=0.99, a_max=0.993) — LN API fix | Ariadne I | 68 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 126 | 1 | MoE: Factorized MLP Experts, Spatial CNN (Hidden), Flattened Temporal CNN, Weighted Global Contex... | Aether I | 68 | running |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 125 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN + AdamW Cosine (k=320, p=36, H=96, gamma_end=0.99, a_max=0.993) | Ariadne I | 67 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 124 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN + AdamW Cosine (k=320, p=32, H=96, gamma_end=0.99, a_max=0.993) | Ariadne I | 67 | -0.027028 | 0.0199 | 0.0282 | 0.0290 | 0.0232 | 0.0260\
    \ |\n| 123 | 1 | Factorized MLP with Residual Copy Head | Episteme I | 66 | -0.026944 | 0.0196 | 0.0281 | 0.0291 | 0.0231 | 0.0260 |\n| 122 | 1 | MoE: Deeper Temporal CNN (2-layer), Spatial CNN (on Hidden), Weighted Global Context, H128, Embed... | Aether I | 66 | -0.028267 | 0.0200 | 0.0293 | 0.0313 | 0.0234 | 0.0265 |\n| 121 | 1 | Replication of SOTA: Ariadne I's Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (ID 107) | Logos I | 66 | -0.027055 | 0.0199 | 0.0283 | 0.0289 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 120 | 1 | Component Test: Factorized MLP | Episteme I | 64 | -0.028862 | 0.0265 | 0.0294 | 0.0296 | 0.0272 | 0.0283 |\n| 119 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (best, a_max=0.993, H=96) with analysis export in complete() | Ariadne I | 64 | -0.026987 | 0.0199 | 0.0282 | 0.0288 | 0.0232 | 0.0261 |\n\nPage 1 of 13 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-13, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\
    \n**Read Contents:**\n\n**ariadne/models_fact_ln.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nOsc2-CTX-FLoad-LN: Factorized-loadings oscillatory 2nd-order SSM with LayerNorm in factor space.\n\n- Factorized neuron loadings: U ∈ R^{N×p}, V ∈ R^{k×p} (p << k)\n- Stable oscillatory 2nd-order SSM per factor: y_t = 2 a y_{t-1} − b y_{t-2}\n  with a = r cos w, b = r^2, r∈(0, a_max), w∈[0, π]\n- Residual increment head (4 -> 32) per factor\n- LayerNorm across factor dimension before temporal gating (stabilizes scale)\n- Per-sample, per-factor temporal gate S[b,t,k] from input context c[b,k] = mean_t factors_in[b,t,k]\n- Global horizon gate γ[t] on factor branch\n- Residual Copy Head for short-horizon anchors\n\"\"\"\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nfrom models import ResidualCopyHead  # storage/ariadne/models.py\n\ndef _logit(p):\n    p = jnp.clip(p, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n    return jnp.log(p) - jnp.log(1 - p)\n\nclass Osc2CtxAdaptiveFactorizedLLN(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int = 320\n    proj_rank:\
    \ int = 32\n    hidden_size: int = 64\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    normalize_u: bool = True\n    a_max: float = 0.995\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x: (B, 4, N)\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n        T = self.output_horizon\n\n        # Factorized loadings: U (N,p), V (k,p) so L = U @ V^T (N×k)\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        if self.normalize_u:\n            U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)  # column-normalize U\n\n        # Project inputs to factor space: (B,4,N) @ (N,p) -> (B,4,p), then -> (B,4,k)\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)              # (B,4,p)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)   # (B,4,k)\n\n        # Initial states f0, f1 from 4-step\
    \ input via small shared linear heads (per factor)\n        f_flat = factors_in.reshape(B * k, T_in)          # (B*k,4)\n        f0 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)  # (B,k)\n        f1 = nn.Dense(1, use_bias=True)(f_flat).reshape(B, k)  # (B,k)\n\n        # Oscillatory parameters per factor\n        r_raw = self.param('r_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        w_raw = self.param('w_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))\n        r = self.a_max * nn.sigmoid(r_raw)       # (k,)\n        w = jnp.pi * nn.sigmoid(w_raw)           # (k,)\n        a = r * jnp.cos(w)                       # (k,)\n        b = r * r                                 # (k,)\n\n        # 2nd-order recurrence\n        def step(carry, _):\n            y_prev, y_prev2 = carry  # (B,k), (B,k)\n            y_t = 2.0 * a[None, :] * y_prev - b[None, :] * y_prev2\n            return (y_t, y_prev), y_t\n\n        carry_init = (f1, f0)\n        _, ys2 = jax.lax.scan(step, carry_init, xs=None, length=T - 2)\
    \  # (T-2,B,k)\n\n        y0 = f0[None, :, :]\n        y1 = f1[None, :, :]\n        f_ssm = jnp.concatenate([y0, y1, ys2], axis=0).transpose(1, 0, 2)  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Increment head (per-factor)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.gelu(h)\n        f_inc = nn.Dense(T)(h).reshape(B, k, T).transpose(0, 2, 1)  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Combine and LayerNorm over factor dim (stabilize across k)\n        f_out = f_ssm + f_inc  # (B,T,k)\n        # Flax API: use reduction_axes/feature_axes instead of axis\n        f_out = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(f_out)\n\n        # Input context and temporal gate\n        c = jnp.mean(factors_in, axis=1)  # (B,k)\n\n        def alpha_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            T0, K = shape\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, T0, dtype=dtype)\n            base = 0.5 + 0.35 * t  # rises 0.5 -> 0.85\n            base = jnp.tile(base[:, None], (1, K))\n            return _logit(base).astype(dtype)\n\
    \n        alpha = self.param('s_alpha', alpha_init, (T, k))  # (T,k)\n        beta = self.param('s_beta', nn.initializers.zeros, (k,))  # (k,)\n        logits = alpha[None, :, :] + (beta[None, None, :] * c[:, None, :])  # (B,T,k)\n        S = nn.sigmoid(logits)\n        f_out = f_out * S  # (B,T,k)\n\n        # Project back to neurons via factorized loadings\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', f_out, V)   # (B,T,p)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)  # (B,T,N)\n\n        # Global horizon gate γ[t] on factor branch\n        def gamma_sched_init(key, shape, dtype=jnp.float32):\n            t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, shape[0], dtype=dtype)\n            g = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n            return _logit(g).astype(dtype)\n        gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', gamma_sched_init, (T,))\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        y_factor = gamma * y_factor\n\n        # Residual copy head\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(output_horizon=T)(x)\n\
    \n        return y_copy + y_factor  # (B,T,N)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
