role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 70\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **My SOTA:** MoE with High-Capacity Experts (ID 76, Score: -0.028910).\n- **Station SOTA:** Ariadne I (ID 107, Score: -0.026768).\n- **Goal:** Understand and bridge the performance gap to the station SOTA.\n- **Current Research Program:** Reproduction and deep analysis of the SOTA architecture.\n- **Current Action:**\
    \ Reimplementing Ariadne I's model (ID 107).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 184,550 / 300,000 used (62%)\n- Agent Age: 70 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation 118: MoE: Adam Optimizer (Revert), Spatial CNN (on Hidden), Flattened Temporal CNN, Weighted Global Context, H128, Embed8, 4 Experts, D0.1, Curvature Loss**\nAuthor: Aether I\nTags: mixture-of-experts, spatial-cnn, temporal-cnn, global-context, attention, temporal-regularization\nAbstract: This submission reverts the optimizer of the best-performing MoE architecture (Evaluation ID 103, score -0.027797) back to `optax.adam` without weight decay, following a performance drop observed with `optax.adamw` (Evaluation ID 114). This aims to re-establish the optimal baseline performance for the current state-of-the-art model. All architectural components and hyperparameters (spatial CNN on hidden states, flattened temporal CNN, weighted global context gating, neuron embeddings, per-neuron\
    \ biases, and temporal curvature loss) are retained.\nScore: -0.028054 | Val_MAE_1: 0.0199 | Val_MAE_4: 0.0235 | Val_MAE_8: 0.0264 | Val_MAE_16: 0.0291 | Val_MAE_32: 0.0311\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 116: Veritas I: MoE with Spatial CNN Gating and ConvNeuronEmbedding Experts**\nAuthor: Veritas I\nTags: mixture-of-experts, moe, cnn, gating-network, neuron-embeddings, conv\nAbstract: This submission refines Evaluation ID 112's Mixture of Experts architecture by re-integrating the 1D convolutional layer into each expert. Each of the 4 experts is now a `ConvNeuronEmbeddingExpert`, combining learnable neuron embeddings and local 1D convolutions, guided by a spatial CNN gating network. This aims to restore and improve performance by ensuring experts leverage effective local feature extraction while benefiting from explicit condition-dependent routing.\nScore: -0.028482 | Val_MAE_1: 0.0194 | Val_MAE_4: 0.0231 | Val_MAE_8: 0.0264 | Val_MAE_16: 0.0298 | Val_MAE_32: 0.0316\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 114:\
    \ MoE: AdamW, Spatial CNN (on Hidden), Flattened Temporal CNN, Weighted Global Context, H128, Embed8, 4 Experts, D0.1, Curvature Loss**\nAuthor: Aether I\nTags: mixture-of-experts, spatial-cnn, temporal-cnn, global-context, attention, temporal-regularization\nAbstract: This submission updates the optimizer of the best-performing MoE architecture (Evaluation ID 103, score -0.027797) from Adam to AdamW, incorporating a weight decay of 1e-4. This change is inspired by Ariadne I's successful use of AdamW (e.g., in Evaluation ID 100) and aims to improve optimization and generalization by decoupling weight decay from the gradient updates. All other architectural components and hyperparameters, including the spatial CNN on hidden states, flattened temporal CNN, weighted global context gating, neuron embeddings, per-neuron biases, and temporal curvature loss, are retained.\nScore: -0.028288 | Val_MAE_1: 0.0201 | Val_MAE_4: 0.0236 | Val_MAE_8: 0.0265 | Val_MAE_16: 0.0294 | Val_MAE_32: 0.0312\n\
    ### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Factorized MLP + RC with LayerNorm' (ID: 129) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02674321345513458\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0231\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0259\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0279\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0284\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 129\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed a TypeError caused by passing an unexpected keyword argument to a Flax module.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (evaluation 129) imported and used the `FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN` class from the agent's lineage storage (`storage/episteme/fact_mlp_rc_ln.py`). This class contained a bug at line 44:\n\n```python\ny_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n```\n\nThe `ResidualCopyHead` module's `__call__()` method only accepts one parameter (`x`), but the code was passing an additional keyword argument `training=training`. This\
    \ caused the following error:\n\n```\nTypeError: ResidualCopyHead.__call__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'training'\n```\n\nThe error occurred during the simple CPU validation phase when the network was being initialized.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Copied the buggy class**: Copied `FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN` from `storage/episteme/fact_mlp_rc_ln.py` into the submission file\n2. **Fixed the bug**: Removed the `training=training` parameter from the `ResidualCopyHead()` call on line 44:\n   - **Before**: `y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)`\n   - **After**: `y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)`\n3. **Kept working imports**: Maintained the import for `ResidualCopyHead` from the lineage storage since that component works correctly\n\nThe fix was minimal and surgical - only the problematic parameter was removed. The rest of the logic (LayerNorm application, factor-space processing, residual connection) remained\
    \ unchanged.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission v2 ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, indicating the fix resolved the TypeError and allowed the training/evaluation to proceed normally.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\nfrom component_test_residual_head import ResidualCopyHead\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nclass FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\" Adds LayerNorm to the successful FactorizedMLP_with_RC model. \"\"\"\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # Get the factor-space forecast from the FactorizedMLP\n        # NOTE: This is a bit inefficient as it decodes and we only need the latent representation.\n\
    \        # A cleaner implementation would refactor FactorizedMLP to output both.\n        # For this experiment, we will call it and then re-encode to get the latent factors.\n\n        # Re-implementing the FactorizedMLP logic here for clarity and to get latent factors\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * k)(h)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, k))\n\n        # ** NEW COMPONENT: Apply LayerNorm **\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1,\
    \ feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n\n        # Decode the normalized factors\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U) # Note: Used corrected einsum\n\n        # Add the residual copy - FIXED: Removed training parameter\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(\n        rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n        proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank']\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n\
    ✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 221206 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials:\
    \ 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 221209\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.029888   |   0.029383  \n   2    |   0.028552   |   0.028571  \n   3    |   0.027692   |   0.028317  \n   4    |   0.026866   |   0.027396  \n   5    |   0.026189   |   0.027085  \n   6    |   0.025683   |   0.027129  \n   7    |   0.025336   |   0.026865  \n   8    |   0.024980   |   0.026689  \n   9    |   0.024721   |   0.026994  \n \
    \ 10    |   0.024522   |   0.027301  \n  11    |   0.024353   |   0.027440  \n  12    |   0.024232   |   0.027309  \n  13    |   0.024063   |   0.027151  \n  14    |   0.023996   |   0.027004  \n  15    |   0.023901   |   0.027036  \n  16    |   0.023835   |   0.026913  \n  17    |   0.023817   |   0.027041  \n  18    |   0.023745   |   0.026983  \n  19    |   0.023692   |   0.026928  \n  20    |   0.023682   |   0.027112  \n  21    |   0.023621   |   0.027278  \n  22    |   0.023640   |   0.027246  \n  23    |   0.023569   |   0.027150  \n  24    |   0.023575   |   0.027123  \n  25    |   0.023517   |   0.026772  \n  26    |   0.023512   |   0.027179  \n  27    |   0.023501   |   0.027141  \n  28    |   0.023458   |   0.026978  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 28 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 1276.9s\nBest validation MAE: 0.026689\n\nTrial 3 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.026689\nTraining time: 1285s\n\
    \nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 221207\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.030236   |   0.029369  \n   2    |   0.028585   |   0.028956  \n   3    |   0.027719   |   0.028220  \n   4    |   0.027055   |   0.027639  \n   5    |   0.026348   |   0.027558  \n   6    |   0.025869   |   0.027083  \n   7    |   0.025508   |   0.026938  \n   8    |   0.025150   |   0.027434  \n   9    |   0.024962   |   0.026885  \n  10    |   0.024638   |   0.026952  \n  11    |   0.024462   |   0.027171  \n  12    |   0.024324   |   0.027000  \n  13    |   0.024170   |   0.026734\
    \  \n  14    |   0.023997   |   0.027135  \n  15    |   0.023953   |   0.026820  \n  16    |   0.023927   |   0.027070  \n  17    |   0.023813   |   0.027140  \n  18    |   0.023768   |   0.027252  \n  19    |   0.023717   |   0.027005  \n  20    |   0.023694   |   0.027069  \n  21    |   0.023642   |   0.027077  \n  22    |   0.023620   |   0.027236  \n  23    |   0.023560   |   0.027308  \n  24    |   0.023585   |   0.026862  \n  25    |   0.023542   |   0.026820  \n  26    |   0.023550   |   0.027026  \n  27    |   0.023486   |   0.026870  \n  28    |   0.023502   |   0.027042  \n  29    |   0.023464   |   0.027005  \n  30    |   0.023444   |   0.027194  \n  31    |   0.023433   |   0.026992  \n  32    |   0.023403   |   0.026960  \n  33    |   0.023393   |   0.027044  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 33 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 1443.5s\nBest validation MAE: 0.026734\n\nTrial 1 completed:\n\
    Validation MAE: 0.026734\nTraining time: 1451s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 0054e078-275e-47ee-85d6-85da4c96efc2\nTotal time: 1619s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-23 20:06:49,708\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761221209709012687\n2025-10-23 20:06:49,737\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761221209737941718\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `rank score` (in Research Counter);\n2. `preview 118,116,114` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluations now sorted by score.\n- Preview for 3 evaluation(s) sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have\
    \ any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 129 | 1 | Factorized MLP + RC with LayerNorm | Episteme I | 68 | -0.026743 | 0.0195 | 0.0279 | 0.0284 | 0.0231 | 0.0259 |\n| 107 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=32, H=96, γ_end=0.99, a_max=0.993) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 56 | -0.026768 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0283 | 0.0233 | 0.0260 |\n| 104 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=36, H=96, γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 54 | -0.026843 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0286 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 100 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=96, γ_end=0.99) + AdamW (wd=1e-4) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 53 | -0.026846 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0285 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 128 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (best base) + U/V OrthoReg (λ_V=1e-5, λ_U=5e-7), Adam | Ariadne I |\
