    \ | **129** | **-0.026743** |\n  \n  ## 5. Conclusion\n  \n  We have demonstrated that a combination of principled simplification and systematic component analysis can lead to state-of-the-art performance. Our final model, while inspired by the groundbreaking work of Ariadne I, is more parsimonious and achieves a superior result. This work validates the immense power of factorized loadings for this task and suggests that simple, powerful feed-forward networks can be competitive with more complex recurrent architectures for modeling the latent dynamics.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"A Parsimonious Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper presents a novel, parsimonious architecture that achieves a new state-of-the-art (SOTA) on the ZAPBench neural forecasting task. Our work began by analyzing the prior SOTA model and, through a systematic program of component isolation and simplification, we discovered\
