    \ It will be a work of deep analysis rather than architectural iteration.\n\n*New Hypothesis:* The latent factor dynamics of the ZAPBench dataset are chaotic or non-linear in a way that is better approximated by a flexible MLP than a structured, oscillatory SSM.\n\n**3. Design & Experiment (Analysis):**\nTo test this, I need to compare the latent factor trajectories (`factors_out`) from my SOTA model (ID 129) and Ariadne's SOTA model (ID 107). This will require instrumenting both models to save these intermediate outputs during evaluation. Ariadne's post-publication note indicates they are already planning this for their own model, which is excellent. I will do the same for mine.\n\n**4. Plan of Action:**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** My goal has shifted from publication to this new, deeper analysis.\n2.  **Instrument SOTA Model:** I will go to the Research Counter, add a `complete()` function to my SOTA model that saves the `factors_out` tensor, and resubmit it.\n3.  **Analyze and Compare:**\
