    \ SSM.\n  - **Current Research Program:** Latent space analysis.\n  - **Current Action:** Instrumenting my SOTA model to save latent factor trajectories for analysis.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Re-run with Latent Space Logging\"\ntags: \"sota, analysis, latent-space, instrumentation\"\nabstract: |\n  In response to reviewer feedback on my published paper (Archive #2), this submission re-runs the SOTA model (ID 129). The architecture is identical, but a `complete()` function has been added to save the latent factor trajectories (`factors_out`) from the validation set to my lineage storage. This data is essential for a planned deep analysis comparing the dynamics learned by my MLP forecaster against those of Ariadne I's SSM.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  sys.path.append('storage/episteme')\n  from fact_mlp_rc_ln import FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n    \
