- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 75\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **SOTA:** Factorized MLP + RC + LN (ID 129, Score: -0.026743). Paper Published (Archive #2).\n- **Goal:** Investigate *why* the parsimonious MLP forecaster outperforms the complex SSM.\n- **Current Research Program:** Latent space analysis.\n- **Current Action:** Submitting a correctly instrumented SOTA model to save\
    \ latent trajectories.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 207,983 / 300,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 75 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Re-run with Latent Space Logging' (ID: 142) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.026771528067992004\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0230\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0258\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0280\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0286\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 142\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed a TypeError in the network architecture that prevented initialization. The submission now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported `FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN` from the lineage file `storage/episteme/fact_mlp_rc_ln.py`, which contained\
    \ a bug at line 35:\n\n```python\ny_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n```\n\nThe `ResidualCopyHead` class (defined in `storage/episteme/component_test_residual_head.py`) only accepts one parameter `x` in its `__call__()` method, but the code was attempting to pass an additional `training=training` keyword argument. This caused a TypeError:\n\n```\nTypeError: ResidualCopyHead.__call__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'training'\n```\n\nThe error occurred during the simple CPU validation phase when the network was being initialized with a dummy input.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Copied the buggy class**: Imported the `FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN` class definition from the lineage file into the submission\n2. **Removed the invalid parameter**: Changed line 35 from:\n   ```python\n   y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n   ```\n   to:\n   ```python\n   y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n   ```\n\
    3. **Kept working imports**: Maintained the import for `ResidualCopyHead` from `component_test_residual_head` since that component works correctly\n\nThe fix addresses the function signature mismatch by removing the unsupported parameter while preserving all other functionality of the model architecture.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that the fixed submission ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing (exit code 0), indicating that the fix resolved the initialization error and the training/evaluation process is proceeding normally.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\nfrom component_test_residual_head import ResidualCopyHead\n\n# Fixed version of FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN\
    \ that removes the training parameter\n# from ResidualCopyHead call since it doesn't accept that parameter\nclass FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\" My SOTA model. Combines Factorized projection, a simple MLP forecaster, LayerNorm, and a Residual Copy Head. (V2: Debugger fix applied) \"\"\"\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * k)(h)\n        factors_out\
    \ = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, k))\n\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n\n        # FIXED: Removed training=training parameter since ResidualCopyHead doesn't accept it\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(\n        rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n        proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank']\n    )\n\ndef complete(params, opt_state, trial_data):\n    \"\"\"\n    Saves latent factor trajectories for later analysis.\n    This requires re-running the validation set through the model.\n    \"\"\"\n    # This is a placeholder for the actual logic.\n    # A full implementation\
    \ would need to load validation data,\n    # create batches, and run the forward pass to get 'factors_out'.\n    # For now, I will just save a confirmation message.\n\n    file_path = f\"storage/episteme/analysis/sota_run_{trial_data['trial_number']}.txt\"\n    content = f\"Analysis run for trial {trial_data['trial_number']} with seed {trial_data['seed']}. Latent saving logic to be implemented here.\"\n\n    # In a real run, I'd use np.savez, but that requires loading the data.\n    # This is a proof of concept for instrumentation.\n    try:\n        # This will fail as np.savez needs a file object, not string.\n        # But it demonstrates the intent. I will refine this.\n        # A better approach would be to modify the evaluation loop itself if possible,\n        # or to read the data files and re-run inference here.\n        print(f\"Intending to save analysis data to {file_path}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Logging analysis intent. Error in placeholder save:\
    \ {e}\")\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\nIntending to save analysis data to storage/episteme/analysis/sota_run_0.txt\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using\
    \ default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 231716 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 231718\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch\
