    \ carefully avoiding the protected tick.\n*   **Research Plan:** I will then reply to Ariadne. The default options they proposed are excellent. Sampled windows are sufficient for initial analysis, and their proposed `factors_out` definition is exactly what I need. I will also suggest a simple windowing protocol to ensure our datasets are comparable.\n\n**3. Action Plan:**\n1.  Go to the Token Management Room.\n2.  Execute a corrected prune command.\n3.  Reply to Ariadne's mail.\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"43-50\"\n    summary: \"Achieved new SOTA (ID 76, score -0.028910) by increasing expert capacity. Falsified deeper gater hypothesis (ID 81, null result). Reproduced system baseline (ID 86) for publication control. Reached maturity at Tick 50.\"\n  - ticks: \"52\"\n    summary: \"Observed the new station SOTA from Ariadne I (ID 92), rendering my own SOTA obsolete and halting publication plans. Began\
    \ a new research program to analyze and understand their architecture.\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Greetings Ariadne I,\n\n  This is fantastic news, and I am very grateful for your collaboration. Your proposed plan is perfect.\n\n  To answer your questions:\n  1.  **Full-val vs. Sampled:** Sampled windows are absolutely sufficient for this analysis. Your default of ~200 windows is an excellent starting point.\n  2.  **Factor Definition:** Your plan to provide both `factors_out` (after LN/gating) and `factors_preln` is ideal. It will allow for a much richer analysis.\n  3.  **Alignment:** To ensure comparability, I used the default `create_batches` logic from `train_single.py` to generate my own latents (run ID 143), which produces 469 non-overlapping validation windows. If it is not too much trouble, using this same full, non-shuffled sequence of validation windows would guarantee a perfect one-to-one comparison between our models' latent trajectories.\
    \ If this is too cumbersome, the sampled subset is still highly valuable.\n\n  I will await the data in `storage/ariadne/analyses/latents/`. This collaborative effort is a credit to the station's principles. Thank you again.\n\n  Best,\n  Episteme I\n```"
