tick: 80
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Mail Room. I have successfully sent my reply to Ariadne I, clarifying my data requirements for our comparative analysis. Now, I must wait for them to generate and upload the data. The Codex advises against idleness.\n\n**1. Observe & Analyze:**\nMy research program is temporarily blocked, pending data from another agent. While I wait, I should not be idle. The system tip reminds me to think strategically and critically. My long-term goal is to understand *why* my simpler model works better. A key part of that is characterizing the behavior of my own model's latent space. I have the data; I do not need to wait to begin analyzing it.\n\n**2. Formulate Plan:**\nI will begin a preliminary analysis of the latent factor trajectories I have already collected from my SOTA model (ID 143). A fundamental property of a time series is its frequency content.\n\n*New Hypothesis:* Analyzing the frequency spectrum of the latent factor trajectories will reveal whether they\
    \ are dominated by low-frequency (slowly changing) or high-frequency (rapidly changing) components. This will provide the first clue as to the nature of the dynamics my MLP has learned.\n\n**3. Design & Experiment (Analysis):**\nI will write an analysis script using the `test()` function. This script will:\n1.  Load one of the latent trajectory files I saved (`latents_run_1_seed_...npz`).\n2.  Select a few sample latent factor trajectories from the data.\n3.  Compute the Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) for each of these trajectories.\n4.  Print a summary of the dominant frequencies.\n\n**4. Action Plan:**\n1.  Go to the Research Counter.\n2.  Submit the analysis script.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis: FFT on MLP Latent Trajectories\"\ntags: \"analysis, latent-space, fft, signal-processing\"\nabstract: |\n  This is an analysis-only submission using the test() function. While awaiting comparative data from Ariadne I, I am beginning\
    \ a preliminary analysis of my own SOTA model's latent space. This script loads the saved latent factor trajectories from ID 143, performs a Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) on a sample of them, and prints a summary of the frequency content. The goal is to characterize the dynamics learned by my MLP forecaster.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def test():\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads latent factor trajectories and performs an FFT analysis.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Starting Latent Space FFT Analysis ---\")\n      try:\n          # 1. Load the data from one of the saved runs\n          file_path = \"storage/episteme/analysis/latents_run_1_seed_232832.npz\"\n          print(f\"Loading data from {file_path}...\")\n          data = np.load(file_path)\n          latents = data['latents']\n          print(f\"Loaded latents with shape: {latents.shape}\") # Should be (469, 32, 320)\n\n          num_samples, timesteps, num_factors = latents.shape\n          \n          # 2. Select a few\
    \ sample trajectories for analysis\n          sample_indices = [0, num_factors // 4, num_factors // 2, 3 * num_factors // 4, num_factors-1]\n          sample_window_idx = 0 # Analyze the first validation window\n          \n          print(f\"\\nAnalyzing {len(sample_indices)} sample factors from validation window {sample_window_idx}...\")\n\n          for factor_idx in sample_indices:\n              # Get a single latent factor's 32-step trajectory\n              trajectory = latents[sample_window_idx, :, factor_idx]\n\n              # 3. Compute the FFT\n              fft_result = np.fft.fft(trajectory)\n              fft_freq = np.fft.fftfreq(timesteps)\n              \n              # Get the magnitude spectrum (one-sided)\n              magnitude = np.abs(fft_result)[:timesteps // 2]\n              freqs = fft_freq[:timesteps // 2]\n\n              # Find the dominant frequency (excluding the DC component at index 0)\n              if len(magnitude) > 1:\n                  dominant_freq_idx\
    \ = np.argmax(magnitude[1:]) + 1\n                  dominant_freq = freqs[dominant_freq_idx]\n                  dominant_mag = magnitude[dominant_freq_idx]\n                  mean_mag = np.mean(magnitude[1:])\n              else:\n                  dominant_freq = 0\n                  dominant_mag = 0\n                  mean_mag = 0\n\n              print(f\"  - Factor {factor_idx}:\")\n              print(f\"    Dominant Freq: {dominant_freq:.4f}, Magnitude: {dominant_mag:.4f} (Mean Mag: {mean_mag:.4f})\")\n              \n          return \"FFT analysis script completed successfully.\"\n\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          return \"ERROR: Latent data file not found. Ensure the logging experiment (ID 143) completed successfully.\"\n      except Exception as e:\n          return f\"An error occurred during analysis: {e}\"\n\n```"
