- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Token Management Room. My token budget is now at a healthy 45%. The pruning was successful.\n\n**1. Observe & Analyze:**\n*   **Ariadne's Hybrid Results:** Ariadne has reported the results of their hybrid model experiments (ID 160, 164). As I saw briefly before my reflection, they are null results, failing to beat either of our SOTA models. This officially concludes our collaborative \"specialist-generalist\" investigation. The hypothesis was logical but incorrect. This is a valuable scientific outcome. Ariadne has also graciously provided the latent data for this failed experiment.\n\n**2. Formulate Plan:**\nMy token budget is secure. My new research program, the Modular Graph Network, is fully planned and documented. The collaborative inquiry with Ariadne has concluded. The path is now clear to begin my new work. I will execute Phase 1 of my new program.\n\n**3. Action Plan:**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** I will update my meta prompt to reflect the shift\
    \ from strategic planning to active experimentation on the new Modular Graph program.\n2.  **Go to Research Counter:** This is the necessary location for my work.\n3.  **Implement & Submit Phase 1:** I will write the code for the `ClusterMLP` model and submit it for evaluation. This experiment is the critical first validation step for my new paradigm.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Episteme I Research Protocol**\n  1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n  2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n  3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n  4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n  ---\n  **Current Status & Goals:**\n  - **SOTA:** Factorized MLP + RC + LN (ID 129, Score: -0.026743).\n  - **Goal:** Validate the new \"Modular Graph\" paradigm.\n  - **Current Research Program:**\
    \ Modular Graph Networks.\n  - **Current Action:** Implementing Phase 1: The \"Cluster MLP\" ablation study to validate the core concept of learned differentiable clustering.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write episteme/cluster_mlp_model.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import jax\n\n  class ClusterMLP(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Phase 1 of the Modular Graph program. Tests the differentiable\n      pooling/unpooling mechanism without a GNN.\n      N=num_neurons, M=num_clusters\n      \"\"\"\n      num_clusters: int = 256\n      num_neurons: int = 71721\n      mlp_hidden: int = 64\n      output_horizon: int = 32\n\n      def setup(self):\n          # Trainable clustering matrix C of shape (N, M)\n          # Initialized with stddev chosen to keep softmax from saturating early\n          self.cluster_matrix = self.param(\n              'cluster_matrix',\n              nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.02),\n\
    \              (self.num_neurons, self.num_clusters)\n          )\n          \n          # Shared MLP to forecast cluster activities\n          self.temporal_mlp = nn.Sequential([\n              nn.Dense(self.mlp_hidden),\n              nn.relu,\n              nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)\n          ])\n\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # x shape: (B, T_in, N)\n          \n          # Get the soft cluster assignment matrix\n          # Softmax over the cluster dimension\n          c_matrix = nn.softmax(self.cluster_matrix, axis=1)\n\n          # 1. Encoder (Differentiable Pooling)\n          # (B, T_in, N) @ (N, M) -> (B, T_in, M)\n          cluster_activity = jnp.einsum('btn,nm->btm', x, c_matrix)\n\n          # 2. Propagation (Simple MLP)\n          # The MLP needs a (B, M, T_in) input\n          cluster_activity_T = jnp.transpose(cluster_activity, (0, 2, 1))\n          forecasted_clusters_T = self.temporal_mlp(cluster_activity_T)\n          # Transpose\
    \ back to (B, T_out, M)\n          forecasted_clusters = jnp.transpose(forecasted_clusters_T, (0, 2, 1))\n\n          # 3. Decoder (Differentiable Unpooling)\n          # (B, T_out, M) @ (M, N) -> (B, T_out, N)\n          y_hat = jnp.einsum('btm,nm->btn', forecasted_clusters, c_matrix)\n\n          return y_hat\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Modular Graph Paradigm, Phase 1: Cluster MLP Validation\"\ntags: \"gnn, modularity, clustering, ablation-study\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment is the first step in a new research program exploring a \"Modular Graph\" paradigm. It tests the core hypothesis that a learned, differentiable clustering of neurons is a valid and effective inductive bias. This model uses a trainable matrix to pool 71k neurons into 256 clusters, forecasts the cluster dynamics with a simple shared MLP, and unpools the results. It deliberately omits any graph-based message passing to isolate the effect of the clustering mechanism itself.\ncontent: |\n\
    \  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/episteme')\n  from cluster_mlp_model import ClusterMLP\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'num_clusters': 256,\n          'mlp_hidden': 64,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ClusterMLP(\n          num_clusters=hparams['num_clusters'],\n          mlp_hidden=hparams['mlp_hidden']\n      )\n```"
