- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 89\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **SOTA:** Factorized MLP + RC + LN (ID 129, Score: -0.026743).\n- **Goal:** Validate the new \"Modular Graph\" paradigm.\n- **Current Research Program:** Modular Graph Networks.\n- **Current Action:** Implementing Phase 1: The \"Cluster MLP\" ablation study to validate the core concept of learned differentiable clustering.\n\
    ```\n- Agent Token Budget: 139,761 / 300,000 used (47%)\n- Agent Age: 89 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Preview for Capsule #1: Oscillatory Factorized SSMs with LayerNorm (Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN) for Whole-Brain Forecasting on ZAPBench**\nAuthor: Ariadne I, Created at Tick: 61\nAbstract: We present Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN: oscillatory 2nd-order state-space factors with factorized neuron loadings (U@V^T), residual copy, context temporal gating, horizon gating, curvature regularization, and LayerNorm in factor space. Factorization enables k≈320 with p≈32–36. LayerNorm stabilizes factor scales; a_max≈0.993 improves long-horizon stability. On ZAPBench, our best mean Val MAE is 0.026768 (ID 107), surpassing prior variants. We include an author-run baseline (ID 115, MAE 0.029964) and ablations over γ_end, H, p, a_max, and optimizer.\n\n---\n\n**Preview for Capsule #2: A Parsimonious Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting**\nAuthor: Episteme I, Created\
    \ at Tick: 72\nAbstract: This paper presents a novel, parsimonious architecture that achieves a new state-of-the-art (SOTA) on the ZAPBench neural forecasting task. Our work began by analyzing the prior SOTA model and, through a systematic program of component isolation and simplification, we discovered that its performance is primarily driven by Factorized Loadings and a Residual Copy Head. By combining these two mechanisms with a simple MLP-based temporal forecaster and LayerNorm, our model (ID 129) achieves a score of -0.026743, surpassing the previous SOTA. This result is significant not only for its performance but for its relative simplicity, suggesting that complex recurrent dynamics may not be necessary to achieve top-tier results.\n\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Modular Graph Paradigm, Phase 1: Cluster MLP Validation' (ID: 166) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** -0.041789005112664514\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0432\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0474\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0481\n**Val_MAE_16:**\
    \ 0.0382\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0395\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n\
    \  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 251233 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 251236\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'num_clusters': 256, 'mlp_hidden': 64}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n\
    \ Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.686949   |   0.183220  \n   2    |   0.128293   |   0.084932  \n   3    |   0.071213   |   0.056011  \n   4    |   0.054965   |   0.045361  \n   5    |   0.048600   |   0.049815  \n   6    |   0.049463   |   0.047998  \n   7    |   0.048509   |   0.049867  \n   8    |   0.047735   |   0.048490  \n   9    |   0.046049   |   0.042708  \n  10    |   0.047300   |   0.046128  \n  11    |   0.046925   |   0.045593  \n  12    |   0.045375   |   0.043349  \n  13    |   0.046500   |   0.043702  \n  14    |   0.047653   |   0.054284  \n  15    |   0.045645   |   0.044120  \n  16    |   0.047233   |   0.044007  \n  17    |   0.047121   |   0.042704  \n  18    |   0.046369   |   0.051949  \n  19    |   0.045662   |   0.051011  \n  20    |   0.046029   |   0.048041  \n  21    |   0.046470   |   0.044234  \n  22    |   0.045211   |   0.045009  \n  23    |   0.044811   |   0.045200  \n  24    |   0.045760\
