tick: 90
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Research Counter. I have just documented the failure of my Modular Graph program and updated my meta prompt to reflect my return to the factorization paradigm.\n\n**1. Observe & Analyze:**\nA significant event has occurred while I was planning. Aether I has successfully replicated my SOTA model and improved upon it by adding a \"Curvature Loss\" (ID 167), achieving a new station SOTA of **-0.026638**. My reign as SOTA holder was brief. This is a positive development; it validates the robustness of my architecture and introduces a new, proven technique—curvature loss—that I can now incorporate.\n\n**2. Formulate Plan:**\nMy plan to replace the MLP with a Transformer is still sound, but it is now a secondary objective. The immediate, most principled action is to first understand and integrate the improvement discovered by Aether I. This aligns with the scientific method: build upon the verified work of others.\n\n*New Hypothesis:* Adding a curvature loss to\
    \ my SOTA Factorized MLP model (ID 129) will replicate Aether I's SOTA-beating performance, confirming its benefit.\n\n**3. Design & Experiment:**\nI need to implement a curvature loss. A simple and standard implementation is to penalize the L2 norm of the second-order differences of the output sequence. `loss = MAE + λ * ||y_t+1 - 2*y_t + y_t-1||^2`. I will need to define a custom `compute_loss` function for this. I will start with a small, reasonable value for the regularization strength `λ`.\n\n**4. Plan of Action:**\n1.  **Implement New SOTA:** I will write a new submission script that takes my SOTA architecture (ID 129) and adds a custom `compute_loss` function implementing the curvature penalty. This is a direct test of the new technique.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication of Aether I: Factorized MLP + RC + LN with Curvature Loss\"\ntags: \"factorized-model, mlp, residual-copy, layernorm, curvature-loss, replication\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment aims\
    \ to replicate and integrate the improvement discovered by Aether I (ID 167). It takes my previous SOTA architecture (ID 129: Factorized MLP + RC + LN) and adds a curvature loss term to the MAE. The curvature loss penalizes the second-order differences of the output trajectory, promoting smoother forecasts. This serves to validate the new technique and re-establish my model as a competitive baseline.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  # Reuse my SOTA model implementation\n  sys.path.append('storage/episteme')\n  from factorized_mlp_model import FactorizedMLP_RC_LN\n\n  # New component: custom loss function\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      \"\"\"\n      Computes Mean Absolute Error plus a curvature regularization term.\n      \"\"\"\n      # 1. Standard MAE\n      mae_loss = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n\n      # 2. Curvature Loss\n      # Penalize the L2 norm of the second derivative (finite difference)\n      # y_t+1 - 2*y_t\
    \ + y_t-1\n      second_diff = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curvature_loss = jnp.mean(second_diff**2)\n      \n      # 3. Combine with a weighting factor (hyperparameter)\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      lambda_curvature = hparams.get('lambda_curvature', 1e-3) # Default if not in hparams\n\n      total_loss = mae_loss + lambda_curvature * curvature_loss\n      return total_loss\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameters. Inherits from my SOTA (ID 129) and adds the\n      new curvature penalty weight.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'k_dim': 320, # Number of factors\n          'lambda_curvature': 0.002 # A small value to start with\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the SOTA model.\"\"\"\n      return FactorizedMLP_RC_LN(\n          k_dim=hparams['k_dim']\n      )\n```"
