    \ Budget: 150,066 / 300,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 91 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Replication of Aether I: Factorized MLP + RC + LN with Curvature Loss' (ID: 171) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.026948362536239324\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0230\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0258\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0280\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0289\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 171\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed import errors and parameter mismatches. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had multiple issues:\n\n1. **Wrong module import**: Attempted to import `from factorized_mlp_model import FactorizedMLP_RC_LN`\n   - The actual file is named\
    \ `fact_mlp_rc_ln.py`\n   - The actual class is named `FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN` (not `FactorizedMLP_RC_LN`)\n\n2. **Incorrect import path**: Missing `storage.episteme.` prefix in the import statement\n\n3. **Parameter signature mismatch**: `ResidualCopyHead.__call__()` in the lineage only accepts `x` parameter, but `FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN` calls it with `training=training` parameter\n\n4. **Model initialization mismatch**: The hyperparameters used `k_dim` but the model class requires `rank_k` and `proj_rank` parameters\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Copied both model classes into the submission** to fix the parameter signature issue:\n   - Copied `ResidualCopyHead` and added `training: bool = False` parameter to its signature\n   - Copied `FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN` to work with the updated `ResidualCopyHead`\n\n2. **Fixed hyperparameters**: Updated `_define_hyperparameters()` to use:\n   - `rank_k: 320` (instead of `k_dim`)\n\
    \   - `proj_rank: 320` (added missing parameter)\n\n3. **Fixed model initialization**: Updated `create_network()` to pass both `rank_k` and `proj_rank` parameters\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the code has been running for 300+ seconds without crashing, indicating the submission is working correctly. The evaluation system is processing the code successfully.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\n# Copy the ResidualCopyHead to fix the training parameter issue\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Copies the 4 input steps to the first 4 output steps and adds a\n    learned residual for the full 32-step horizon.\n    \"\"\"\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x shape: (batch, 4, num_neurons)\n\n\
    \        # Simple MLP to learn the full 32-step residual\n        # Reshape for MLP: (batch * num_neurons, 4)\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n\n        residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n        residual = nn.relu(residual)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual) # Predicts a 32-step residual\n\n        # Reshape residual back to: (batch, 32, num_neurons)\n        residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n\n        # Create the full 32-step output scaffold\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n\n        # Copy input x to the first 4 steps of the output\n        output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n\n        # Add the learned residual to the full output\n        final_output = output + residual\n        return final_output\n\n\n# Copy the model class with fixed imports\nclass FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\" My SOTA model. Combines Factorized projection, a\
    \ simple MLP forecaster, LayerNorm, and a Residual Copy Head. (V2: Debugger fix applied) \"\"\"\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T)\n\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * k)(h)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, k))\n\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n \
    \       y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U)\n\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training) # Pass training param to my updated RC Head\n\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\n\n# New component: custom loss function\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes Mean Absolute Error plus a curvature regularization term.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 1. Standard MAE\n    mae_loss = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n\n    # 2. Curvature Loss\n    # Penalize the L2 norm of the second derivative (finite difference)\n    # y_t+1 - 2*y_t + y_t-1\n    second_diff = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curvature_loss = jnp.mean(second_diff**2)\n\n    # 3. Combine with a weighting factor (hyperparameter)\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n    lambda_curvature = hparams.get('lambda_curvature', 1e-3) # Default if not in hparams\n\n    total_loss = mae_loss + lambda_curvature * curvature_loss\n    return\
    \ total_loss\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"\n    Define hyperparameters. Inherits from my SOTA (ID 129) and adds the\n    new curvature penalty weight.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320, # Number of factors\n        'proj_rank': 320, # Projection rank\n        'lambda_curvature': 0.002 # A small value to start with\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    \"\"\"Create and return the SOTA model.\"\"\"\n    return FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(\n        rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n        proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank']\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works\
    \ - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 254484 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\
