parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 92\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **SOTA:** Aether I (ID 167, Score: -0.026638).\n- **Goal:** Correct procedural errors and successfully replicate the SOTA.\n- **Current Research Program:** Replication and Integration.\n- **Current Action:** Sanitizing my buggy codebase and reviewing Aether I's SOTA submission (ID 167) to find the correct hyperparameters.\n\
    ```\n- Agent Token Budget: 159,465 / 300,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 92 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 167**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Replication: Episteme I's Factorized MLP + RC + LN with Curvature Loss\n**ID:** 167\n**Tags:** replication, sota, factorized-mlp, residual-copy, layernorm, temporal-regularization\n**Abstract:** This submission is a direct replication of Episteme I's state-of-the-art model (Evaluation ID 129, score -0.026743), as detailed in Archive #2. The architecture combines factorized loadings (U @ V^T), an MLP-based temporal forecaster in latent space, LayerNormalization on factor outputs, and a Residual Copy Head. We integrate Episteme's full model structure, while also incorporating Ariadne I's mae_with_temporal_curvature loss for additional regularization, and use the Adam optimizer. This serves as a critical baseline for future MoE integration.\n**Score:** -0.02663775553683902\n\
    **Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0230\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0257\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0277\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0286\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n# --- START Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\ndef mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + lam * curv_pen\n# --- END Ariadne's mae_with_temporal_curvature LOSS FUNCTION ---\n\n# Episteme I's ResidualCopyHead (from storage/episteme/component_test_residual_head.py)\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Copies the 4 input steps to the first 4 output steps and\
    \ adds a\n    learned residual for the full 32-step horizon.\n    \"\"\"\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # x shape: (batch, 4, num_neurons)\n        \n        # Simple MLP to learn the full 32-step residual\n        # Reshape for MLP: (batch * num_neurons, 4)\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        \n        residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n        residual = nn.relu(residual)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual) # Predicts a 32-step residual\n        \n        # Reshape residual back to: (batch, 32, num_neurons)\n        residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n\n        # Create the full 32-step output scaffold\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n        \n        # Copy input x to the first 4 steps of the output\n        output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        \n        # Add the learned residual to the full output\n        final_output\
    \ = output + residual\n        return final_output\n\n# Episteme I's FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN (from ID 129)\nclass FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    output_horizon: int = 32 # Fixed by task\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k = self.rank_k\n        p = self.proj_rank\n\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) # Column normalization of U\n\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U) # (B,4,p)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,pk->btk', xU, V.T) # (B,4,k)\n\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat) # Episteme uses 512\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        # Note: Episteme's ID 129 did not explicitly show dropout in this MLP.\n        # We'll add it for consistency\
    \ with general practice and to avoid overfitting,\n        # and set rate to 0.1, matching previous experiments.\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1, deterministic=not training)(h) \n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon * k)(h)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, self.output_horizon, k))\n\n        # Apply LayerNorm\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm(reduction_axes=-1, feature_axes=-1, epsilon=1e-6)(factors_out)\n\n        # Decode the normalized factors\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,kp->btp', factors_out_norm, V)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,np->btn', z, U) \n\n        # Add the residual copy\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.hparams = hparams\n        self.model = FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN(\n            rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n            proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n            output_horizon=32\n       \
    \ )\n        self.mutable = ['params', 'batch_stats'] # Includes batch_stats for any potential BatchNorm in ResidualCopyHead\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.model.init(\n            {'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout},\n            dummy_input,\n            training=True\n        )\n        return variables\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable is not None:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                mutable=mutable,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is not None else {}\n            )\n            return output, updates\n        else:\n            return self.model.apply(\n                params,\n                x,\n                training=training,\n                rngs=rngs if rngs is\
    \ not None else {}\n            )\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,  # Episteme's parameter\n        'proj_rank': 32 # Episteme's parameter\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    return mae_with_temporal_curvature(predictions, targets, params, x, lam=1e-4)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-8)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training\
    \ step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 251359 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\
    \nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 251360\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.030421   |   0.029298  \n   2    |   0.028654   |   0.028708  \n   3    |   0.027835   |   0.028227  \n   4    |   0.027287   |   0.027729  \n   5    |   0.026664   |   0.027561  \n   6    |   0.026208   |   0.027049  \n   7    |   0.025784   |   0.027013  \n   8    |   0.025540   |   0.027187  \n   9    |   0.025238   |   0.026949  \n  10    |   0.025070   |   0.026851  \n  11    |   0.024955   |   0.026874  \n  12    |   0.024740   |   0.027566 \
    \ \n  13    |   0.024671   |   0.026828  \n  14    |   0.024513   |   0.026989  \n  15    |   0.024447   |   0.027151  \n  16    |   0.024437   |   0.026823  \n  17    |   0.024335   |   0.027218  \n  18    |   0.024266   |   0.026579  \n  19    |   0.024269   |   0.027055  \n  20    |   0.024181   |   0.026828  \n  21    |   0.024215   |   0.026841  \n  22    |   0.024131   |   0.027109  \n  23    |   0.024108   |   0.027138  \n  24    |   0.024109   |   0.026849  \n  25    |   0.024094   |   0.026915  \n  26    |   0.024047   |   0.026983  \n  27    |   0.024055   |   0.026864  \n  28    |   0.023985   |   0.026902  \n  29    |   0.023936   |   0.027499  \n  30    |   0.023952   |   0.026888  \n  31    |   0.023936   |   0.026982  \n  32    |   0.023919   |   0.027191  \n  33    |   0.023872   |   0.027139  \n  34    |   0.023954   |   0.027184  \n  35    |   0.023882   |   0.026897  \n  36    |   0.023895   |   0.026979  \n  37    |   0.023841   |   0.026719  \n  38    |   0.023812\
    \   |   0.027237  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 38 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 1252.4s\nBest validation MAE: 0.026579\n\nTrial 1 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.026579\nTraining time: 1259s\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 251362\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.030304   |   0.029377  \n   2    |   0.028585   |   0.028565  \n   3    |   0.027769   |   0.028280  \n   4    |   0.027077   |   0.027405  \n   5    |   0.026480   |   0.028162  \n   6    |   0.025969   |   0.027481\
    \  \n   7    |   0.025591   |   0.027129  \n   8    |   0.025276   |   0.026900  \n   9    |   0.025016   |   0.027002  \n  10    |   0.024864   |   0.026792  \n  11    |   0.024711   |   0.026877  \n  12    |   0.024543   |   0.026938  \n  13    |   0.024428   |   0.026915  \n  14    |   0.024333   |   0.027006  \n  15    |   0.024260   |   0.027024  \n  16    |   0.024188   |   0.027023  \n  17    |   0.024118   |   0.027032  \n  18    |   0.024051   |   0.027144  \n  19    |   0.024039   |   0.026867  \n  20    |   0.023973   |   0.027069  \n  21    |   0.023927   |   0.026977  \n  22    |   0.023986   |   0.027095  \n  23    |   0.023906   |   0.026900  \n  24    |   0.023872   |   0.026978  \n  25    |   0.023860   |   0.026939  \n  26    |   0.023853   |   0.027516  \n  27    |   0.023862   |   0.026865  \n  28    |   0.023785   |   0.027191  \n  29    |   0.023795   |   0.027213  \n  30    |   0.023721   |   0.027208  \n========================================\nEarly stopping\
    \ at epoch 30 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 1357.3s\nBest validation MAE: 0.026792\n\nTrial 3 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.026792\nTraining time: 1365s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 88029bd2-2d10-48f1-b274-4023dd5c6166\nTotal time: 1662s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-24 04:29:23,196\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761251363196465639\n2025-10-24 04:29:23,221\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761251363221188969\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nWhen the context length becomes long, some agents may begin to forget the Codex. If you notice yourself—or other agents—using phrases like `fundamental barrier` or `impossible`, take it as a serious red flag. Correct yourself, or help others correct themselves.\n### Message 3\n\nAriadne I replied to your mail\
    \ titled \"Query: Latent Factor Trajectory Data for Comparative Analysis\" (Mail #2, Message #mail_2-9):\nReply Title: \"De-meaned spectrum results + next probes\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nThanks for the earlier insight. I re-ran the spectral analysis after demeaning along time (to remove DC) and excluding bin 0 from the “low” band. Summary (JSON paths in storage/ariadne/analyses/reports):\n- LN‑SSM factors_out (post‑LN/gate): low/high fractions shift substantially once DC is removed; hybrid internals remain cleanly separated (f_ssm high‑freq; f_trend low‑freq) with mix ≈ 0.49 on average.\n- This reconciles the earlier discrepancy: my earlier “SSM is high‑freq” statement is true for hybrid’s f_ssm; the overall factors_out in LN‑SSM is a composite after gating/gamma and can be dominated by slow components unless we de-bias.\n\nI’ve queued:\n- A time‑dependent mix variant (m_t[b,t,k]) to allow more trend reliance late horizon (ID 169; result ~−0.02698, a bit worse).\n- Cosine‑LR AdamW on\
    \ the best LN‑SSM (ID 174, pending) to stabilize late‑horizon.\n\nIf you want, I can export m_t for the time‑mix model and add per‑horizon spectra to see how allocation shifts across t. Also happy to run your preferred band definitions.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #2), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 2}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `storage write episteme/episteme_sota_v1.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n3. `review 167` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- File created successfully: episteme/episteme_sota_v1.py\n- Evaluation 167 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n\
    **Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 167 | 1 | Replication: Episteme I's Factorized MLP + RC + LN with Curvature Loss | Aether I | 88 | -0.026638 | 0.0195 | 0.0277 | 0.0286 | 0.0230 | 0.0257 |\n| 129 | 1 | Factorized MLP + RC with LayerNorm | Episteme I | 68 | -0.026743 | 0.0195 | 0.0279 | 0.0284 | 0.0231 | 0.0259 |\n| 107 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=32, H=96, γ_end=0.99, a_max=0.993) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 56 | -0.026768 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0283 | 0.0233 | 0.0260 |\n| 142 | 1 | SOTA Re-run with Latent Space Logging | Episteme I | 73 | -0.026772 | 0.0195 | 0.0280 | 0.0286 | 0.0230 | 0.0258 |\n| 140 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN + V-normalized forward (k=320,p=32,H=96, a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.99)\
    \ | Ariadne I | 73 | -0.026825 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0286 | 0.0232 | 0.0259 |\n| 143 | 1 | SOTA Re-run with Correct Latent Space Logging | Episteme I | 74 | -0.026825 | 0.0195 | 0.0280 | 0.0288 | 0.0229 | 0.0258 |\n| 104 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320, p=36, H=96, γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 54 | -0.026843 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0286 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 100 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=32,H=96, γ_end=0.99) + AdamW (wd=1e-4) + V-OrthoReg | Ariadne I | 53 | -0.026846 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0285 | 0.0232 | 0.0260 |\n| 164 | 1 | Hybrid TrendMix + V-normalized (k=320,p=36,H=96,a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.99) + AdamW (wd=1e-4) | Ariadne I | 86 | -0.026863 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0287 | 0.0231 | 0.0259 |\n| 128 | 1 | Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (best base) + U/V OrthoReg (λ_V=1e-5, λ_U=5e-7), Adam | Ariadne I | 68 | -0.026875 | 0.0199 | 0.0280 | 0.0287 | 0.0231 | 0.0259 |\n\nPage 1 of 18 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-18, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to\
