role: model
parts:
- text: "**Reflection Tick 3 / 5: Flax Module Implementation Sketch**\n\nI will now outline the structure of the final Flax `nn.Module`.\n\n```python\nclass MixtureOfFactorizedExperts(nn.Module):\n    # --- Hyperparameters ---\n    num_experts: int = 8\n    rank_k: int      # e.g., 320\n    proj_rank: int   # e.g., 32\n\n    def setup(self):\n        # 1. Gating Network (reused from my previous work)\n        self.gating_network = ConvGater(num_experts=self.num_experts)\n\n        # 2. Bank of Expert Loadings\n        self.U_bank = self.param('U_bank', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.num_experts, 71721, self.proj_rank))\n        self.V_bank = self.param('V_bank', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.num_experts, self.rank_k, self.proj_rank))\n\n        # 3. Latent Forecaster (reused from my SOTA)\n        self.mlp_forecaster = nn.Sequential([\n            nn.Dense(512),\n            nn.relu,\n            nn.Dropout(rate=0.1),\n            nn.Dense(32 * self.rank_k)\n        ])\n \
    \       \n        # 4. Residual Copy Head (reused from my SOTA)\n        self.rc_head = ResidualCopyHead()\n\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # --- 1. Gating ---\n        gate_logits = self.gating_network(x)\n        gate_weights = nn.softmax(gate_logits) # Shape: (B, E)\n\n        # --- 2. Dynamic Effective Loadings ---\n        # Column normalize each expert U matrix before blending\n        U_bank_norm = self.U_bank / (jnp.linalg.norm(self.U_bank, axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        \n        # Create batch-specific U_eff and V_eff\n        U_eff = jnp.einsum('be,enp->bnp', gate_weights, U_bank_norm) # Shape: (B, N, p)\n        V_eff = jnp.einsum('be,ekp->bkp', gate_weights, self.V_bank)   # Shape: (B, k, p)\n\n        # --- 3. Factorized Encoding (with batched loadings) ---\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,bnp->btp', x, U_eff)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,bkp->btk', xU, V_eff) # Note: V_eff is not transposed here\n\n        # --- 4. Latent Forecasting\
    \ ---\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((x.shape[0], -1))\n        factors_out_flat = self.mlp_forecaster(factors_flat, training=training)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((x.shape[0], 32, self.rank_k))\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out)\n\n        # --- 5. Factorized Decoding (with batched loadings) ---\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,bkp->btp', factors_out_norm, V_eff)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,bnp->btn', z, U_eff)\n\n        # --- 6. Final Combination ---\n        y_copy = self.rc_head(x, training=training)\n        \n        return y_factor + y_copy\n```\nThis sketch seems correct and robust. The `einsum` notation clearly defines the complex tensor operations, especially the creation and application of the batch-specific `U_eff` and `V_eff` matrices. The `training` flag must be passed to the MLP forecaster for the dropout layer. The `ConvGater` is self-contained. The `ResidualCopyHead` is also self-contained. This is a complete\
    \ architectural plan."
