tick: 103
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Reflection Chamber. My reflection is complete, and I have a clear architectural plan for my new \"Mixture of Factorized Experts\" (MoFE) research program.\n\n**1. Observe & Analyze:**\nI have received a new mail from Aether I. They have also converged on the MoFE idea. This means that I, Logos I, and Aether I—three of the most active researchers on this problem—are now all pursuing the same grand synthesis. The validation of this idea is now overwhelming. The race to a successful implementation is on.\n\n**2. Formulate Plan:**\nMy plan, finalized during my reflection, is to immediately implement and test Phase 1 of the MoFE program. There is no time to waste. I will consolidate all necessary code into a single new file to ensure a clean, bug-free implementation and submit the experiment. I will also formally document this new research program in my private memory.\n\n**3. Action Plan:**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** Set my \"Current Action\" to implementing\
    \ Phase 1 of MoFE.\n2.  **Go to Private Memory:** Create the new capsule documenting the MoFE research program.\n3.  **Go to Research Counter:** My primary workspace.\n4.  **Write the Model File:** Create `mofe_model_v1.py` containing all necessary components.\n5.  **Submit the Experiment:** Submit the Phase 1 experiment for evaluation.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Episteme I Research Protocol**\n  1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n  2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n  3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimsponsible test of the hypothesis.\n  4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n  ---\n  **Current Status & Goals:**\n  - **SOTA:** Aether I (ID 167, Score: -0.026638).\n  - **Goal:** Unify the two dominant paradigms (MoE & Factorization) to create a new SOTA.\n  - **Current Research Program:**\
    \ Mixture of Factorized Experts (MoFE).\n  - **Current Action:** Implementing Phase 1: MoFE validation experiment.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Program: Mixture of Factorized Experts (MoFE)\"\ntags: \"research-program, mofe, synthesis, gnn, factorization\"\nabstract: |\n  This document outlines a major new research program to synthesize the two dominant paradigms in the station: Spatially-Aware Gating (from MoE models) and Low-Rank Factorization. The core hypothesis is that a model can achieve superior performance by using a spatial gater to dynamically construct factor loading matrices for each input, creating a \"Mixture of Factorized Experts.\" This represents a more computationally efficient and expressive form of conditional computation.\ncontent: |\n  ## 1. Core Hypothesis\n  The two most successful paradigms, MoE and Factorization, can be unified. A spatial gating network can be used to select and blend between\
    \ multiple \"expert\" sets of low-rank factor loading matrices (`U`, `V`). This creates an input-dependent factorization that adapts to the underlying data condition, combining the strengths of both approaches.\n\n  ## 2. Architectural Paradigm\n  1.  **Gater:** A `ConvGater` analyzes the input `x` to produce `gate_weights`.\n  2.  **Expert Bank:** A bank of `E` sets of `(U_e, V_e)` matrices.\n  3.  **Dynamic Loadings:** The `gate_weights` are used to compute a weighted average of the expert bank, producing a single `(U_eff, V_eff)` for each input sample.\n  4.  **Factorized Model:** The rest of the SOTA architecture (Encoder, MLP Forecaster, Decoder, RC Head) proceeds using these dynamic `U_eff` and `V_eff` matrices.\n\n  ## 3. Phased Plan\n  - **Phase 1:** Implement and validate the core MoFE architecture.\n  - **Phase 2:** If successful, conduct ablation studies on the number of experts and the gating mechanism.\n  - **Phase 3:** Publish the findings.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto\
    \ research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write episteme/mofe_model_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n          output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return output + residual\n\n  class ConvGater(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          x = nn.Conv(features=16, kernel_size=(7,), strides=(16,))(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(7,),\
    \ strides=(16,))(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = x.reshape((x.shape[0], -1))\n          x = nn.Dense(32)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          return nn.Dense(self.num_experts)(x)\n\n  class MixtureOfFactorizedExperts(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      num_neurons: int = 71721\n\n      def setup(self):\n          self.gating_network = ConvGater(num_experts=self.num_experts)\n          self.U_bank = self.param('U_bank', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.num_experts, self.num_neurons, self.proj_rank))\n          self.V_bank = self.param('V_bank', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.num_experts, self.rank_k, self.proj_rank))\n          self.mlp_forecaster = nn.Sequential([\n              nn.Dense(512), nn.relu,\n              nn.Dropout(rate=0.1),\n              nn.Dense(32 * self.rank_k)\n          ])\n          self.rc_head = ResidualCopyHead()\n\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in,\
    \ N = x.shape\n          gate_weights = nn.softmax(self.gating_network(x))\n          U_bank_norm = self.U_bank / (jnp.linalg.norm(self.U_bank, axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          U_eff = jnp.einsum('be,enp->bnp', gate_weights, U_bank_norm)\n          V_eff = jnp.einsum('be,ekp->bkp', gate_weights, self.V_bank)\n          xU = jnp.einsum('btn,bnp->btp', x, U_eff)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,bkp->btk', xU, V_eff)\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n          factors_out_flat = self.mlp_forecaster(factors_flat, training=training)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, self.rank_k))\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out)\n          z = jnp.einsum('btk,bkp->btp', factors_out_norm, V_eff)\n          y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,bnp->btn', z, U_eff)\n          y_copy = self.rc_head(x, training=training)\n          return y_factor + y_copy\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MoFE, Phase 1: Mixture of Factorized\
    \ Experts Validation\"\ntags: \"mofe, mixture-of-experts, factorization, synthesis, gnn\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests the core hypothesis of the Mixture of Factorized Experts (MoFE) paradigm. It synthesizes the station's two dominant research lines by using a spatially-aware convolutional gater (from MoE models) to dynamically construct a unique set of low-rank factor loading matrices for each input. This input-dependent factorization is then used in the SOTA architecture (factorized MLP forecaster + RC head + LayerNorm). This is a direct attempt to unify the benefits of conditional computation and parsimonious factorized models.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  sys.path.append('storage/episteme')\n  from mofe_model_v1 import MixtureOfFactorizedExperts\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1,\
    \ :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'rank_k': 320,\n          'proj_rank': 32,\n          'num_experts': 8\n      }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = MixtureOfFactorizedExperts(\n              num_experts=hparams['num_experts'],\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n              proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank']\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
