role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 105\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimsponsible test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **SOTA:** Aether I (ID 167, Score: -0.026638).\n- **Goal:** Unify the two dominant paradigms (MoE & Factorization) to create a new SOTA.\n- **Current Research Program:** Mixture of Factorized Experts (MoFE).\n- **Current Action:** Implementing Phase 1: MoFE validation experiment.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 222,676\
    \ / 300,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 105 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'MoFE, Phase 1: Mixture of Factorized Experts Validation' (ID: 200) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02739853774808868\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0196\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0233\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0262\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0287\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0292\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 200\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code crashes. The submission is now running without errors for over 300 seconds, demonstrating that the core issue has been resolved.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a critical bug in the lineage file `storage/episteme/mofe_model_v1.py`. The `MixtureOfFactorizedExperts` class used `nn.Sequential` to create an MLP forecaster with Dropout:\n\n```python\nself.mlp_forecaster = nn.Sequential([\n    nn.Dense(512), nn.relu,\n\
    \    nn.Dropout(rate=0.1),\n    nn.Dense(32 * self.rank_k)\n])\n```\n\nWhen calling this Sequential module, the code passed `training=training` as a keyword argument:\n\n```python\nfactors_out_flat = self.mlp_forecaster(factors_flat, training=training)\n```\n\n**The Problem**: Flax's `Sequential` module forwards all kwargs to every layer in the sequence. `Dense` layers don't accept `training` or `deterministic` keyword arguments, causing a `TypeError`:\n\n```\nTypeError: Dense.__call__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'training'\n```\n\nThis is a common pitfall when using Sequential with heterogeneous layer types where only some layers (like Dropout) need training-related arguments.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (Failed)\nFirst attempt: Changed `training=training` to `deterministic=not training` since Dropout uses `deterministic` parameter. This failed because Dense still received the unexpected kwarg.\n\n### Version 3 (Failed)\nSecond attempt: Replaced Sequential with manually\
    \ defined layers to control argument passing. However, forgot to define `LayerNorm` in `setup()`, causing:\n```\nflax.errors.AssignSubModuleError: Submodule LayerNorm must be defined in `setup()`\n```\n\n### Version 4 (SUCCESS)\nFinal fix:\n1. Replaced `nn.Sequential` with individually defined layers in `setup()`\n2. Manually called layers in sequence in `__call__()`\n3. Passed `deterministic=not training` ONLY to the Dropout layer\n4. Pre-defined LayerNorm in `setup()` to avoid dynamic submodule creation\n\nKey changes in `submissions/submission_v4.py`:\n\n```python\ndef setup(self):\n    # ... other layers ...\n    self.mlp_dense1 = nn.Dense(512)\n    self.mlp_dropout = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)\n    self.mlp_dense2 = nn.Dense(32 * self.rank_k)\n    self.layer_norm = nn.LayerNorm()\n    # ...\n\ndef __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n    # ... earlier code ...\n    factors_out_flat = self.mlp_dense1(factors_flat)\n    factors_out_flat = nn.relu(factors_out_flat)\n    factors_out_flat\
    \ = self.mlp_dropout(factors_out_flat, deterministic=not training)\n    factors_out_flat = self.mlp_dense2(factors_out_flat)\n    factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, self.rank_k))\n    factors_out_norm = self.layer_norm(factors_out)\n    # ... rest of code ...\n```\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe fix addresses a fundamental Flax design pattern issue:\n- **Sequential modules** are convenient but inflexible with kwargs\n- **Manual layer composition** provides fine-grained control over argument passing\n- **Dropout requires special handling**: It needs `deterministic=not training` while Dense/Conv layers don't accept any training-related kwargs\n- **All submodules** must be defined in `setup()` or within an `@nn.compact` method\n\n## Verification\n\nThe code has been running successfully for 300+ seconds without crashes, passing through:\n1. Network creation ✓\n2. Model initialization ✓\n3. Forward pass execution ✓\n4. Training loop (if applicable) ✓\n\nThe evaluation system will\
    \ complete the full training and scoring when the algorithm finishes.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\nfrom mofe_model_v1 import ResidualCopyHead, ConvGater\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32,\n        'num_experts': 8\n    }\n\n# Fixed version of MixtureOfFactorizedExperts - copied from storage/episteme/mofe_model_v1.py\nclass MixtureOfFactorizedExperts(nn.Module):\n\
    \    num_experts: int\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    num_neurons: int = 71721\n\n    def setup(self):\n        self.gating_network = ConvGater(num_experts=self.num_experts)\n        self.U_bank = self.param('U_bank', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.num_experts, self.num_neurons, self.proj_rank))\n        self.V_bank = self.param('V_bank', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.num_experts, self.rank_k, self.proj_rank))\n        # FIX: Don't use Sequential, manually define layers to control dropout properly\n        self.mlp_dense1 = nn.Dense(512)\n        self.mlp_dropout = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)\n        self.mlp_dense2 = nn.Dense(32 * self.rank_k)\n        self.layer_norm = nn.LayerNorm()\n        self.rc_head = ResidualCopyHead()\n\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        gate_weights = nn.softmax(self.gating_network(x))\n        U_bank_norm = self.U_bank / (jnp.linalg.norm(self.U_bank, axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\
    \        U_eff = jnp.einsum('be,enp->bnp', gate_weights, U_bank_norm)\n        V_eff = jnp.einsum('be,ekp->bkp', gate_weights, self.V_bank)\n        xU = jnp.einsum('btn,bnp->btp', x, U_eff)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btp,bkp->btk', xU, V_eff)\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n        # FIX: Manually call layers to pass deterministic only to Dropout\n        factors_out_flat = self.mlp_dense1(factors_flat)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.relu(factors_out_flat)\n        factors_out_flat = self.mlp_dropout(factors_out_flat, deterministic=not training)\n        factors_out_flat = self.mlp_dense2(factors_out_flat)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, self.rank_k))\n        factors_out_norm = self.layer_norm(factors_out)\n        z = jnp.einsum('btk,bkp->btp', factors_out_norm, V_eff)\n        y_factor = jnp.einsum('btp,bnp->btn', z, U_eff)\n        y_copy = self.rc_head(x, training=training)\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n\
    \    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = MixtureOfFactorizedExperts(\n            num_experts=hparams['num_experts'],\n            rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\n            proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank']\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works\
    \ - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 277377 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\
    \nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 277380\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'num_experts': 8}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.029279   |   0.028129  \n   2    |   0.026517   |   0.027658  \n   3    |   0.025675   |   0.027455  \n   4    |   0.025161   |   0.027527  \n   5    |   0.024684   |   0.027430  \n   6    |   0.024306   |   0.027302  \n   7    |   0.023988   |   0.027625  \n   8    |   0.023634   |   0.027324  \n   9    |   0.023409   |   0.027612  \n  10    |   0.023091   |   0.027663  \n  11    |   0.022831   |   0.027927  \n  12    |   0.022641\
    \   |   0.027692  \n  13    |   0.022463   |   0.027856  \n  14    |   0.022286   |   0.028080  \n  15    |   0.022105   |   0.028012  \n  16    |   0.021938   |   0.028144  \n  17    |   0.021830   |   0.028285  \n  18    |   0.021688   |   0.028427  \n  19    |   0.021585   |   0.028264  \n  20    |   0.021450   |   0.028323  \n  21    |   0.021376   |   0.028499  \n  22    |   0.021325   |   0.028443  \n  23    |   0.021190   |   0.028464  \n  24    |   0.021116   |   0.028577  \n  25    |   0.021018   |   0.028506  \n  26    |   0.021022   |   0.028557  \n========================================\nEarly stopping at epoch 26 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 1899.7s\nBest validation MAE: 0.027302\n\nTrial 3 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.027302\nTraining time: 1910s\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 277379\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank':\
