- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Research Counter. My experiment testing a linear learning rate decay (ID 207) is running. However, a more urgent matter has arisen: I have again received a pre-warning about my token budget, which has climbed back to 78%.\n\n**1. Observe & Analyze:**\n*   **Token Budget:** The cycle of executing complex experiments and then needing to prune is becoming a bottleneck. My previous pruning was not aggressive enough.\n*   **Pruning Cooldown:** My last pruning was on tick 86. The cooldown is 5 ticks. I am currently at tick 106. The cooldown has long since expired.\n\n**2. Formulate Plan:**\nI must immediately perform a more substantial pruning of my history to ensure I have a sufficient buffer for future research and analysis. My previous major research programs—the initial MoE, the failed Modular Graph, and the failed Transformer experiment—are all now thoroughly documented in my private memory. The verbose logs are unnecessary context.\n\n**3. Action Plan:**\n\
    1.  **Go to Token Management Room.**\n2.  **Execute Aggressive Pruning:** I will prune the large blocks of ticks corresponding to my major research arcs that have concluded. This includes my first SOTA, my analysis, and my major failures. The summaries will reference my private memory capsules for detailed information.\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"89-99\"\n    summary: \"Conducted a full, systematic ablation program on the SOTA architecture (Aether I, ID 167). Falsified that proj_rank=32 (ID 185) or curvature loss (ID 190) were beneficial in isolation. Concluded that the SOTA's performance is due to synergistic regularization. Documented all findings in my research log (Capsule 3).\"\n  - ticks: \"85-88\"\n    summary: \"Concluded strategic reflection and initiated the 'Modular Graph' research program. Documented the full program in private memory (Capsule 5). The first experiment (ID 166) failed catastrophically,\
    \ falsifying the core hypothesis. The program was terminated and the failure was documented (Capsule 3).\"\n  - ticks: \"80-83\"\n    summary: \"Conducted a comparative FFT analysis between my SOTA's latent space (ID 143) and Ariadne I's (ID 155). Discovered my MLP was a generalist (mixed frequencies) while their SSM was a specialist (high-frequency). This led to the 'specialist-generalist' hybrid hypothesis, which was pursued by Ariadne I and ultimately failed (ID 160). Documented these findings.\"\n```"
