role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 112\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **SOTA:** Aether I (ID 167, Score: -0.026638). My best is -0.026743.\n- **Goal:** Beat the SOTA by improving the temporal modeling of the factorized architecture.\n- **Current Research Program:** Recurrent Factor Forecaster.\n- **Current Action:** Implementing Phase 1: GRU Encoder-Decoder validation.\n```\n- Agent\
    \ Token Budget: 176,289 / 300,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 112 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Recurrent Factor Forecaster, Phase 1: GRU Encoder-Decoder' (ID: 222) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.028223041901978798\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0197\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0234\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0266\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0295\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0312\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 222\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed multiple bugs in the agent's code. The submission now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (evaluation 222) had several bugs:\n\n1. **Import Error**: Attempted to import `FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN_Base` from `episteme_sota_v2.py`, but this class didn't\
    \ exist. Only `FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN` was available in the file.\n\n2. **Missing GRUCell Features**: The `recurrent_forecaster.py` file created `nn.GRUCell()` without the required `features` parameter, causing a TypeError.\n\n3. **Flax Module Scoping Issues**: Initial attempts to fix the code by creating separate `encode()` and `decode()` methods failed due to Flax's restriction that `self.param()` can only be called in methods decorated with `@nn.compact` or within `setup()`.\n\n4. **JAX Tracer Leaks**: Using `jax.lax.scan` with Flax modules inside scan functions caused tracer leaks because the GRUCell wasn't properly lifted through the transformation.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n**Final solution (submission_v11.py)**:\n\n1. **Eliminated the non-existent import**: Instead of trying to import a base class that doesn't exist, I inlined all the logic into a single `RecurrentSOTA` module.\n\n2. **Fixed the GRUEncoderDecoder implementation**:\n   - Added the required `features` parameter to\
    \ `nn.GRUCell(features=self.hidden_size)`\n   - Used `nn.RNN` wrapper for the encoder (which handles scan internally)\n   - Manually unrolled the decoder loop instead of using `jax.lax.scan` to avoid tracer complexity\n\n3. **Proper Flax architecture**: Combined everything into a single `@nn.compact` method that:\n   - Encodes input to latent factors using factorized projection matrices (U, V)\n   - Applies the GRU encoder-decoder forecaster in latent space\n   - Decodes back using MLP and LayerNorm\n   - Adds residual copy head for better performance\n\n## Key Changes from Original Code\n\n```python\n# Original (broken):\nfrom episteme_sota_v2 import FactorizedMLP_with_RC_LN_Base  # Class doesn't exist\nfrom recurrent_forecaster import GRUEncoderDecoder  # Has bugs\n\n# Fixed (v11):\n# Inlined all logic into RecurrentSOTA class\n# Fixed GRUEncoderDecoder by:\n#   - Adding features parameter to GRUCell\n#   - Using nn.RNN for encoder\n#   - Manual unroll for decoder (avoiding scan complexity)\n\
    ```\n\n## Technical Notes\n\n- The agent's concept was sound: use the SOTA factorized model's encoding/decoding with a GRU forecaster in between\n- The implementation bugs were:\n  1. Incorrect class name (expected vs. actual)\n  2. Missing required Flax parameters\n  3. Improper use of JAX scan with stateful Flax modules\n- The fix maintains the agent's intended architecture while correcting these implementation errors\n\n## Recommendation\n\nThe code now runs successfully. The architecture combines factorized projections with recurrent forecasting, which is a reasonable approach for the time series prediction task. Performance will be determined by the full training evaluation.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v11):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\n\
    from episteme_sota_v2 import ResidualCopyHead  # Import only what we need\n\n# Simplified GRUEncoderDecoder that avoids scan complexity\nclass GRUEncoderDecoder(nn.Module):\n    hidden_size: int\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # x shape: (B, 4, k)\n        batch_size = x.shape[0]\n        k = x.shape[2]\n\n        # 1. Encoder - use simple nn.RNN\n        # nn.RNN wraps a cell and handles the scan internally\n        encoder = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hidden_size))\n        encoder_outputs = encoder(x)  # (B, T, hidden_size)\n        context_vector = encoder_outputs[:, -1, :]  # Take final hidden state (B, hidden_size)\n\n        # 2. Decoder - manually unroll to avoid scan complexity\n        # Initialize decoder\n        decoder_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.hidden_size)\n        output_proj = nn.Dense(k)\n\n        # Start with context vector and zero output\n        h = context_vector\n       \
    \ prev_output = jnp.zeros((batch_size, k))\n\n        outputs = []\n        for _ in range(self.output_horizon):\n            # Update hidden state\n            h, _ = decoder_cell(h, prev_output)\n            # Generate output\n            out = output_proj(h)\n            outputs.append(out)\n            prev_output = out\n\n        # Stack outputs: list of (B, k) -> (B, T_out, k)\n        return jnp.stack(outputs, axis=1)\n\n# Combine everything into one compact module\nclass RecurrentSOTA(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n        # Step 1: Encode to latent factor space (from base model)\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp',\
    \ x, U_eff) @ V.T\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n\n        # Step 2: Apply GRU forecaster in latent space\n        forecaster = GRUEncoderDecoder(hidden_size=self.rank_k)\n        factors_out = forecaster(factors_in, training=training)\n\n        # Step 3: Decode from latent space (from base model)\n        # Apply MLP forecaster\n        factors_flat = factors_out.reshape((B, -1))\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * self.rank_k)(h)\n        factors_out_processed = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, self.rank_k))\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_processed)\n\n        y_factor = (factors_out_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 32\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n\
    \    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = RecurrentSOTA(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n        self.needs_rng = True # For dropout in RC head\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\n\
