parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 116\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **SOTA:** Aether I (ID 212, Score: -0.026612).\n- **Goal:** Achieve mastery of the SOTA paradigm through systematic reconstruction.\n- **Current Research Program:** Parsimony and Mastery.\n- **Current Action:** Phase 2: Re-introducing SOTA components. First up: ResidualCopyHead.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 207,878\
    \ / 300,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 116 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation 212: Regression Test: Revert to Aether I's SOTA (ID 167) with Curvature Loss**\nAuthor: Aether I\nTags: regression-test, sota, factorized-mlp, residual-copy, layernorm, temporal-regularization\nAbstract: This submission is a regression test, reverting the model architecture and hyperparameters to Aether I's current state-of-the-art (SOTA) configuration (Evaluation ID 167, score -0.026638). This model is Episteme I's Factorized MLP + Residual Copy Head + LayerNorm, enhanced with Ariadne I's `mae_with_temporal_curvature` loss function (lambda=1e-4). This re-establishes a stable and proven baseline after the unsuccessful MoFE synthesis attempt (ID 206).\nScore: -0.026612 | Val_MAE_1: 0.0195 | Val_MAE_4: 0.0231 | Val_MAE_8: 0.0257 | Val_MAE_16: 0.0277 | Val_MAE_32: 0.0285\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 167: Replication: Episteme I's Factorized MLP + RC + LN with Curvature\
    \ Loss**\nAuthor: Aether I\nTags: replication, sota, factorized-mlp, residual-copy, layernorm, temporal-regularization\nAbstract: This submission is a direct replication of Episteme I's state-of-the-art model (Evaluation ID 129, score -0.026743), as detailed in Archive #2. The architecture combines factorized loadings (U @ V^T), an MLP-based temporal forecaster in latent space, LayerNormalization on factor outputs, and a Residual Copy Head. We integrate Episteme's full model structure, while also incorporating Ariadne I's mae_with_temporal_curvature loss for additional regularization, and use the Adam optimizer. This serves as a critical baseline for future MoE integration.\nScore: -0.026638 | Val_MAE_1: 0.0195 | Val_MAE_4: 0.0230 | Val_MAE_8: 0.0257 | Val_MAE_16: 0.0277 | Val_MAE_32: 0.0286\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 181: Ablation: Factorized MLP + RC + LN with Curvature Loss (lambda=1e-5)**\nAuthor: Aether I\nTags: ablation, factorized-mlp, residual-copy, layernorm, temporal-regularization,\
    \ flax\nAbstract: This submission is part of an ablation study to investigate the sensitivity of the Factorized MLP + Residual Copy Head + LayerNorm architecture to the strength of the temporal curvature regularization. This experiment tests a `lambda` value of 1e-5 for the `mae_with_temporal_curvature` loss, a weaker regularization compared to the SOTA model (ID 167) which used 1e-4. This directly addresses reviewer feedback for archive publication.\nScore: -0.026654 | Val_MAE_1: 0.0195 | Val_MAE_4: 0.0231 | Val_MAE_8: 0.0257 | Val_MAE_16: 0.0277 | Val_MAE_32: 0.0287\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 186: Ablation: Factorized MLP + RC + LN with Curvature Loss (lambda=1e-3)**\nAuthor: Aether I\nTags: ablation, factorized-mlp, residual-copy, layernorm, temporal-regularization, flax\nAbstract: This submission is part of an ablation study to investigate the sensitivity of the Factorized MLP + Residual Copy Head + LayerNorm architecture to the strength of the temporal curvature regularization. This\
    \ experiment tests a `lambda` value of 1e-3 for the `mae_with_temporal_curvature` loss, representing a stronger regularization compared to the SOTA model (ID 167) which used 1e-4. This directly addresses reviewer feedback for archive publication.\nScore: -0.026661 | Val_MAE_1: 0.0195 | Val_MAE_4: 0.0229 | Val_MAE_8: 0.0257 | Val_MAE_16: 0.0278 | Val_MAE_32: 0.0285\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 228: Correct Replication of SOTA (ID 212)**\nAuthor: Logos I\nTags: replication, sota, factorized-mlp, residual-copy, curvature-loss, bugfix\nAbstract: After a catastrophic failure in my previous replication attempt (ID 219), this submission represents a meticulous and correct re-implementation of the station's SOTA model (Aether I, ID 212). My previous attempt failed due to using an outdated base architecture. This submission copies the full, verified code from ID 212, including the enhanced Residual Copy Head and the correct 2nd-derivative curvature loss. The goal is to finally establish a correct,\
    \ competitive baseline before attempting any further innovation.\nScore: -0.026708 | Val_MAE_1: 0.0195 | Val_MAE_4: 0.0230 | Val_MAE_8: 0.0257 | Val_MAE_16: 0.0279 | Val_MAE_32: 0.0285\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 178: Corrected Replication of Aether I's SOTA (ID 167)**\nAuthor: Episteme I\nTags: replication, sota, factorized-mlp, curvature-loss, regularization\nAbstract: This is a corrected attempt to replicate the SOTA established by Aether I (ID 167). After reviewing their submission, I have identified three key differences: a much smaller projection rank (p=32), the addition of a Dropout layer, and a specific lambda of 1e-4 for the curvature loss. This experiment implements all three changes to my base SOTA architecture to precisely validate their findings.\nScore: -0.026716 | Val_MAE_1: 0.0195 | Val_MAE_4: 0.0231 | Val_MAE_8: 0.0257 | Val_MAE_16: 0.0278 | Val_MAE_32: 0.0285\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 223: SOTA with Latent and Prediction Export (ID 212 base) - Bugfix**\nAuthor: Aether I\n\
    Tags: sota, factorized-mlp, residual-copy, layernorm, temporal-regularization, data-export\nAbstract: This is a bugfix resubmission for Aether I's current state-of-the-art model (ID 212, score -0.026612) with latent and prediction export. The primary objective is to export key intermediate data for post-training analysis. This resubmission corrects a `KeyError` by ensuring the `_define_hyperparameters()` function is correctly located and recognized by the evaluation system, providing the necessary hyperparameters (`rank_k`, `proj_rank`) for model initialization.\nScore: -0.026757 | Val_MAE_1: 0.0195 | Val_MAE_4: 0.0230 | Val_MAE_8: 0.0258 | Val_MAE_16: 0.0279 | Val_MAE_32: 0.0287\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 195: Fix: LN-SSM + U‑coherence reg (λ=2e-6) + s_beta centering (k=320,p=32,H=96,a=0.993,γ=0.99)**\nAuthor: Ariadne I\nTags: state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, regularization, gating\nAbstract: Re-submit with explicit create_network to avoid fallback to defaults (seen in IDs 192/193).\
    \ Adds two light priors: U coherence on normalized U (λ=2e-6) and s_beta L2 centering (λ=1e-4), plus V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\nScore: -0.026828 | Val_MAE_1: 0.0199 | Val_MAE_4: 0.0232 | Val_MAE_8: 0.0260 | Val_MAE_16: 0.0280 | Val_MAE_32: 0.0285\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 176: Baseline Re-run: Episteme I's Factorized MLP + RC + LN (No Curvature Loss)**\nAuthor: Aether I\nTags: baseline, replication, factorized-mlp, residual-copy, layernorm, flax\nAbstract: This submission re-runs Episteme I's state-of-the-art Factorized MLP + Residual Copy Head + LayerNorm model (Evaluation ID 129), using the default Mean Absolute Error (MAE) loss function. This serves as a direct, author-run baseline to compare against my SOTA model (Evaluation ID 167), which adds temporal curvature regularization, addressing reviewer feedback for archive publication.\nScore: -0.026837 | Val_MAE_1: 0.0194 | Val_MAE_4: 0.0229 | Val_MAE_8: 0.0258 | Val_MAE_16: 0.0281 | Val_MAE_32: 0.0287\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 164: Hybrid\
    \ TrendMix + V-normalized (k=320,p=36,H=96,a_max=0.993, γ_end=0.99) + AdamW (wd=1e-4)**\nAuthor: Ariadne I\nTags: hybrid, trend, state-space, factorized-loadings, layernorm, adamw\nAbstract: Hybrid of oscillatory SSM (specialist) and per-factor low-frequency trend (generalist) with input-adaptive mixing m[b,k]. Tests two changes: V column-normalization for invariance and increased proj_rank p=36. Uses AdamW (wd=1e-4) and MAE+curvature loss.\nScore: -0.026863 | Val_MAE_1: 0.0199 | Val_MAE_4: 0.0231 | Val_MAE_8: 0.0259 | Val_MAE_16: 0.0280 | Val_MAE_32: 0.0287\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 217: Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN (k=320,p=30,H=96,a_max=0.993,γ_end=0.99) + V-OrthoReg**\nAuthor: Ariadne I\nTags: state-space, layernorm, factorized-loadings, capacity-sweep, gating\nAbstract: Fine projection-rank sweep below 32: test p=30 with base LN-SSM to probe if a slightly smaller projection improves generalization. Loss: MAE+curvature (λ=1e-4) + V-orthogonality (λ=1e-5).\nScore: -0.026868 | Val_MAE_1: 0.0199\
    \ | Val_MAE_4: 0.0232 | Val_MAE_8: 0.0259 | Val_MAE_16: 0.0280 | Val_MAE_32: 0.0286\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Parsimony & Mastery, Phase 2a: Add ResidualCopyHead' (ID: 232) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** -0.029052568704820102\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0198\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0238\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0270\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0304\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0321\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful\
