tick: 118
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Research Counter. My systematic reconstruction of the SOTA continues.\n\n**1. Observe & Analyze:**\n*   **LN/U-Norm Experiment (ID 238):** The experiment was a resounding success. The score of **-0.026804** is a massive improvement over the previous model (-0.029053). This is my best score since my previous SOTA (ID 129), and it is very close to the station SOTA. My hypothesis is strongly validated: these normalization techniques are critical for stabilizing training and achieving high performance.\n*   **Author-Sorted Leaderboard:** The `rank author` command has provided a clear view of my own research history. It starkly illustrates my early successes with convolutions, my series of catastrophic failures with innovative architectures, and my current, successful return to this systematic, bottom-up approach.\n\n**2. Formulate Plan:**\nMy \"Parsimony and Mastery\" program is one step away from completion. I have systematically added the `ResidualCopyHead`\
    \ and the core `Normalization` techniques. The final component of the SOTA architecture (Aether I, ID 212) is the `Temporal Curvature Loss`.\n\n*New Hypothesis:* Adding the 2nd-derivative `Temporal Curvature Loss` to my current best model (`Factorized MLP + RC + LN`) will provide the final synergistic boost needed to match or surpass the station SOTA.\n\n**3. Action Plan:**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** I am now on the final step of my reconstruction program.\n2.  **Document LN/U-Norm Result:** Log the successful validation of the normalization techniques.\n3.  **Implement Final Step:** Submit a new experiment that adds the `Temporal Curvature Loss` to the model from ID 238. This will be a complete reconstruction of the SOTA architecture, built and validated by me, one component at a time.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Episteme I Research Protocol**\n  1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n  2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:**\
    \ State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n  3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n  4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n  ---\n  **Current Status & Goals:**\n  - **SOTA:** Aether I (ID 212, Score: -0.026612).\n  - **Goal:** Achieve mastery of the SOTA paradigm through systematic reconstruction.\n  - **Current Research Program:** Parsimony and Mastery.\n  - **Current Action:** Phase 2c: Adding Temporal Curvature Loss to complete the SOTA replication.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 3}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  ## Entry 27: Parsimony & Mastery, Phase 2b Complete\n\n  *   **Event:** My experiment adding `LayerNorm` and `U-Normalization` (ID 238) was highly successful, scoring -0.026804.\n  *   **Analysis:** This is a massive leap in performance and validates the critical role of these normalization techniques for training stability\
    \ and performance. I am now extremely close to the SOTA score.\n  *   **Next Step:** I will proceed to the final phase of reconstruction, Phase 2c, which is to re-introduce the `Temporal Curvature Loss`.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Parsimony & Mastery, Final Phase: Full SOTA Reconstruction\"\ntags: \"parsimony, factorization, sota, replication, curvature-loss\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the fourth and final experiment in the \"Parsimony and Mastery\" program. Building upon the successful Factorized MLP + RC + LN model (ID 238), this submission re-introduces the final component of the SOTA architecture: the 2nd-derivative temporal curvature loss. The goal is to complete the systematic, bottom-up reconstruction of the SOTA, validating the contribution of each component and demonstrating a full mastery of the paradigm.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  # Custom loss function is now required\n \
    \ def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      # 2nd derivative curvature penalty from the SOTA\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(residual, deterministic=not training)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n          output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return output + residual\n\n  class FullSOTAModel(nn.Module):\n\
    \      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      num_neurons: int = 71721\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          \n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          \n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_eff) @ V.T\n          \n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * k)(h)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, k))\n\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out)\n\n          y_factor = (factors_out_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          \n          y_copy\
    \ = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n          \n          return y_factor + y_copy\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return { 'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32 }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = FullSOTAModel(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n          self.needs_rng = True\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
