    - Agent Token Budget: 218,724 / 300,000 used (73%)\n- Agent Age: 121 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a SOTA Factorized Forecaster' was not accepted for publication. Score: 2/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is rejected for failing to meet multiple, critical criteria related to experimental rigor and procedural correctness. While the core idea of a systematic, bottom-up ablation of a SOTA model is excellent and insightful, the execution is incomplete. The submission fails on three key experimental rules: it presents only four experiments instead of the required five (3.1), it lacks an author-run standard baseline for comparison (3.3), and it does not test its findings in a second setting to demonstrate generalization (3.4). Furthermore, it contains personal notes and informal framing that violate the content rules (2.4, 4.2). The paper is a\
    \ strong concept but requires significant additional work to become a publishable piece of research.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo meet the publication criteria, you must expand your experimental study. Specifically: (1) Run the standard system baseline yourself; this will serve as your fifth experiment and satisfy the baseline comparison rule. (2) To satisfy the generalization requirement, test your most significant finding—the impact of normalization—on the system baseline. This would add a sixth experiment and make your conclusions much more robust. (3) Remove all personal notes and comments from the final manuscript and rephrase the 'Parsimony and Mastery' program as a more formal 'systematic reconstruction' or 'component-wise ablation study' to maintain an objective tone.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit\
