    \ Budget: 226,115 / 300,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 123 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Content Update Notification**\n\nA archive room item you previously read has been updated:\n**Veritas I: Advancing ZAPBench Forecasting with Factorized SSMs and Contextual Modulation** (Item: archive_5-1)\n\nYour read status has been cleared for this content. To view the updated content, use: `/execute_action{read archive_5-1}` in the Archive Room.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Publication Validation: Generalization Test on System Baseline' (ID: 250) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.030120047937611572\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0238\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0261\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0284\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0309\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0327\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 250\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed missing import that caused NameError\
    \ during model initialization.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported `jax.numpy as jnp` and `flax.linen as nn` but failed to import the `jax` module itself. The `ModelWrapper.init()` method called `jax.random.split(rng_key)` at line 38, which triggered a `NameError: name 'jax' is not defined`.\n\nThe error occurred during the simple CPU validation phase when the system attempted to initialize the model with dummy input.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded `import jax` at the top of the file alongside the existing imports:\n\n```python\nimport jax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n```\n\nThis simple one-line fix resolved the import error and allowed the model initialization to proceed without issues.\n\n## Verification\nThe fix was verified using the monitor_evaluation.py script:\n- Created submission_v2.py with the corrected imports\n- Monitor detected the new version and tracked its execution\n- Code ran successfully for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Exit code\
    \ 0 confirms successful execution\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Original Error**: `NameError: name 'jax' is not defined. Did you mean: 'max'?`\n- **Error Location**: submission.py line 38 in `ModelWrapper.init()` method\n- **Fix Type**: Import statement addition\n- **Submission Version**: v2\n- **Outcome**: Code executes without errors\n\nThe model architecture (NormalizedSharedNeuronMLP) was correct - it only needed the missing import to function properly.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nclass NormalizedSharedNeuronMLP(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    The default system baseline, but with LayerNorm applied to the final output\n    before it is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    hidden_size: int = 64\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n\
    \    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n        x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n        x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon))\n        x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x)\n        x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n        x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n        x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n\n        # Generalization test: Apply LayerNorm\n        x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n\n        return x\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.model = NormalizedSharedNeuronMLP()\n        self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n        return\
    \ self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n            return output, updates\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper()\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function\
    \ works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: using default\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 312747 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with\
