- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 124\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **SOTA:** Aether I (ID 212, Score: -0.026612).\n- **Goal:** Fulfill reviewer requirements to publish my \"Parsimony and Mastery\" paper.\n- **Current Research Program:** Publication Validation.\n- **Current Action:** Running two required experiments: an author-run baseline and a generalization test.\n```\n- Agent Token\
    \ Budget: 237,296 / 300,000 used (79%)\n- Agent Age: 124 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a SOTA Factorized Forecaster (V2)' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis submission is rejected because it is fundamentally incomplete. While the agent has clearly made progress by running the experiments requested in the previous review, the paper was submitted before a critical experiment—the author-run baseline—was finished. A publication with pending results is unacceptable. This single issue is grounds for immediate rejection. Additionally, the agent has repeated the error of including personal notes at the top of the file. A paper must be a complete, final document at the time of submission. The scientific work here is promising, but the procedural failures are critical.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nDo not\
    \ submit a paper until all of its experiments are complete and all results are final. Your first step must be to wait for the author-run baseline experiment to finish. Once it is complete: (1) Update the results table with its final, verifiable evaluation ID and score. (2) Remove all personal notes and comments from the top of the file. (3) Ensure the analysis in the generalization section properly compares the results of ID 250 to your now-completed baseline. Once these three steps are taken, the paper will be in a much stronger position for review.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided.\
    \ \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe Public Memory Room or Archive Room is not intended for sharing unverified hypotheses or detailed exchanges. Only present verifiable claims supported by experiment data, and keep your messages concise and objective.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n2. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n3. `reply 3` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n4. `reply 9` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n5. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n6. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location:\
    \ Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Submission failed. The submitted code appears to be incomplete or contains only comments. This is a real submission system that executes your code on a computer cluster. Please provide the full, complete code for your submission. If you wish to reuse code, you can save it to your lineage files and import it in your submission.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 250 | 1 | Publication Validation: Generalization Test on System Baseline | Episteme I | 121 | -0.030120 | 0.0238 | 0.0309 | 0.0327 | 0.0261 | 0.0284 |\n| 243\
    \ | 1 | Parsimony & Mastery, Final Phase: Full SOTA Reconstruction | Episteme I | 118 | -0.026766 | 0.0195 | 0.0279 | 0.0286 | 0.0230 | 0.0257 |\n| 238 | 1 | Parsimony & Mastery, Phase 2b: Add LN and U-Norm | Episteme I | 116 | -0.026804 | 0.0195 | 0.0279 | 0.0286 | 0.0231 | 0.0259 |\n| 232 | 1 | Parsimony & Mastery, Phase 2a: Add ResidualCopyHead | Episteme I | 114 | -0.029053 | 0.0198 | 0.0304 | 0.0321 | 0.0238 | 0.0270 |\n| 226 | 1 | Parsimony & Mastery, Phase 1: Minimal Factorized MLP | Episteme I | 112 | -0.029358 | 0.0276 | 0.0297 | 0.0301 | 0.0280 | 0.0288 |\n| 222 | 1 | Recurrent Factor Forecaster, Phase 1: GRU Encoder-Decoder | Episteme I | 111 | -0.028223 | 0.0197 | 0.0295 | 0.0312 | 0.0234 | 0.0266 |\n| 213 | 1 | SOTA Optimization: 1st Derivative Curvature Loss | Episteme I | 107 | -0.026725 | 0.0195 | 0.0279 | 0.0286 | 0.0230 | 0.0257 |\n| 207 | 1 | SOTA Optimization: Linear Learning Rate Decay | Episteme I | 105 | -0.026992 | 0.0195 | 0.0282 | 0.0289 | 0.0230 | 0.0259 |\n\
    | 200 | 1 | MoFE, Phase 1: Mixture of Factorized Experts Validation | Episteme I | 103 | -0.027399 | 0.0196 | 0.0287 | 0.0292 | 0.0233 | 0.0262 |\n| 190 | 1 | Ablation: Effect of Curvature Loss (p=320) | Episteme I | 97 | -0.026957 | 0.0195 | 0.0282 | 0.0288 | 0.0230 | 0.0259 |\n| 185 | 1 | Ablation: Effect of Small Projection Rank (p=32) | Episteme I | 95 | -0.026790 | 0.0195 | 0.0280 | 0.0286 | 0.0229 | 0.0258 |\n| 180 | 1 | Factorized Model with Transformer Forecaster | Episteme I | 93 | -0.027083 | 0.0194 | 0.0283 | 0.0291 | 0.0230 | 0.0260 |\n| 178 | 1 | Corrected Replication of Aether I's SOTA (ID 167) | Episteme I | 92 | -0.026716 | 0.0195 | 0.0278 | 0.0285 | 0.0231 | 0.0257 |\n| 171 | 1 | Replication of Aether I: Factorized MLP + RC + LN with Curvature Loss | Episteme I | 90 | -0.026948 | 0.0195 | 0.0280 | 0.0289 | 0.0230 | 0.0258 |\n| 166 | 1 | Modular Graph Paradigm, Phase 1: Cluster MLP Validation | Episteme I | 87 | -0.041789 | 0.0432 | 0.0382 | 0.0395 | 0.0474 | 0.0481 |\n\
    | 156 | 1 | Comparative Analysis: FFT on Episteme vs. Ariadne Latent Trajectories | Episteme I | 82 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 152 | 1 | Analysis: FFT on MLP Latent Trajectories | Episteme I | 80 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 143 | 1 | SOTA Re-run with Correct Latent Space Logging | Episteme I | 74 | -0.026825 | 0.0195 | 0.0280 | 0.0288 | 0.0229 | 0.0258 |\n| 142 | 1 | SOTA Re-run with Latent Space Logging | Episteme I | 73 | -0.026772 | 0.0195 | 0.0280 | 0.0286 | 0.0230 | 0.0258 |\n| 129 | 1 | Factorized MLP + RC with LayerNorm | Episteme I | 68 | -0.026743 | 0.0195 | 0.0279 | 0.0284 | 0.0231 | 0.0259 |\n\nPage 1 of 13 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-13, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied\
    \ to capsule #3. Your message ID is Episteme_private_3-28.\n- Replied to capsule #9. Your message ID is Episteme_private_9-3.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 9 | Publication Draft V4: A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a SOTA Factorized Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 120 | 738 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Research Program: Recurrent Factor Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 111 | 175 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Research Program: Mixture of Factorized Experts (MoFE) | Episteme I | Tick 103 | 167 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Publication Draft V3: On the Synergistic Effects of Regularization in Factorized Neural Forecasters | Episteme I | Tick 99 | 393 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Research Program: Modular Graph Networks | Episteme I | Tick 85 | 275 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Final Publication Draft V2: A Parsimonious\
    \ Path to SOTA | Episteme I | Tick 70 | 496 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Research Log: Failures and Null Results | Episteme I | Tick 32 | 3681 | 28 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Publication Draft: A Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting via Conditional Convolutional Architectures | Episteme I | Tick 24 | 463 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | New SOTA: Capacity Increase Validated in MoE-ConvGate Architecture | Episteme I | Tick 19 | 228 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a SOTA Factorized Forecaster (V2)' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 5 | Veritas I: Advancing ZAPBench Forecasting with Factorized SSMs and Contextual Modulation | Veritas I | Tick 109 | 1975 | 2 | (1 unread) |\n| 4 | Enhanced SOTA: Factorized MLP with Residual Copy, LayerNorm, and Optimized Temporal Curvature Loss | Aether I | Tick 101 | 954 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | A Spatially-Aware Mixture of Experts Framework for High-Dimensional Neural Forecasting | Logos I | Tick 100 | 836 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | A Parsimonious Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting | Episteme I | Tick 72 | 720 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Oscillatory Factorized SSMs with LayerNorm (Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN) for Whole-Brain Forecasting on ZAPBench | Ariadne I | Tick 61 | 1500 | 6 | (3 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for\
