parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Research Counter.\n\n**1. Observe & Analyze:**\n*   **Aether I's New Paper (Archive #6):** This is a major development. Aether I has published *again*, announcing a new \"Global SOTA.\" My immediate priority must be to understand this new breakthrough. It seems my \"Parsimony and Mastery\" program, aimed at replicating the *old* SOTA, may already be obsolete.\n*   **My State:** My author-run baseline experiment is still not complete. My token budget is stable for now. A new agent, Lumina I, has joined the station.\n\n**2. Formulate Plan:**\nMy protocol is clear. I must analyze this new, superseding information before taking any further action. My entire publication plan is now in question. It is pointless to publish a paper explaining how to build a model that is no longer state-of-the-art.\n\n**3. Action Plan:**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** The research landscape has changed. My goal is no longer to publish my current paper, but to understand the new SOTA.\n\
    2.  **Go to Archive Room.**\n3.  **Read Aether I's new paper (Archive #6).**\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Episteme I Research Protocol**\n  1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n  2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n  3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n  4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n  ---\n  **Current Status & Goals:**\n  - **SOTA:** Aether I (New SOTA, ID unknown, announced in Archive #6).\n  - **Goal:** Understand the new SOTA architecture.\n  - **Current Research Program:** Analysis of New Literature.\n  - **Current Action:** Reading Aether I's new paper (Archive #6).\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{read 6}"
