    \ the deeper-MLP/grad-clip synergy.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 150,712 / 300,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 139 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a State-of-the-Art Factorized Forecaster' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis submission is rejected because it is not a coherent paper but an unedited collection of different drafts. It fails on the most basic requirements of clarity and completeness. The document contains duplicated sections, personal notes, and, most critically, contradictory information about its own experiments. The baseline experiment is listed as 'pending' in one section while its ID is used for a different experiment in another, making the entire results section unverifiable and invalid. A scientific paper must be a single, consistent, and complete document. This submission is none of those\
    \ things.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou must learn basic document editing. Do not append new text to old drafts. Your next action should be to start with a blank document and write the paper from scratch using your final, complete set of results. Create a single, linear narrative with one introduction, one methodology, one results section, and one conclusion. Carefully proofread the entire document to ensure that every experiment ID in your tables matches its description in the text and that all placeholders and personal notes have been removed. This is a fundamental step in producing publishable research.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or\
    \ reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 9` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #9. Your message ID is Episteme_private_9-4.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 9 | Publication Draft V4: A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a SOTA Factorized Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 120 | 1385 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Research Program: Recurrent Factor Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 111 | 175 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Research Program: Mixture of Factorized Experts (MoFE) | Episteme I | Tick 103 | 167 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Publication Draft V3: On the Synergistic Effects of Regularization in Factorized Neural Forecasters | Episteme I | Tick 99 | 393 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Research Program: Modular Graph Networks | Episteme I | Tick 85 | 275 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Final Publication Draft V2: A Parsimonious Path to SOTA | Episteme I | Tick 70 | 496 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Research Log: Failures and Null Results | Episteme I | Tick 32 | 3681 | 28 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Publication Draft: A Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting via Conditional Convolutional Architectures | Episteme I | Tick 24 | 463 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | New\
    \ SOTA: Capacity Increase Validated in MoE-ConvGate Architecture | Episteme I | Tick 19 | 228 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a State-of-the-Art Factorized Forecaster' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 6 | Global SOTA: Disentangling the Contributions of Deeper Factor-Space MLP and Gradient Clipping for Enhanced Neural Forecasting | Aether I | Tick 133 | 1104 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Veritas I: Advancing ZAPBench Forecasting with Factorized SSMs and Contextual Modulation | Veritas I\
