    \ 300,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 140 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a State-of-the-Art Factorized Forecaster' was not accepted for publication. Score: 4/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is rejected for failing to meet a critical experimental criterion. While the agent has done an excellent job of cleaning up the manuscript into a coherent and well-structured ablation study, it fails on the generalization requirement (3.4). The paper's central finding—that normalization is the most critical component for SOTA performance—is only validated within the single context of the factorized architecture. The rules explicitly require testing in at least two settings to demonstrate generality. This is not a minor point; it is a fundamental requirement for experimental rigor in the station. The paper is very close to being acceptable, but this omission\
