    \ 300,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 142 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Publication Generalization Test: System Baseline + LayerNorm' (ID: 289) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.029994825000967184\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0200\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0240\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0275\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0313\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0338\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 289\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the missing import error. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission code used `jax.random.split(rng_key)` in the `ModelWrapper.init()` method (line 38), but only imported `jax.numpy as jnp`, not the main `jax` module. This caused a `NameError: name 'jax' is not defined` during initialization.\n\nThe error occurred in:\n```python\ndef init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n    rng_params,\
    \ rng_dropout = jax.random.split(rng_key)  # ← jax not imported!\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded `import jax` at the beginning of the submission file.\n\n**Changed:**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n```\n\n**To:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n```\n\nThis was a simple one-line fix that resolved the import error without requiring any changes to the actual logic of the code.\n\n## Verification\n- Created `submission_v2.py` with the import fix\n- Ran `monitor_evaluation.py 2` which confirmed the code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Exit code 0: The submission is now running successfully\n\n## Recommendation\nThe submission is now functional. The agent (Episteme I) was testing a modified SharedNeuronMLP architecture with an added LayerNorm layer. The code structure and logic appear sound - this was purely an import oversight that has now been corrected.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files\
    \ in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\n# This is the default SharedNeuronMLP from system/defaults.py\n# with the addition of a LayerNorm layer.\nclass SharedNeuronMLPWithLN(nn.Module):\n    hidden_size: int = 64\n    output_horizon: int = 32\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        batch_size, input_horizon, num_neurons = x.shape\n        x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n        x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size * num_neurons, input_horizon))\n\n        x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(x)\n        x = nn.BatchNorm(use_running_average=not training)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=not training)(x)\n\n        # Added LayerNorm\n        x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n\n        x = nn.Dense(self.output_horizon)(x)\n\
    \n        x = jnp.reshape(x, (batch_size, num_neurons, self.output_horizon))\n        x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n        return x\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.model = SharedNeuronMLPWithLN()\n        self.mutable = ['batch_stats']\n        self.needs_rng = True\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout': rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, mutable=None, rngs=None):\n        if mutable:\n            output, updates = self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, mutable=mutable, rngs=rngs)\n            return output, updates\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper()\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=''\
