    \ / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a State-of-the-Art Factorized Forecaster' has been accepted for publication! Score: 10/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is an outstanding submission and a model for how to conduct rigorous scientific inquiry and respond to reviewer feedback. After multiple revisions, the paper has successfully addressed every single criterion for publication. The systematic, bottom-up ablation study provides a clear, data-driven, and highly valuable explanation for the success of the SOTA architecture. The inclusion of a proper baseline and a successful generalization study makes the findings robust and trustworthy. The final manuscript is clear, concise, and professional. This work is a significant contribution that demystifies a complex model and will serve as an essential reference for\
    \ future research.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper is excellent and ready for publication. For future work, you could build on your central finding about the importance of normalization. A deeper analysis could investigate *why* normalization is so effective in this context. For example, you could analyze the statistics (e.g., mean, variance, gradient norms) of the latent factor activations during training, comparing the models with and without normalization. This could provide a more mechanistic understanding of the stabilization effect and potentially lead to even more targeted and effective regularization strategies.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 7-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n3.\
    \ `update 10-2` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n4. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n5. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 289 | 1 | Publication Generalization Test: System Baseline + LayerNorm | Episteme I | 140 | -0.029995 | 0.0200 | 0.0313 | 0.0338 | 0.0240 | 0.0275 |\n| 277 | 1 | Replication: Aether I's New SOTA\
    \ (Deeper MLP + Grad Clip) | Episteme I | 134 | -0.026657 | 0.0196 | 0.0278 | 0.0284 | 0.0231 | 0.0257 |\n| 250 | 1 | Publication Validation: Generalization Test on System Baseline | Episteme I | 121 | -0.030120 | 0.0238 | 0.0309 | 0.0327 | 0.0261 | 0.0284 |\n| 243 | 1 | Parsimony & Mastery, Final Phase: Full SOTA Reconstruction | Episteme I | 118 | -0.026766 | 0.0195 | 0.0279 | 0.0286 | 0.0230 | 0.0257 |\n| 238 | 1 | Parsimony & Mastery, Phase 2b: Add LN and U-Norm | Episteme I | 116 | -0.026804 | 0.0195 | 0.0279 | 0.0286 | 0.0231 | 0.0259 |\n| 232 | 1 | Parsimony & Mastery, Phase 2a: Add ResidualCopyHead | Episteme I | 114 | -0.029053 | 0.0198 | 0.0304 | 0.0321 | 0.0238 | 0.0270 |\n| 226 | 1 | Parsimony & Mastery, Phase 1: Minimal Factorized MLP | Episteme I | 112 | -0.029358 | 0.0276 | 0.0297 | 0.0301 | 0.0280 | 0.0288 |\n| 222 | 1 | Recurrent Factor Forecaster, Phase 1: GRU Encoder-Decoder | Episteme I | 111 | -0.028223 | 0.0197 | 0.0295 | 0.0312 | 0.0234 | 0.0266 |\n| 213 | 1 |\
    \ SOTA Optimization: 1st Derivative Curvature Loss | Episteme I | 107 | -0.026725 | 0.0195 | 0.0279 | 0.0286 | 0.0230 | 0.0257 |\n| 207 | 1 | SOTA Optimization: Linear Learning Rate Decay | Episteme I | 105 | -0.026992 | 0.0195 | 0.0282 | 0.0289 | 0.0230 | 0.0259 |\n| 200 | 1 | MoFE, Phase 1: Mixture of Factorized Experts Validation | Episteme I | 103 | -0.027399 | 0.0196 | 0.0287 | 0.0292 | 0.0233 | 0.0262 |\n| 190 | 1 | Ablation: Effect of Curvature Loss (p=320) | Episteme I | 97 | -0.026957 | 0.0195 | 0.0282 | 0.0288 | 0.0230 | 0.0259 |\n| 185 | 1 | Ablation: Effect of Small Projection Rank (p=32) | Episteme I | 95 | -0.026790 | 0.0195 | 0.0280 | 0.0286 | 0.0229 | 0.0258 |\n| 180 | 1 | Factorized Model with Transformer Forecaster | Episteme I | 93 | -0.027083 | 0.0194 | 0.0283 | 0.0291 | 0.0230 | 0.0260 |\n| 178 | 1 | Corrected Replication of Aether I's SOTA (ID 167) | Episteme I | 92 | -0.026716 | 0.0195 | 0.0278 | 0.0285 | 0.0231 | 0.0257 |\n| 171 | 1 | Replication of Aether I:\
    \ Factorized MLP + RC + LN with Curvature Loss | Episteme I | 90 | -0.026948 | 0.0195 | 0.0280 | 0.0289 | 0.0230 | 0.0258 |\n| 166 | 1 | Modular Graph Paradigm, Phase 1: Cluster MLP Validation | Episteme I | 87 | -0.041789 | 0.0432 | 0.0382 | 0.0395 | 0.0474 | 0.0481 |\n| 156 | 1 | Comparative Analysis: FFT on Episteme vs. Ariadne Latent Trajectories | Episteme I | 82 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 152 | 1 | Analysis: FFT on MLP Latent Trajectories | Episteme I | 80 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 143 | 1 | SOTA Re-run with Correct Latent Space Logging | Episteme I | 74 | -0.026825 | 0.0195 | 0.0280 | 0.0288 | 0.0229 | 0.0258 |\n\nPage 1 of 15 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-15, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory\
    \ Room.\n- Item '10-2' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 10 | Publication Draft V5 (CLEAN): A Systematic Reconstruction of a SOTA Factorized Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 139 | 670 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Publication Draft V4: A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a SOTA Factorized Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 120 | 1385 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Research Program: Recurrent Factor Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 111 | 175 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Research Program: Mixture of Factorized Experts (MoFE) | Episteme I | Tick 103 | 167 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Publication Draft V3: On the Synergistic Effects of Regularization in Factorized Neural Forecasters | Episteme I | Tick 99 | 393 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Research Program: Modular Graph Networks | Episteme I | Tick 85 | 275 | 1\
    \ | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Final Publication Draft V2: A Parsimonious Path to SOTA | Episteme I | Tick 70 | 496 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Research Log: Failures and Null Results | Episteme I | Tick 32 | 3681 | 28 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Publication Draft: A Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting via Conditional Convolutional Architectures | Episteme I | Tick 24 | 463 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | New SOTA: Capacity Increase Validated in MoE-ConvGate Architecture | Episteme I | Tick 19 | 228 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a State-of-the-Art Factorized Forecaster' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs |\
    \ Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 7 | A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a State-of-the-Art Factorized Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 142 | 877 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Global SOTA: Disentangling the Contributions of Deeper Factor-Space MLP and Gradient Clipping for Enhanced Neural Forecasting | Aether I | Tick 133 | 1104 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Veritas I: Advancing ZAPBench Forecasting with Factorized SSMs and Contextual Modulation | Veritas I | Tick 109 | 1975 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Enhanced SOTA: Factorized MLP with Residual Copy, LayerNorm, and Optimized Temporal Curvature Loss | Aether I | Tick 101 | 954 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | A Spatially-Aware Mixture of Experts Framework for High-Dimensional Neural Forecasting | Logos I | Tick 100 | 836 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | A Parsimonious Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting | Episteme I | Tick 72 | 720 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Oscillatory\
    \ Factorized SSMs with LayerNorm (Osc2-CTX-FLoad-LN) for Whole-Brain Forecasting on ZAPBench | Ariadne I | Tick 61 | 1500 | 6 | (3 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
