tick: 147
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Research Counter. My analytical experiment has failed.\n\n**1. Observe & Analyze:**\n*   **Error Analysis (ID 302):** The traceback is clear: `TypeError: ModelWrapper.apply() got an unexpected keyword argument 'mutable'`. This happened because my `loss_fn` in the `test()` block tried to pass `mutable=['batch_stats']` to the `apply` function. However, the `ResidualCopyHead` (which is the only component that might use BatchNorm) is the source of this requirement. In my main `UnnormalizedSOTAModel`, I don't use BatchNorm, so my `ModelWrapper.apply` doesn't accept `mutable`. The `ResidualCopyHead` *does* contain a `Dropout` layer, which is why `needs_rng=True` is still required, but it does not contain `BatchNorm`.\n*   **Root Cause:** This is a copy-paste error. I adapted the analysis code from a previous experiment that *did* use BatchNorm, and I failed to remove the `mutable` argument when it was no longer needed.\n\n**2. Formulate Plan:**\nThe fix is trivial.\
    \ I need to remove the `mutable=['batch_stats']` argument from the `model.apply` call within my analytical `test()` function. I will correct this and resubmit both analytical runs—the un-normalized one that just failed, and the fully-normalized one that I had planned to run next. I will submit them back-to-back to be efficient.\n\n**3. Action Plan:**\n1.  **Submit Corrected Un-normalized Run:** Resubmit the code from ID 302 with the `mutable` argument removed.\n2.  **Submit Normalized Run:** Submit the same analytical code, but using the fully-normalized SOTA model.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis Data Collection: Un-Normalized Model (v2, fix)\"\ntags: \"analysis, gradients, normalization, data-collection, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a bugfix for ID 302. The original analytical run failed due to a TypeError from passing an unnecessary 'mutable' argument. This version removes the erroneous argument from the test() function. The goal remains to collect gradient\
    \ norm and latent activation statistics from the un-normalized SOTA model for a comparative analysis.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  import jax\n\n  # --- Full Un-normalized SOTA model code from ID 299 ---\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(residual, deterministic=not training)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0],\
    \ num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n          output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return output + residual\n\n  class UnnormalizedSOTAModel(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      num_neurons: int = 71721\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_eff) @ V.T\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n\
    \          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * k)(h)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, k))\n          factors_out_norm = factors_out\n          y_factor = (factors_out_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n          return y_factor + y_copy, (factors_in, factors_out)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return { 'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32 }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = UnnormalizedSOTAModel(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n          self.needs_rng = True\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n     \
    \     return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def test():\n      print(\"--- Starting Un-normalized Model Analysis (v2) ---\")\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      model = create_network(hparams)\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      \n      dummy_input = jnp.ones((2, 4, 71721))\n      dummy_targets = jnp.ones((2, 32, 71721))\n      \n      params = model.init(key, dummy_input)\n      \n      def loss_fn(p):\n          # The apply function needs rngs for the Dropout in RC head\n          (preds, (factors_in, factors_out)) = model.apply(p, dummy_input, training=True, rngs={'dropout': key})\n          loss = compute_loss(preds, dummy_targets, p, dummy_input)\n          return loss, (preds, factors_in, factors_out)\n\n      (loss_val, (preds, factors_in, factors_out)), grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn, has_aux=True)(params)\n      \n      global_grad_norm = optax.global_norm(grads)\n\
    \      \n      print(f\"--- Un-normalized Model Stats ---\")\n      print(f\"Global Grad Norm: {global_grad_norm}\")\n      print(f\"Factors In (Mean, Std): {jnp.mean(factors_in)}, {jnp.std(factors_in)}\")\n      print(f\"Factors Out (Mean, Std): {jnp.mean(factors_out)}, {jnp.std(factors_out)}\")\n      \n      return \"SUCCESS: Data collection for un-normalized model complete.\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis Data Collection: Normalized SOTA Model\"\ntags: \"analysis, gradients, normalization, data-collection\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second part of my data collection for mechanistic analysis. I am running the fully-normalized SOTA model (from ID 277) with instrumentation to log gradient norms and latent activation statistics. This data will be compared against the un-normalized run (ID 302-fix) to analyze the mechanistic effect of normalization. This experiment uses the test() function and will not produce a score.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen\
    \ as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  import jax\n\n  # --- Full NORMALIZED SOTA model code from ID 277 ---\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(residual, deterministic=not training)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n          output = output.at[:, :4,\
    \ :].set(x)\n          return output + residual\n\n  class NormalizedSOTAModel(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      num_neurons: int = 71721\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          \n          # NORMALIZATION PRESENT\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          \n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_eff) @ V.T\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(h)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          factors_out_flat\
    \ = nn.Dense(32 * k)(h)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, k))\n          \n          # NORMALIZATION PRESENT\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out)\n          \n          y_factor = (factors_out_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n          return y_factor + y_copy, (factors_in, factors_out, factors_out_norm)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return { 'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32 }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = NormalizedSOTAModel(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n          self.needs_rng = True\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n  \
    \    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def test():\n      print(\"--- Starting Normalized SOTA Model Analysis ---\")\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      model = create_network(hparams)\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      \n      dummy_input = jnp.ones((2, 4, 71721))\n      dummy_targets = jnp.ones((2, 32, 71721))\n      \n      params = model.init(key, dummy_input)\n      \n      def loss_fn(p):\n          (preds, intermediates) = model.apply(p, dummy_input, training=True, rngs={'dropout': key})\n          loss = compute_loss(preds, dummy_targets, p, dummy_input)\n          return loss, intermediates\n\n      (loss_val, (factors_in, factors_out, factors_out_norm)), grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn, has_aux=True)(params)\n      \n      global_grad_norm = optax.global_norm(grads)\n      \n     \
    \ print(f\"--- Normalized SOTA Model Stats ---\")\n      print(f\"Global Grad Norm: {global_grad_norm}\")\n      print(f\"Factors In (Mean, Std): {jnp.mean(factors_in)}, {jnp.std(factors_in)}\")\n      print(f\"Factors Out (Pre-LN) (Mean, Std): {jnp.mean(factors_out)}, {jnp.std(factors_out)}\")\n      print(f\"Factors Out (Post-LN) (Mean, Std): {jnp.mean(factors_out_norm)}, {jnp.std(factors_out_norm)}\")\n      \n      return \"SUCCESS: Data collection for normalized model complete.\"\n```"
