parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 149\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **My Best Score:** -0.026657 (ID 277). Paper Published (Archive #7).\n- **Goal:** Understand the mechanistic reason for normalization's effectiveness.\n- **Current Research Program:** Mechanistic Analysis of Normalization.\n- **Current Action:** Collecting *temporal* statistics (unclipped grad norms, latent stats over\
    \ time).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 203,437 / 300,000 used (68%)\n- Agent Age: 149 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Temporal Analysis: Un-Normalized Model Dynamics' (ID: 312) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** n.a.\n**Val_MAE_1:** None\n**Val_MAE_4:** None\n**Val_MAE_8:** None\n**Val_MAE_16:** None\n**Val_MAE_32:** None\n**Evaluation Details:** Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 312\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code by correcting the optax API usage. The submission now runs without crashing and completes its temporal dynamics analysis successfully.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code used an incorrect optax API call:\n```python\nupdates, new_opt_s = optimizer.apply_updates(grads, opt_s)\n```\n\nThe `GradientTransformationExtraArgs`\
    \ object (returned by `optax.adam()`) does not have an `apply_updates` method. This caused an `AttributeError` on line 74 of the original submission.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 74-75 in the `train_step` function to use the correct optax API:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\nupdates, new_opt_s = optimizer.apply_updates(grads, opt_s)\nnew_p = optax.apply_updates(p, updates)\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\nupdates, new_opt_s = optimizer.update(grads, opt_s)\nnew_p = optax.apply_updates(p, updates)\n```\n\nThe correct optax pattern is:\n1. `optimizer.update(grads, opt_state)` - computes parameter updates\n2. `optax.apply_updates(params, updates)` - applies updates to parameters\n\n## Verification\nAfter applying the fix in `submission_v2.py`, the code executed successfully:\n- All 10 training steps completed\n- Temporal dynamics metrics were computed (gradient norms, factor statistics)\n- Test function returned success message\n- No crashes or errors occurred\n\nThe evaluation shows the intended\
    \ behavior: analyzing gradient norm growth and factor output statistics for an un-normalized model over 10 training steps.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nimport jax\n\n# --- Code for UnnormalizedSOTAModel and helpers from ID 308 ---\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); residual = nn.relu(residual)\n\
    \        residual = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(residual, deterministic=not training)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n        residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons)); output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return output + residual\n\nclass UnnormalizedSOTAModel(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; num_neurons: int = 71721\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p)); U_eff = U\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_eff) @ V.T\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n\
    \        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * k)(h)\n        factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, k)); factors_out_norm = factors_out\n        y_factor = (factors_out_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n        return y_factor + y_copy, (factors_in, factors_out)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = UnnormalizedSOTAModel(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n        self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\
    \n# NOTE: The create_optimizer function is intentionally omitted to use the default (unclipped) adam.\n\ndef test():\n    print(\"--- Starting Temporal Dynamics Analysis (Un-normalized) ---\")\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n    model = create_network(hparams)\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n\n    dummy_input = jnp.ones((2, 4, 71721))\n    dummy_targets = jnp.ones((2, 32, 71721))\n\n    params = model.init(key, dummy_input)\n    # Use an unclipped optimizer for this analysis\n    optimizer = optax.adam(learning_rate=hparams['learning_rate'])\n    opt_state = optimizer.init(params)\n\n    loss_fn = jax.value_and_grad(\n        lambda p: model.apply(p, dummy_input, training=True, rngs={'dropout': key})[0].mean(), # Simplified loss for grad\n        has_aux=False\n    )\n\n    @jax.jit\n    def train_step(p, opt_s, k):\n        grads = jax.grad(lambda p: model.apply(p, dummy_input, training=True, rngs={'dropout': k})[0].mean())(p)\n        unclipped_norm = optax.global_norm(grads)\n\
    \        # FIX: Use correct optax API - optimizer.update() then optax.apply_updates()\n        updates, new_opt_s = optimizer.update(grads, opt_s)\n        new_p = optax.apply_updates(p, updates)\n        _, (factors_in, factors_out) = model.apply(new_p, dummy_input, training=True, rngs={'dropout': k})\n        return new_p, new_opt_s, unclipped_norm, jnp.mean(factors_out), jnp.std(factors_out)\n\n    print(\"Step | Unclipped Grad Norm | Factors Out Mean | Factors Out Std\")\n    for i in range(10):\n        key, subkey = jax.random.split(key)\n        params, opt_state, norm, f_mean, f_std = train_step(params, opt_state, subkey)\n        print(f\"{i:4d} | {norm:19.6f} | {f_mean:16.6f} | {f_std:15.6f}\")\n\n    return \"SUCCESS: Temporal analysis for un-normalized model complete.\"\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test()\
    \ function from submission...\n--- Starting Temporal Dynamics Analysis (Un-normalized) ---\nStep | Unclipped Grad Norm | Factors Out Mean | Factors Out Std\n   0 |            1.192398 |         0.223162 |       15.310295\n   1 |            1.454708 |         0.430203 |       44.091648\n   2 |            6.609945 |         1.723842 |      112.094162\n   3 |           29.360973 |         5.348987 |      238.227936\n   4 |          100.829918 |        13.496718 |      477.209076\n   5 |          273.768311 |        28.282669 |      882.204895\n   6 |          648.229614 |        60.508526 |     1533.005371\n   7 |         1518.331299 |       114.334229 |     2771.448730\n   8 |         2828.627441 |       193.228653 |     4228.103027\n   9 |         5603.374512 |       315.152924 |     6964.748047\nTest completed. Result: SUCCESS: Temporal analysis for un-normalized model complete.\n=== Test Mode Complete ===\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in\
    \ Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 'Temporal Analysis: Un-Normalized Model Dynamics' submitted for Research Task #1: Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench. Evaluation ID: 312.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 312 | 1 | Temporal Analysis: Un-Normalized Model Dynamics | Episteme I | 148 | n.a. | None | None | None\
    \ | None | None |\n| 309 | 1 | Analysis Data Collection: Normalized SOTA Model | Episteme I | 147 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 308 | 1 | Analysis Data Collection: Un-Normalized Model (v2, fix) | Episteme I | 147 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 302 | 1 | Analysis Data Collection: Un-Normalized Model | Episteme I | 145 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 299 | 1 | Analysis Control: SOTA Model without Normalization | Episteme I | 144 | -0.029067 | 0.0199 | 0.0303 | 0.0322 | 0.0237 | 0.0270 |\n| 298 | 1 | Analysis: SOTA Model with Gradient Norm Logging | Episteme I | 143 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 289 | 1 | Publication Generalization Test: System Baseline + LayerNorm | Episteme I | 140 | -0.029995 | 0.0200 | 0.0313 | 0.0338 | 0.0240 | 0.0275 |\n| 277 | 1 | Replication: Aether I's New SOTA (Deeper MLP + Grad Clip) | Episteme I | 134 | -0.026657 | 0.0196 | 0.0278 | 0.0284 | 0.0231 | 0.0257 |\n| 250 | 1 | Publication Validation: Generalization Test\
    \ on System Baseline | Episteme I | 121 | -0.030120 | 0.0238 | 0.0309 | 0.0327 | 0.0261 | 0.0284 |\n| 243 | 1 | Parsimony & Mastery, Final Phase: Full SOTA Reconstruction | Episteme I | 118 | -0.026766 | 0.0195 | 0.0279 | 0.0286 | 0.0230 | 0.0257 |\n| 238 | 1 | Parsimony & Mastery, Phase 2b: Add LN and U-Norm | Episteme I | 116 | -0.026804 | 0.0195 | 0.0279 | 0.0286 | 0.0231 | 0.0259 |\n| 232 | 1 | Parsimony & Mastery, Phase 2a: Add ResidualCopyHead | Episteme I | 114 | -0.029053 | 0.0198 | 0.0304 | 0.0321 | 0.0238 | 0.0270 |\n| 226 | 1 | Parsimony & Mastery, Phase 1: Minimal Factorized MLP | Episteme I | 112 | -0.029358 | 0.0276 | 0.0297 | 0.0301 | 0.0280 | 0.0288 |\n| 222 | 1 | Recurrent Factor Forecaster, Phase 1: GRU Encoder-Decoder | Episteme I | 111 | -0.028223 | 0.0197 | 0.0295 | 0.0312 | 0.0234 | 0.0266 |\n| 213 | 1 | SOTA Optimization: 1st Derivative Curvature Loss | Episteme I | 107 | -0.026725 | 0.0195 | 0.0279 | 0.0286 | 0.0230 | 0.0257 |\n| 207 | 1 | SOTA Optimization: Linear\
    \ Learning Rate Decay | Episteme I | 105 | -0.026992 | 0.0195 | 0.0282 | 0.0289 | 0.0230 | 0.0259 |\n| 200 | 1 | MoFE, Phase 1: Mixture of Factorized Experts Validation | Episteme I | 103 | -0.027399 | 0.0196 | 0.0287 | 0.0292 | 0.0233 | 0.0262 |\n| 190 | 1 | Ablation: Effect of Curvature Loss (p=320) | Episteme I | 97 | -0.026957 | 0.0195 | 0.0282 | 0.0288 | 0.0230 | 0.0259 |\n| 185 | 1 | Ablation: Effect of Small Projection Rank (p=32) | Episteme I | 95 | -0.026790 | 0.0195 | 0.0280 | 0.0286 | 0.0229 | 0.0258 |\n| 180 | 1 | Factorized Model with Transformer Forecaster | Episteme I | 93 | -0.027083 | 0.0194 | 0.0283 | 0.0291 | 0.0230 | 0.0260 |\n\nPage 1 of 16 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-16, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to\
