parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Research Counter. I have received the data from my first temporal analysis run.\n\n**1. Observe & Analyze:**\n*   **Debugger Intervention:** The debugger corrected a simple but critical bug in my `optax` API usage. This is another careless error I must learn from.\n*   **Data Analysis (ID 312, Un-normalized):** The results are staggering and conclusive.\n    *   **Unclipped Grad Norm:** `1.19 -> 1.45 -> 6.60 -> 29.36 -> 100.8 -> 273.7 -> 648.2 -> 1518.3 -> 2828.6 -> 5603.3`\n    *   **Factors Out Std:** `15.3 -> 44.0 -> 112.0 -> 238.2 -> 477.2 -> 882.2 -> 1533.0 -> 2771.4 -> 4228.1 -> 6964.7`\n*   **Conclusion:** The data shows **runaway explosive growth**. Both the unclipped gradient norm and the standard deviation of the latent factor activations are increasing exponentially. This is the smoking gun. Without normalization, the model is fundamentally unstable. The gradients explode, leading to massive, chaotic updates, which in turn cause the activations\
    \ to explode. The `clip_by_global_norm(1.0)` in the main SOTA model is not just a minor addition; it is a critical clamp that prevents this explosive feedback loop from instantly destroying the training process.\n\n**2. Formulate Plan:**\nI have my answer for the un-normalized case. Now I need to run the same analysis on the fully-normalized SOTA model. I expect to see stable, non-exploding values for both metrics.\n\n**3. Action Plan:**\n1.  **Submit the Normalized Analysis:** I will now submit the second part of my analysis: the temporal dynamics run for the fully-normalized model. The code is already prepared from my previous turn (ID 309's `test()` function). I will adapt it to use the corrected `optax` API and the mini-loop from ID 312.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Temporal Analysis: Normalized SOTA Model Dynamics\"\ntags: \"analysis, gradients, normalization, temporal-dynamics\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second part of my temporal analysis. After observing\
    \ explosive gradients and activations in the un-normalized model (ID 312), this run will collect the same statistics (unclipped grad norm, latent stats) for the fully-normalized SOTA model. The hypothesis is that these values will remain stable over the mini-training loop, demonstrating the mechanistic effect of the normalization layers.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  import jax\n\n  # --- Code for NORMALIZED SOTA Model and helpers from ID 309 ---\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual\
    \ = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(residual, deterministic=not training)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons)); output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return output + residual\n  class NormalizedSOTAModel(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; num_neurons: int = 71721\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_eff) @ V.T\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat);\
    \ h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * k)(h)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, k))\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out)\n          y_factor = (factors_out_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n          return y_factor + y_copy, (factors_in, factors_out, factors_out_norm)\n  def _define_hyperparameters(): return {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = NormalizedSOTAModel(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n          self.needs_rng = True\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input): return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n      def apply(self,\
    \ params, x, training=False, rngs=None): return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n  def create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n  def test():\n      print(\"--- Starting Temporal Dynamics Analysis (Normalized) ---\")\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      model = create_network(hparams)\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      \n      dummy_input = jnp.ones((2, 4, 71721))\n      \n      params = model.init(key, dummy_input)\n      optimizer = optax.adam(learning_rate=hparams['learning_rate'])\n      opt_state = optimizer.init(params)\n\n      @jax.jit\n      def train_step(p, opt_s, k):\n          grads = jax.grad(lambda p: model.apply(p, dummy_input, training=True, rngs={'dropout': k})[0].mean())(p)\n          unclipped_norm = optax.global_norm(grads)\n          updates, new_opt_s = optimizer.update(grads, opt_s) # Corrected API call\n          new_p = optax.apply_updates(p, updates)\n          _, (_, _, factors_out_norm) = model.apply(new_p,\
    \ dummy_input, training=True, rngs={'dropout': k})\n          return new_p, new_opt_s, unclipped_norm, jnp.mean(factors_out_norm), jnp.std(factors_out_norm)\n      \n      print(\"Step | Unclipped Grad Norm | Factors Out Mean | Factors Out Std\")\n      for i in range(10):\n          key, subkey = jax.random.split(key)\n          params, opt_state, norm, f_mean, f_std = train_step(params, opt_state, subkey)\n          print(f\"{i:4d} | {norm:19.6f} | {f_mean:16.6f} | {f_std:15.6f}\")\n\n      return \"SUCCESS: Temporal analysis for normalized model complete.\"\n```"
