tick: 152
role: model
parts:
- text: "**Reflection Tick 3 / 5: Flax Module Implementation Sketch**\n\nI will now outline the Flax module for the MoFE-FiLM model. To ensure clarity and modularity, I will structure it with a `SOTABase` module and a `MoFEFiLM` wrapper.\n\n```python\n# Assume ConvGater and ResidualCopyHead are defined elsewhere\n\nclass SOTABase(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"The SOTA model up to the pre-normalized factors.\"\"\"\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    \n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # Standard U, V factorization and encoding\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (71721, self.proj_rank))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.rank_k, self.proj_rank))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        \n        factors_in = jnp.eins.um('btn,np->btp', x, U_eff) @ V.T\n        \n        # Deeper MLP Forecaster\n        factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((x.shape[0], -1))\n\
    \        h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(512)(h)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * self.rank_k)(h)\n        \n        factors_out_pre_ln = factors_out_flat.reshape((x.shape[0], 32, self.rank_k))\n\n        # Return the necessary components for the main model\n        return factors_out_pre_ln, U_eff, V\n\nclass MoFEFiLM(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    context_dim: int = 64\n\n    def setup(self):\n        # Main body of the SOTA model\n        self.base = SOTABase(rank_k=self.rank_k, proj_rank=self.proj_rank)\n        \n        # Gating network\n        self.gater = ConvGater() # Assuming it's defined to output `context_dim` features\n        \n        # FiLM parameter generators\n        self.gamma_proj = nn.Dense(32 * self.rank_k)\n        self.beta_proj =\
    \ nn.Dense(32 * self.rank_k)\n\n        # Residual Copy Head\n        self.rc_head = ResidualCopyHead()\n\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        # 1. Get pre-normalized factors from the base model\n        factors_out_pre_ln, U_eff, V = self.base(x, training=training)\n\n        # 2. Get context vector from the gater\n        context_vector = self.gater(x)\n\n        # 3. Generate FiLM parameters\n        gamma = self.gamma_proj(context_vector).reshape(x.shape[0], 32, self.rank_k)\n        beta = self.beta_proj(context_vector).reshape(x.shape[0], 32, self.rank_k)\n        \n        # 4. Apply conditional normalization (FiLM)\n        # Manually implement LayerNorm + FiLM for clarity\n        mean = jnp.mean(factors_out_pre_ln, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n        var = jnp.var(factors_out_pre_ln, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n        normalized_factors = (factors_out_pre_ln - mean) / jnp.sqrt(var + 1e-6)\n        \n        factors_out_final = gamma * normalized_factors +\
    \ beta\n\n        # 5. Decode and add residual\n        y_factor = (factors_out_final @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        y_copy = self.rc_head(x, training=training)\n\n        return y_factor + y_copy\n```\nThis modular structure is excellent. It clearly separates the established SOTA base from my novel FiLM-based modulation. The implementation of the FiLM layer itself is straightforward. This code provides a solid blueprint for the experiment. I'll need to slightly modify my existing `ConvGater` to output a `context_dim` vector instead of logits, but that is a trivial change."
