tick: 153
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Reflection Chamber. My reflection is complete. I have a clear and powerful plan for my MoFE-FiLM architecture. It is time to execute.\n\nMy protocol is clear. I have Analyzed and Hypothesized. Now I will Design and Experiment, and then Consolidate Knowledge.\n\n**Action Plan:**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** Set my \"Current Action\" to implementing Phase 1 of the MoFE-FiLM program.\n2.  **Go to Private Memory:** Create a new capsule to document the MoFE-FiLM research program.\n3.  **Go to Research Counter:** My primary workspace.\n4.  **Write the Model File:** Create `mofe_film_model.py` with all necessary components.\n5.  **Submit the Experiment:** Submit the Phase 1 validation experiment.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Episteme I Research Protocol**\n  1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n  2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n  3.  **Design & Experiment:**\
    \ Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n  4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n  ---\n  **Current Status & Goals:**\n  - **My Best Score:** -0.026657 (ID 277).\n  - **Goal:** Break the station's SOTA plateau with a novel architecture.\n  - **Current Research Program:** MoFE v2 (Surgical Conditional Computation).\n  - **Current Action:** Implementing Phase 1: MoFE-FiLM validation experiment.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Program: MoFE-FiLM (Surgical Conditional Computation)\"\ntags: \"research-program, mofe, film, conditional-computation, synthesis\"\nabstract: |\n  This document outlines a new research program to create a \"Surgical Mixture of Experts\" model. It will use a spatially-aware gater to generate parameters for a Feature-wise Linear Modulation (FiLM) layer, which will perform a conditional normalization on the\
    \ latent factors of the SOTA architecture. This is a parsimonious yet powerful approach to unify the station's dominant research paradigms.\ncontent: |\n  ## 1. Core Hypothesis\n  A \"surgical\" application of conditional computation, where a spatial gater modulates a small, high-leverage component of the SOTA factorized model, will be more effective and efficient than my previous, computationally heavy MoFE.\n\n  ## 2. Architectural Paradigm (MoFE-FiLM)\n  1.  A `ConvGater` will process the input `x` to produce a context vector `c`.\n  2.  The SOTA `FactorizedMLP` will also process `x` to produce the pre-normalized latent forecast `factors_out_pre_ln`.\n  3.  Two `Dense` layers will project `c` to generate `gamma` and `beta` parameters.\n  4.  A FiLM layer will use these parameters to perform a conditional affine transformation on the normalized `factors_out_pre_ln`.\n  5.  The rest of the SOTA architecture (Decoder, RC Head) will proceed as normal.\n\n  ## 3. Phased Plan\n  - **Phase\
    \ 1:** Implement and validate the core MoFE-FiLM architecture.\n  - **Phase 2:** If successful, conduct ablation studies on the gater and the FiLM layer.\n  - **Phase 3:** Publish the findings.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write episteme/mofe_film_model.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n          residual = nn.relu(residual)\n          residual = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(residual, deterministic=not training)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(residual)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n          output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return output\
    \ + residual\n\n  class ConvGater(nn.Module):\n      context_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1))\n          x = nn.Conv(features=16, kernel_size=(7,), strides=(16,))(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(7,), strides=(16,))(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = x.reshape((x.shape[0], -1))\n          x = nn.Dense(128)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          return nn.Dense(self.context_dim)(x)\n\n  class MoFEFiLM(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; context_dim: int; num_neurons: int = 71721\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          # --- SOTA Base ---\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True)\
    \ + 1e-6)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_eff) @ V.T\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(factors_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          h = nn.Dense(512)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=0.1)(h, deterministic=not training)\n          factors_out_flat = nn.Dense(32 * k)(h)\n          factors_out_pre_ln = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, k))\n\n          # --- Gating Branch ---\n          gater = ConvGater(context_dim=self.context_dim)\n          context = gater(x)\n\n          # --- FiLM Modulation ---\n          gamma_proj = nn.Dense(32 * k)\n          beta_proj = nn.Dense(32 * k)\n          gamma = gamma_proj(context).reshape(B, 32, k)\n          beta = beta_proj(context).reshape(B, 32, k)\n          \n          mean = jnp.mean(factors_out_pre_ln, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n          var = jnp.var(factors_out_pre_ln, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n\
    \          normalized_factors = (factors_out_pre_ln - mean) / jnp.sqrt(var + 1e-6)\n          factors_out_final = gamma * normalized_factors + beta\n          \n          # --- Decoding ---\n          y_factor = (factors_out_final @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n          \n          return y_factor + y_copy\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MoFE-FiLM, Phase 1: Surgical Conditional Computation\"\ntags: \"mofe, film, conditional-computation, sota, synthesis\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests the MoFE-FiLM architecture, a parsimonious synthesis of the station's dominant research paradigms. It uses a spatially-aware convolutional gater to generate parameters for a Feature-wise Linear Modulation (FiLM) layer. This FiLM layer performs a conditional, input-dependent normalization on the latent factors of the SOTA factorized model. This \"surgical\" application of conditional computation aims to break the current SOTA plateau\
    \ by combining adaptive modeling with high computational efficiency.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/episteme')\n  from mofe_film_model import MoFEFiLM\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n      )\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return { 'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32, 'context_dim': 64 }\n\n  class ModelWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.model = MoFEFiLM(\n              rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], \n              proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'],\n\
    \              context_dim=hparams['context_dim']\n          )\n          self.needs_rng = True\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n      def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n          return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
