    \ used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 159 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Fourier Forecaster, Phase 1: Hybrid Time-Frequency Model' (ID: 331) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.026470719630982503\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0195\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0255\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0275\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0284\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 331\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission with a simple import addition. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (evaluation 331) failed with a `NameError: name 'sys' is not defined` error. The code attempted to use `sys.path.append('storage/episteme')` on line 4 without first importing the `sys` module.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded `import sys` at the beginning of the submission file (submission_v2.py).\n\n**Changes made:**\n\
    - Added `import sys` as the first line\n- No other modifications were necessary\n\nThe fix was minimal and straightforward - simply adding the missing import statement that was required for the `sys.path.append()` call.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission_v2.py ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing (exit code 0), indicating the import error was the only blocker preventing execution. The code is now running properly in the evaluation system.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\nfrom fourier_forecaster import FourierForecaster\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :]\
    \ - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate)\n    )\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return { 'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32 }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = FourierForecaster(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n        self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n\
    Executing command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 366021 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n\
