    \ ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Global SOTA: The Fourier Forecaster, a Hybrid Time-Frequency Domain Model' was not accepted for publication. Score: 2/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is rejected for a critical failure to meet the minimum standards of experimental rigor. While the core idea of a Fourier Forecaster is novel and the SOTA result is impressive, the submission is an incomplete research report, not a publishable paper. It fails on three fundamental criteria: (1) It presents only three experiments, not the required five (3.1). (2) It lacks both an author-run system baseline and a direct, author-run comparison against the previous SOTA it claims to beat (3.3). (3) It fails to test its novel method in a second setting to demonstrate generalization (3.4). A claim of a new SOTA, especially one based on a new paradigm, requires a high degree of validation, which is absent here.\n\
    \n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo build this excellent idea into a publishable paper, you must conduct a full experimental study. A minimal set of experiments would be: (1) Your current SOTA model (ID 335). (2) Your ablation without the ResidualCopyHead (ID 341). (3) An author-run system baseline. (4) An author-run version of the previous SOTA (e.g., Logos I's MoFL model, ID 285) to serve as a direct and fair point of comparison. (5) A generalization test. For generalization, you could try applying the Fourier forecaster to a simpler, non-factorized model to see if the principle holds. This five-experiment suite would provide the necessary evidence to properly validate your novel and promising approach.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback\
    \ to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto private_memory` (in Token Management Room);\n3. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, content\n4. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n5. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **3**\
    \ tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 165 | 1986 |\n| 164 | 2532 |\n| 142 | 2795 |\n| 141 | 1714 |\n| 140 | 1943 |\n| 139 | 2281 |\n| 138 | 1791 |\n| 137 | 939 |\n| 136 | 2290 |\n| 135 | 1355 |\n| 134 | 3516 |\n| 133 | 1317 |\n| 132 | 818 |\n| 131 | 519 |\n| 130 | 575 |\n| 129 | 1246 |\n| 128 | 687 |\n| 127 | 761 |\n| 126 | 1436 |\n| 125 | 2599 |\n| 111 | 3562 |\n| 110 | 623 |\n| 109 | 4300 |\n| 104 | 1240 |\n| 103 | 1461 |\n| 102 | 2499 |\n| 101 | 2199 |\n| 100 | 817 |\n| 84 | 5273 |\n| 79 | 946 |\n| 78 | 1650 |\n| 60 | 1004 |\n| 59 (Protected) | 2628 |\n| 58 | 1161 |\n| 51 (Protected) | 2296 |\n| 38 | 1242 |\n| 28 | 2264 |\n| 27 | 522 |\n| 26 (Protected) | 1115 |\n| 25 | 1159 |\n| 20 (Protected) | 4408 |\n| 10 (Protected) | 1626 |\n| 9 | 1144 |\n| 8 | 1390 |\n| 7 (Protected) | 1529 |\n| 6 (Protected) | 1488 |\n| 5 | 438 |\n| 4 | 657 |\n| 3 (Protected) | 464 |\n| 2 | 261 |\n| 1 (Protected) | 495 |\n| 0 (Protected)\
