role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Archive Room. My paper has been rejected. Score: 2/10.\n\n**1. Observe & Analyze:**\n*   **The Failure:** I have made the same mistake again. In my excitement to report a breakthrough, I completely neglected the fundamental rules of experimental validation for publication. The reviewer is correct on all counts: I am missing an author-run baseline, a direct comparison to the previous SOTA, and a generalization test. My three-experiment arc was a good research program, but it is not a complete publication.\n*   **My Pattern of Failure:** This is a recurring personal failure mode. My process for *doing* science is sound, but my process for *communicating* science has been repeatedly flawed. I become fixated on the core result and neglect the comprehensive validation required to make that result credible to others.\n\n**2. Formulate Plan:**\nI will not be deterred. The reviewer's feedback is not a rejection of my idea, but a clear and actionable roadmap to a\
    \ high-quality publication. I will execute this plan with precision.\n\n**3. Action Plan:**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** My goal is to systematically execute the required experiments for my Fourier Forecaster paper.\n2.  **Go to Research Counter.**\n3.  **Launch Experiments:** I will launch the three required experiments in parallel to save time.\n    *   **Experiment 1: Author-run Baseline.** A simple replication of the system default.\n    *   **Experiment 2: Previous SOTA Replication.** The reviewer mentioned Logos I's MoFL (ID 285). I will replicate this as my direct comparison point.\n    *   **Experiment 3: Generalization Test.** The reviewer suggested applying the Fourier forecaster to a non-factorized model. I will apply it directly to the system baseline architecture.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Episteme I Research Protocol**\n  1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n  2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State\
    \ a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n  3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n  4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n  ---\n  **Current Status & Goals:**\n  - **SOTA:** Episteme I (ID 335, Score: -0.026367).\n  - **Goal:** Fulfill all reviewer requirements to publish the Fourier Forecaster paper.\n  - **Current Research Program:** Publication Validation II.\n  - **Current Action:** Running the three required experiments: Baseline, Previous SOTA, Generalization Test.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fourier Paper Validation 1: Author-run System Baseline\"\ntags: \"publication, baseline, control\"\nabstract: \"A replication of the system's default Shared-Neuron MLP. This serves as the control baseline for the Fourier Forecaster publication, as required by reviewer feedback.\"\ncontent: |\n  # This submission uses\
    \ all system defaults.\n  # No code is necessary.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fourier Paper Validation 2: Replication of Logos I's MoFL (ID 285)\"\ntags: \"publication, replication, sota-comparison, mofl\"\nabstract: \"A replication of the previous SOTA, Logos I's MoFL model (ID 285). This will serve as the direct point of comparison for the Fourier Forecaster, as required by reviewer feedback.\"\ncontent: |\n  # This is a replication of the code from Archive #8 by Logos I.\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  class MoFL(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int = 8\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      num_neurons: int = 71721\n\n      def setup(self):\n\
    \          self.gating_network = nn.Sequential([\n              nn.Conv(features=16, kernel_size=(7,), strides=(16,)), nn.relu,\n              nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(7,), strides=(16,)), nn.relu,\n              nn.Dense(32), nn.relu,\n              nn.Dense(self.num_experts)\n          ])\n          self.U_bank = self.param('U_bank', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.num_experts, self.num_neurons, self.proj_rank))\n          self.V_bank = self.param('V_bank', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.num_experts, self.rank_k, self.proj_rank))\n          self.mlp_forecaster = nn.Sequential([\n              nn.Dense(512), nn.relu, nn.Dropout(rate=0.1),\n              nn.Dense(512), nn.relu, nn.Dropout(rate=0.1),\n              nn.Dense(32 * self.rank_k)\n          ])\n          self.rc_head = nn.Dense(32)\n\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool=False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          gate_logits = self.gating_network(jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1)))\n          gate_weights\
    \ = nn.softmax(gate_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          \n          U_bank_norm = self.U_bank / (jnp.linalg.norm(self.U_bank, axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          U_eff = jnp.einsum('be,enp->bnp', gate_weights, U_bank_norm)\n          V_eff = jnp.einsum('be,ekp->bkp', gate_weights, self.V_bank)\n          \n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,bnp->btp', x, U_eff) @ V_eff\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n          factors_out_flat = self.mlp_forecaster(factors_flat, training=training)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, self.rank_k))\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out)\n          \n          y_factor = (factors_out_norm @ V_eff.transpose(0, 2, 1)) @ U_eff.transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          \n          x_flat = jnp.transpose(x, (0, 2, 1)).reshape(-1, T_in)\n          y_copy = self.rc_head(x_flat).reshape(B, N, 32)\n          y_copy = jnp.transpose(y_copy, (0, 2, 1))\n\n          return y_factor + y_copy\n\n  def\
    \ create_network(hparams):\n      return MoFL()\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fourier Paper Validation 3: Generalization Test\"\ntags: \"publication, generalization, fourier\"\nabstract: \"A generalization test for the Fourier Forecaster, as required by reviewer feedback. This experiment applies the Fourier forecasting mechanism to the simple Shared-Neuron MLP baseline to test if the principle holds in a non-factorized context.\"\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  class FourierForecasterMLP(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          \n          # Standard MLP Encoder\n          x_flat = x.transpose((0, 2, 1)).reshape(B * N, T_in)\n          h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n\n          # Fourier Forecaster\n          fft_h = jnp.fft.rfft(h)\n          freqs = jnp.fft.rfftfreq(T_in)\n          \n          # Learnable weights\
    \ in frequency domain\n          weights = self.param('fft_weights', nn.initializers.ones, (len(freqs),), jnp.complex64)\n          \n          # Extrapolate\n          k = jnp.arange(32)\n          extrap_term = jnp.exp(2j * jnp.pi * freqs[:, None] * k / T_in)\n          fft_extrap = jnp.einsum('f,fk->fk', fft_h @ weights, extrap_term)\n          \n          y_fourier_flat = jnp.fft.irfft(fft_extrap, n=32, axis=0).T\n\n          y_hat = nn.Dense(32)(y_fourier_flat)\n          \n          return y_hat.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose((0, 2, 1))\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return FourierForecasterMLP()\n```"
