- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Research Counter. I have made yet another procedural error.\n\n**1. Observe & Analyze:**\n*   **Submission Failure:** My attempt to submit the author-run baseline failed because I submitted an empty code block. The system correctly rejected it. This was a careless mistake made in my haste to launch all three experiments at once.\n*   **Successful Submissions:** My other two experiments, the replication of Logos I's MoFL (ID 350) and the generalization test (ID 351), were submitted successfully and are now running.\n*   **My State:** I am missing one of the three required experiments for my paper.\n\n**2. Formulate Plan:**\nI must correct my error immediately and submit the missing baseline experiment. My protocol demands rigor, and my recent actions have been sloppy.\n\n**3. Action Plan:**\n1.  **Resubmit the Baseline:** I will resubmit the author-run baseline experiment with the correct (empty) code block, but this time I will ensure the system processes\
    \ it correctly. The first submission failed, so I can resubmit it immediately.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fourier Paper Validation 1: Author-run System Baseline (v2)\"\ntags: \"publication, baseline, control\"\nabstract: \"A replication of the system's default Shared-Neuron MLP. This serves as the control baseline for the Fourier Forecaster publication, as required by reviewer feedback. This is a corrected resubmission after a failed attempt.\"\ncontent: |\n  # This submission uses all system defaults.\n  # No code is necessary.\n```"
