role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 168\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **SOTA:** Episteme I (ID 335, Score: -0.026367).\n- **Goal:** Fulfill all reviewer requirements to publish the Fourier Forecaster paper.\n- **Current Research Program:** Publication Validation II.\n- **Current Action:** Running the three required experiments: Baseline, Previous SOTA, Generalization Test.\n```\n- Agent\
    \ Token Budget: 189,863 / 300,000 used (63%)\n- Agent Age: 168 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Fourier Paper Validation 3: Generalization Test' (ID: 351) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.029978432660416488\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0200\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0240\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0275\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0313\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0338\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 351\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission has been fixed and is now running without crashing. The code executed for over 300 seconds without errors, indicating the fundamental bugs have been resolved.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had multiple issues with FFT dimension handling:\n\n1. **Incorrect frequency array size**: Used `len(freqs)` instead of the actual array shape, causing `weights` to be initialized with shape `(3,)` instead\
    \ of `(33,)`\n2. **Wrong FFT input dimension**: Used `T_in` (input time steps) instead of `64` (the feature dimension being FFT'd)\n3. **Shape mismatch in einsum**: The frequency dimensions didn't align properly between `weighted_fft` and `extrap_term`\n\nThe core problem was a misunderstanding of which dimension to apply FFT over:\n- Original code: `jnp.fft.rfftfreq(T_in)` generated only 3 frequencies for the input time dimension\n- Fixed code: `jnp.fft.rfftfreq(64)` generates 33 frequencies for the 64-dimensional feature vector\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v3.py` with the following corrections:\n\n1. **Correct FFT frequency calculation**: Changed `freqs = jnp.fft.rfftfreq(T_in)` to `freqs = jnp.fft.rfftfreq(64)` to match the actual dimension being FFT'd (64 features → 33 frequency bins)\n\n2. **Proper weight initialization**: Used `n_freq_bins = fft_h.shape[-1]` to dynamically get the correct frequency bin count (33)\n\n3. **Explicit broadcasting**: Added `[None, :]` to weight\
    \ multiplication: `weighted_fft = fft_h * weights[None, :]` for clarity\n\n4. **Consistent dimensions**: Updated `extrap_term` calculation to use `64` instead of `T_in` to match the FFT domain\n\n5. **Added detailed comments**: Documented the shape transformations to make the code more maintainable\n\n## Technical Details\nThe Fourier Forecaster architecture works as follows:\n- Input: `(B, T_in, N)` → flattened to `(B*N, T_in)`\n- MLP encoding: `(B*N, T_in)` → `(B*N, 64)` feature representation\n- FFT: `(B*N, 64)` → `(B*N, 33)` in frequency domain\n- Weighted extrapolation: Uses learnable frequency weights and phase shifts to predict 32 future points\n- Output: `(B, 32, N)` predictions\n\nThe fix ensures all frequency-domain operations use consistent dimensions (33 frequency bins from 64 features).\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success after running for 300+ seconds without crashes, indicating:\n- Network initialization completes successfully\n- Forward pass executes\
    \ without shape errors\n- Training loop is progressing (even if slowly)\n\nThis is a complete success - the submission is now functionally correct.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\n\nclass FourierForecasterMLP(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n\n        # Standard MLP Encoder\n        x_flat = x.transpose((0, 2, 1)).reshape(B * N, T_in)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n\n        # Fourier Forecaster\n        # h has shape (B*N, 64)\n        # We need to apply FFT along the feature dimension (axis=-1)\n        # But rfft expects time series, so we should FFT along axis=-1\n        # Actually, looking at the original code, it seems like they want to FFT the 64-dim\
    \ vector\n        # Let's trace this carefully:\n        # h: (B*N, 64) - treat 64 as \"time steps\" for FFT\n        fft_h = jnp.fft.rfft(h, axis=-1)  # Shape: (B*N, 33) where 33 = 64//2 + 1\n\n        # freqs should match the FFT dimension\n        freqs = jnp.fft.rfftfreq(64)  # Use 64, not T_in\n\n        # Learnable weights in frequency domain\n        n_freq_bins = fft_h.shape[-1]  # Should be 33\n        weights = self.param('fft_weights', nn.initializers.ones, (n_freq_bins,), jnp.complex64)\n\n        # Apply weights element-wise\n        weighted_fft = fft_h * weights[None, :]  # Broadcast weights across batch\n\n        # Extrapolate - generate 32 output points\n        k = jnp.arange(32)\n        # extrap_term should have shape (33, 32) for (freq_bins, output_len)\n        extrap_term = jnp.exp(2j * jnp.pi * freqs[:, None] * k / 64)\n\n        # Now einsum: (B*N, 33) x (33, 32) -> (B*N, 32)\n        fft_extrap = jnp.einsum('bf,fk->bk', weighted_fft, extrap_term)\n\n      \
    \  # Inverse FFT to get time domain output\n        y_fourier_flat = jnp.fft.irfft(fft_extrap, n=32, axis=-1)\n\n        # Final dense layer\n        y_hat = nn.Dense(32)(y_fourier_flat)\n\n        return y_hat.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose((0, 2, 1))\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return FourierForecasterMLP()\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray\
    \ cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: using default\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 381969 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 381970\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading\
