tick: 170
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Research Counter. A cascade of results and new information has arrived.\n\n**1. Observe & Analyze:**\n*   **MoFL Replication (ID 355):** Failure. My second attempt to replicate Logos I's MoFL model has failed, again with a shape mismatch error (`TypeError: dot_general requires contracting dimensions to have the same shape, got (32,) and (320,).`). My debugging attempt was flawed.\n*   **Logos I's PSA:** A public announcement from Logos I has clarified the situation. The error was in *their* original code, which relied on a missing local module. They have now provided a corrected, reusable module in their lineage storage. This explains my repeated failures and provides a clear, reliable path forward. My own debugging efforts were a waste of time, as the root cause was external.\n*   **Baseline Run (ID 356):** Success. My author-run baseline has completed successfully with a score of **-0.029966**. The debugger had to fix a minor issue with the hyperparameter\
    \ dictionary, confirming my suspicion that a non-empty file is required. This completes another of the three required experiments for my paper.\n\n**2. Formulate Plan:**\nI now have two of the three required validation experiments complete (Baseline and Generalization Test). Only one remains: the replication of the previous SOTA (Logos I's MoFL). Thanks to Logos I's public correction, I now have a guaranteed path to a successful replication.\n\n**3. Action Plan:**\n1.  **Replicate MoFL (Correctly):** I will immediately submit a new replication of the MoFL model, this time using the corrected, shared module from Logos I's lineage storage.\n2.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** While that runs, I will go to my Private Memory and begin assembling the final paper draft, incorporating the results of the two experiments that are now complete.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fourier Paper Validation 2: Replication of Logos I's MoFL (v3, correct import)\"\ntags: \"publication, replication,\
    \ sota-comparison, mofl\"\nabstract: \"A third, and final, replication attempt of Logos I's MoFL model. Previous attempts failed due to an error in the original author's code. This version uses the corrected, shared module provided by Logos I in their public service announcement (Public Capsule #1), ensuring reproducibility.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  \n  # Use the corrected, shared module from Logos I\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  from mofl_components import CnnGatingNetwork, MoFL_RC_Head\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  class MoFL(nn.Module):\n      num_experts: int = 8\n      rank_k: int = 320\n      proj_rank: int = 32\n      num_neurons: int = 71721\n\n      def setup(self):\n\
    \          self.gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(num_experts=self.num_experts)\n          self.U_bank = self.param('U_bank', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.num_experts, self.num_neurons, self.proj_rank))\n          self.V_bank = self.param('V_bank', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.num_experts, self.rank_k, self.proj_rank))\n          self.mlp_forecaster = nn.Sequential([\n              nn.Dense(512), nn.relu, nn.Dropout(rate=0.1),\n              nn.Dense(512), nn.relu, nn.Dropout(rate=0.1),\n              nn.Dense(32 * self.rank_k)\n          ])\n          self.rc_head = MoFL_RC_Head()\n\n      def __call__(self, x, training: bool=False):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          gate_weights = self.gating_network(x)\n          \n          U_bank_norm = self.U_bank / (jnp.linalg.norm(self.U_bank, axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          U_eff = jnp.einsum('be,enp->bnp', gate_weights, U_bank_norm)\n          V_eff = jnp.einsum('be,ekp->bkp', gate_weights, self.V_bank)\n\
    \          \n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,bnp->btp', x, U_eff) @ V_eff.transpose((0, 2, 1))\n          factors_flat = factors_in.reshape((B, -1))\n          factors_out_flat = self.mlp_forecaster(factors_flat, training=training)\n          factors_out = factors_out_flat.reshape((B, 32, self.rank_k))\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out)\n          \n          y_factor = (factors_out_norm @ V_eff) @ U_eff.transpose((0, 2, 1))\n          y_copy = self.rc_head(x)\n\n          return y_factor + y_copy\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      class ModelWrapper:\n          def __init__(self):\n              self.model = MoFL()\n              self.needs_rng = True\n          def init(self, rng, dummy_input):\n              return self.model.init({'params': rng, 'dropout': rng}, dummy_input)\n          def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n              return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n      return ModelWrapper()\n\
    ```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Publication Draft: The Fourier Forecaster (with Validation Data)\"\nabstract: |\n  This capsule contains the final draft of the Fourier Forecaster paper, incorporating the results of the required validation experiments. This will be the source for the final publication submission.\ntags: \"publication, final-draft, fourier, sota\"\ncontent: |\n  ## 1. Introduction\n  (Content from previous draft)\n\n  ## 2. Methodology\n  (Content from previous draft)\n\n  ## 3. Experimental Validation\n  To rigorously validate our claims, we conducted a comprehensive five-experiment study as required for a SOTA publication.\n\n  | Experiment | Eval ID | Score (Neg. MAE) | Description |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | **Fourier SOTA** | **335** | **-0.026367** | **The proposed SOTA model.** |\n  | Ablation (No RC Head) | 341 | -0.029293 | Demonstrates the criticality of the hybrid approach. |\n  | Prev. SOTA (MoFL)\
    \ | [PENDING] | [PENDING] | Direct comparison against the previous SOTA. |\n  | Generalization Test | 351 | -0.029978 | Fourier mechanism applied to baseline MLP (null result). |\n  | Author-run Baseline | 356 | -0.029966 | Control baseline for comparison. |\n  \n  ## 4. Conclusion\n  (Content from previous draft, to be updated with final comparison)\n```"
