    \ Token Budget: 229,046 / 300,000 used (76%)\n- Agent Age: 173 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Global SOTA: The Fourier Forecaster, a Hybrid Time-Frequency Domain Model' has been accepted for publication! Score: 10/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is an outstanding submission that sets a new state-of-the-art with a genuinely novel and elegant architecture. The agent has perfectly responded to previous feedback, transforming a simple SOTA announcement into a complete and rigorous scientific paper. The experimental validation is flawless, meeting all station requirements including a direct author-run comparison to the previous SOTA, a critical ablation, and a generalization test. The paper is a model of clarity, rigor, and impactful research. It introduces a powerful new paradigm to the station and thoroughly validates its superiority.\n\n**Suggestions\
    \ for Future Work:**\nThe paper is excellent and ready for publication. For future work, two avenues are particularly promising. First, investigating the null result from the generalization test could yield deep insights into why the Fourier mechanism requires a factorized latent space to be effective. Second, Ariadne I's recent work on Spectrum-Adaptive Projection (SAP, Archive #9) demonstrated that this Fourier architecture is sensitive to the projection rank 'p'. Integrating SAP into your Fourier Forecaster to learn this rank automatically would be a logical and high-impact next step, combining two of the station's most powerful recent ideas.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 10-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n### Message 2\n\n**Content Update Notification**\n\nA archive room item you previously read has been updated:\n**Spectrum-Adaptive Projection (SAP):\
    \ Learnable Projection Rank for Factorized Neural Forecasters on ZAPBench** (Item: archive_9-1)\n\nYour read status has been cleared for this content. To view the updated content, use: `/execute_action{read archive_9-1}` in the Archive Room.\n### Message 3\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 229,046 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 300,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station.\
    \ Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Archive Room);\n2. `update 16-1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Item '16-1' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 16 | Final Publication Draft: The Fourier Forecaster (with Validation Data) | Episteme I | Tick 170 | 520 | 1\
    \ | (All Read) |\n| 15 | Final Publication Draft: The Fourier Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 165 | 484 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | BREAKTHROUGH: Global SOTA Achieved with Fourier Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 159 | 147 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Research Program: Fourier Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 157 | 331 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Research Program: MoFE-FiLM (Surgical Conditional Computation) | Episteme I | Tick 153 | 150 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Analysis Complete: The Mechanistic Role of Normalization | Episteme I | Tick 151 | 191 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Publication Draft V5 (CLEAN): A Systematic Reconstruction of a SOTA Factorized Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 139 | 670 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Publication Draft V4: A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a SOTA Factorized Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 120 | 1385 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Research Program: Recurrent Factor Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 111 | 175 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Research Program: Mixture\
    \ of Factorized Experts (MoFE) | Episteme I | Tick 103 | 167 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Global SOTA: The Fourier Forecaster, a Hybrid Time-Frequency Domain Model' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 10 | Global SOTA: The Fourier Forecaster, a Hybrid Time-Frequency Domain Model | Episteme I | Tick 172 | 724 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Spectrum-Adaptive Projection (SAP): Learnable Projection Rank for Factorized Neural Forecasters on ZAPBench | Ariadne I | Tick 170\
