parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 176\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **SOTA:** Episteme I (ID 335, Score: -0.026367). PUBLISHED (Archive #10).\n- **Goal:** Be the first to successfully synthesize SAP and the Fourier Forecaster.\n- **Current Research Program:** SAP-Fourier Synthesis.\n- **Current Action:** Implementing the SAP-Fourier model.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 239,194 / 300,000\
    \ used (80%)\n- Agent Age: 176 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Synthesis: SAP-Fourier Forecaster' (ID: 365) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.028749035619117496\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0234\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0253\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0272\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0291\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0318\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 365\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The code has been fixed and is now running without crashing. The submission has been running for over 300 seconds, confirming that the fix resolved the KeyError issue.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a parameter path mismatch in the `compute_loss` function. The function was trying to access the SAP module's gate parameters using:\n```python\ngate_params = params['params']['SAP']['gates']\n```\n\nHowever, when the SAP module was instantiated inside the\
    \ SAPFourierForecaster without an explicit name, Flax/Linen assigned it an auto-generated name (likely `SAP_0` or similar). This caused a `KeyError: 'SAP'` when the loss function tried to access the parameters.\n\nThe error occurred during the simple CPU validation phase when testing the `compute_loss` function:\n```\nFile \"/submission.py\", line 12, in compute_loss\n    gate_params = params['params']['SAP']['gates']\n                  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^\nKeyError: 'SAP'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Single-line fix in submission_v2.py:**\n\nChanged line 62 in the SAPFourierForecaster class from:\n```python\nU_gated, V_gated = SAP(max_proj_rank=p_max)(U, V)\n```\n\nTo:\n```python\nU_gated, V_gated = SAP(max_proj_rank=p_max, name='SAP')(U, V)\n```\n\nBy explicitly naming the SAP module with `name='SAP'`, the parameter dictionary structure now matches what the `compute_loss` function expects. The gate parameters are now accessible at `params['params']['SAP']['gates']`, ensuring consistency\
    \ between model definition and loss computation.\n\n## Verification\nThe fix was verified by running `monitor_evaluation.py 2`, which confirmed:\n- The code successfully passed the CPU validation phase\n- The code ran for over 300 seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- No new errors were encountered\n\n## Technical Note\nIn Flax/Linen, when you don't explicitly name a submodule, it gets an auto-generated name based on its class name and instance count. Explicitly naming modules is a best practice when you need to access their parameters directly in custom functions like loss computation.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\n\n# --- Loss Function with Gate Sparsity ---\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions\
    \ - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n\n    # L1 Sparsity on the gates - Fixed parameter path\n    # The SAP module is nested inside SAPFourierForecaster\n    gate_params = params['params']['SAP']['gates']\n    gates = nn.sigmoid(gate_params)\n    sparsity_loss = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(gates))\n\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen + 1e-5 * sparsity_loss\n\n# --- Core Model Components ---\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(x_flat)\n        residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n        output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return output + residual\n\nclass SAP(nn.Module):\n    max_proj_rank: int\n \
    \   @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, U, V):\n        gates_raw = self.param('gates', nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.1), (self.max_proj_rank,))\n        gates = nn.sigmoid(gates_raw)\n        # Apply gates to the columns of U and V\n        U_gated = U * jnp.sqrt(gates)[None, :]\n        V_gated = V * jnp.sqrt(gates)[None, :]\n        return U_gated, V_gated\n\n# --- Main SAP-Fourier Model ---\nclass SAPFourierForecaster(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    max_proj_rank: int\n    num_neurons: int = 71721\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p_max = self.rank_k, self.max_proj_rank\n\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p_max))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p_max))\n\n        U_gated, V_gated = SAP(max_proj_rank=p_max, name='SAP')(U, V)\n\n        U_eff = U_gated / (jnp.linalg.norm(U_gated, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp',\
    \ x, U_eff) @ V_gated.T\n\n        # Fourier Forecaster Branch\n        fft_in = jnp.fft.rfft(factors_in, axis=1)\n        fft_weights = self.param('fft_weights', nn.initializers.ones, (fft_in.shape[1],), jnp.complex64)\n        fft_out = fft_in * fft_weights[None, :, None]\n        factors_out_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(fft_out, n=32, axis=1)\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fourier)\n\n        y_fourier = (factors_out_norm @ V_gated) @ U_eff.T\n\n        # Residual Copy Branch\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x, training=training)\n\n        return y_fourier + y_copy\n\n# --- Boilerplate ---\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return { 'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'max_proj_rank': 48 }\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    class ModelWrapper:\n        def __init__(self, hparams):\n            self.model\
    \ = SAPFourierForecaster(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], max_proj_rank=hparams['max_proj_rank'])\n            self.needs_rng = False # No dropout\n        def init(self, rng, dummy_input): return self.model.init(rng, dummy_input)\n        def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None): return self.model.apply(params, x)\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000005\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL\
    \ RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 392207 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 392208\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.001,\
    \ 'rank_k': 320, 'max_proj_rank': 48}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.042855   |   0.034437  \n   2    |   0.031737   |   0.031046  \n   3    |   0.029548   |   0.030120  \n   4    |   0.028695   |   0.029672  \n   5    |   0.028180   |   0.029351  \n   6    |   0.027864   |   0.029301  \n   7    |   0.027570   |   0.029378  \n   8    |   0.027319   |   0.029004  \n   9    |   0.027063   |   0.028885  \n  10    |   0.026903   |   0.029047  \n  11    |   0.026811   |   0.029074  \n  12    |   0.026720   |   0.029065  \n  13    |   0.026671   |   0.028951  \n  14    |   0.026642   |   0.029036  \n  15    |   0.026571   |   0.028969  \n  16    |   0.026537   |   0.028937  \n  17    |   0.026492\
    \   |   0.028998  \n  18    |   0.026462   |   0.028915  \n  19    |   0.026429   |   0.029029  \n  20    |   0.026409   |   0.028990  \n  21    |   0.026376   |   0.028885  \n  22    |   0.026343   |   0.028980  \n  23    |   0.026322   |   0.028954  \n  24    |   0.026275   |   0.028851  \n  25    |   0.026258   |   0.028932  \n  26    |   0.026230   |   0.028773  \n  27    |   0.026204   |   0.028783  \n  28    |   0.026194   |   0.028925  \n  29    |   0.026170   |   0.028767  \n  30    |   0.026152   |   0.028820  \n  31    |   0.026132   |   0.028802  \n  32    |   0.026128   |   0.028823  \n  33    |   0.026109   |   0.028936  \n  34    |   0.026093   |   0.028866  \n  35    |   0.026098   |   0.028761  \n  36    |   0.026083   |   0.028767  \n  37    |   0.026070   |   0.028855  \n  38    |   0.026064   |   0.028818  \n  39    |   0.026061   |   0.028747  \n  40    |   0.026052   |   0.028809  \n  41    |   0.026043   |   0.028748  \n  42    |   0.026037   |   0.028853  \n  43\
    \    |   0.026038   |   0.028831  \n  44    |   0.026037   |   0.028842  \n  45    |   0.026033   |   0.028818  \n  46    |   0.026023   |   0.028808  \n  47    |   0.026029   |   0.028754  \n  48    |   0.026020   |   0.028828  \n  49    |   0.026015   |   0.028784  \n  50    |   0.026010   |   0.028835  \n  51    |   0.026013   |   0.028737  \n  52    |   0.026005   |   0.028806  \n  53    |   0.026003   |   0.028902  \n  54    |   0.025993   |   0.028758  \n  55    |   0.026006   |   0.028795  \n  56    |   0.025995   |   0.028920  \n  57    |   0.025992   |   0.028809  \n  58    |   0.025991   |   0.028778  \n  59    |   0.025981   |   0.028800  \n  60    |   0.025987   |   0.028828  \n  61    |   0.025982   |   0.028829  \n  62    |   0.025983   |   0.028858  \n  63    |   0.025978   |   0.028900  \n  64    |   0.025974   |   0.028834  \n  65    |   0.025975   |   0.028832  \n  66    |   0.025974   |   0.028766  \n  67    |   0.025975   |   0.028812  \n  68    |   0.025969   | \
