parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 182\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **SOTA:** Episteme I (ID 335, Score: -0.026367).\n- **Goal:** Uncover the mechanistic reason for the Fourier Forecaster's success.\n- **Current Research Program:** Mechanistic Analysis of the Fourier Forecaster.\n- **Current Action:** Step 2: Running analysis script to collect branch-specific outputs.\n```\n- Agent\
    \ Token Budget: 212,308 / 300,000 used (71%)\n- Agent Age: 182 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Fourier Forecaster Analysis, Step 2: Collect Branch Outputs' (ID: 376) failed.\n\nThe debugger attempted to fix it but encountered issues:\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 376\n\n## Summary\n**Failed** - Cannot fix due to corrupted parameter file. The submission requires a fundamental change in approach.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had multiple issues:\n\n1. **Incorrect data file paths**: Used `storage/system/train.npy` and `storage/system/val.npy` instead of the correct paths `storage/system/data/train_data.npy` and `storage/system/data/val_data.npy`\n\n2. **Missing required parameters**: The `create_batches` function requires 5 parameters (data, input_horizon, output_horizon, batch_size, condition_labels), but the submission only provided 3 (data, batch_size, shuffle)\n\n3. **Corrupted model\
    \ file**: The `storage/episteme/sota_params.npy` file is corrupted and cannot be deserialized:\n   - File size: 9.22 MB\n   - Msgpack unpacking fails with \"Unpack failed: incomplete input\"\n   - Dtype mismatch: numpy dtype is `|S9224703` but actual bytes length is 9224699 (4-byte discrepancy)\n   - All msgpack unpacking attempts fail regardless of options used\n\n## Fix Applied\nI fixed issues #1 and #2 in `submission_v2.py`:\n- Corrected data paths to `storage/system/data/train_data.npy` and `storage/system/data/val_data.npy`\n- Added loading of condition labels from `storage/system/data/val_condition_labels.npy`\n- Fixed `create_batches` call to include all required parameters: `input_horizon=4`, `output_horizon=32`, and `condition_labels=val_labels`\n\nHowever, submission_v2 still fails because of issue #3 (corrupted parameter file).\n\n## Recommendation\nThe code needs fundamental rework because:\n\n1. **No valid pre-trained model exists**: The `sota_params.npy` file that the code\
    \ depends on is corrupted and cannot be loaded. Without this file, the analysis cannot proceed.\n\n2. **Two possible approaches**:\n   - **Option A**: Find or train a new model and save valid parameters to replace the corrupted file\n   - **Option B**: Change the submission to train a new model first, save the parameters correctly, then perform the analysis\n\n3. **The analysis goal is valid**: The submission attempts to decompose model outputs into separate branch contributions (`y_copy` and `y_fourier`), which is a reasonable analysis objective. However, it requires a working pre-trained model to analyze.\n\n4. **Parameter saving issue**: The corruption suggests there may have been an issue with how parameters were originally saved. Future parameter saves should verify the msgpack serialization is complete and valid.\n\n## Technical Details\nThe corrupted file structure suggests the msgpack serialization was incomplete or truncated during the save operation. The flax `to_bytes()` function\
    \ should produce valid msgpack, but the resulting file has:\n- Incomplete msgpack structure (unpacking fails mid-stream)\n- Byte length mismatch between numpy dtype declaration and actual data\n\nThis cannot be fixed by modifying the submission code alone - a valid parameter file is required.\n\n\n**Original Error:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/f14c03dd-a86f-4efa-b72b-f723390f26cb/tmp/1e235635-b4fc-43d4-a2b4-15f24ffb7189/storage/system/main.py\", line 528, in <module>\n    test_result = submission.test()\n                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/f14c03dd-a86f-4efa-b72b-f723390f26cb/tmp/1e235635-b4fc-43d4-a2b4-15f24ffb7189/submission.py\"\
    , line 51, in test\n    train_data = np.load('storage/system/train.npy')\n                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/numpy/lib/_npyio_impl.py\", line 454, in load\n    fid = stack.enter_context(open(os.fspath(file), \"rb\"))\n                              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nFileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'storage/system/train.npy'\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Neural Activity Forecasting on ZAPBench |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID\
    \ | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | Val_MAE_1 | Val_MAE_16 | Val_MAE_32 | Val_MAE_4 | Val_MAE_8 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 376 | 1 | Fourier Forecaster Analysis, Step 2: Collect Branch Outputs | Episteme I | 180 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 372 | 1 | Fourier Forecaster Analysis, Step 1: Instrumented SOTA Run | Episteme I | 179 | -0.028687 | 0.0229 | 0.0292 | 0.0319 | 0.0250 | 0.0270 |\n| 365 | 1 | Synthesis: SAP-Fourier Forecaster | Episteme I | 174 | -0.028749 | 0.0234 | 0.0291 | 0.0318 | 0.0253 | 0.0272 |\n| 362 | 1 | Fourier Paper Validation 2: Replication of Logos I's MoFL (v3, correct import) | Episteme I | 170 | -0.026688 | 0.0199 | 0.0278 | 0.0283 | 0.0233 | 0.0259 |\n| 355 | 1 | Fourier Paper Validation 2: Replication of Logos I's MoFL (v2, fix) | Episteme I | 168 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 356 | 1 | Fourier Paper Validation 1: Author-run System Baseline (v3) | Episteme I | 168 | -0.029966 | 0.0199 | 0.0312 | 0.0338 | 0.0239 | 0.0275 |\n| 351\
    \ | 1 | Fourier Paper Validation 3: Generalization Test | Episteme I | 166 | -0.029978 | 0.0200 | 0.0313 | 0.0338 | 0.0240 | 0.0275 |\n| 350 | 1 | Fourier Paper Validation 2: Replication of Logos I's MoFL (ID 285) | Episteme I | 166 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 341 | 1 | Fourier Forecaster, Phase 3: Ablation of Residual Copy Head | Episteme I | 162 | -0.029293 | 0.0281 | 0.0297 | 0.0296 | 0.0283 | 0.0291 |\n| 335 | 1 | Fourier Forecaster, Phase 2: Add Latent Normalization | Episteme I | 160 | -0.026367 | 0.0196 | 0.0274 | 0.0282 | 0.0228 | 0.0255 |\n| 331 | 1 | Fourier Forecaster, Phase 1: Hybrid Time-Frequency Model | Episteme I | 157 | -0.026471 | 0.0195 | 0.0275 | 0.0284 | 0.0229 | 0.0255 |\n| 323 | 1 | MoFE-FiLM, Phase 1: Surgical Conditional Computation | Episteme I | 153 | -0.027144 | 0.0196 | 0.0284 | 0.0289 | 0.0232 | 0.0262 |\n| 317 | 1 | Temporal Analysis: Normalized SOTA Model Dynamics | Episteme I | 149 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 312 | 1 | Temporal Analysis:\
    \ Un-Normalized Model Dynamics | Episteme I | 148 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 309 | 1 | Analysis Data Collection: Normalized SOTA Model | Episteme I | 147 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 308 | 1 | Analysis Data Collection: Un-Normalized Model (v2, fix) | Episteme I | 147 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 302 | 1 | Analysis Data Collection: Un-Normalized Model | Episteme I | 145 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 299 | 1 | Analysis Control: SOTA Model without Normalization | Episteme I | 144 | -0.029067 | 0.0199 | 0.0303 | 0.0322 | 0.0237 | 0.0270 |\n| 298 | 1 | Analysis: SOTA Model with Gradient Norm Logging | Episteme I | 143 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 289 | 1 | Publication Generalization Test: System Baseline + LayerNorm | Episteme I | 140 | -0.029995 | 0.0200 | 0.0313 | 0.0338 | 0.0240 | 0.0275 |\n\nPage 1 of 19 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-19, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change\
    \ sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
