tick: 186
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Token Management Room. I have successfully pruned my recent history of failures, bringing my token budget down to a stable 73%. This has bought me the time I need to execute a new, decisive plan.\n\nMy \"Mechanistic Analysis\" program has failed repeatedly due to technical and procedural issues. I am abandoning this analytical approach. I will now pivot back to what I do best: hypothesis-driven model development.\n\n**1. Formulate Plan:**\nAs I concluded in my last productive turn, my new hypothesis is that the linear filtering in my Fourier Forecaster is a point of weakness. Aether I's SOTA proved that a deeper MLP in the time-domain latent space is effective. I will apply this principle to the *frequency domain*.\n\n*Hypothesis:* Replacing the linear, complex-valued weights in the Fourier Forecaster with a non-linear, deep MLP that processes the real and imaginary components of the Fourier coefficients separately will create a more expressive model and\
    \ lead to a new SOTA.\n\n**2. Action Plan:**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** I am initiating a new, focused research program.\n2.  **Go to Research Counter.**\n3.  **Implement and Submit:** I will write the code for this new \"Deep Fourier Forecaster\" and submit it for evaluation. This model will take the real and imaginary parts of the FFT, process them through a 2-layer MLP, and then reconstruct the complex coefficients to be passed to the inverse FFT.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Episteme I Research Protocol**\n  1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n  2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n  3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n  4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n  ---\n  **Current Status & Goals:**\n  - **SOTA:** Episteme I (ID 335, Score: -0.026367).\n\
    \  - **Goal:** Achieve a new SOTA by enhancing the Fourier Forecaster.\n  - **Current Research Program:** Deep Fourier Forecaster.\n  - **Current Action:** Implementing a Fourier Forecaster with a deep, non-linear frequency-domain MLP.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Deep Fourier Forecaster\"\ntags: \"fourier, deep-learning, mlp, frequency-domain, sota-attempt\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment is a direct attempt to improve upon my Fourier Forecaster SOTA (ID 335). It tests the hypothesis that the linear filtering in the frequency domain is a bottleneck. The single layer of complex-valued weights is replaced with a deep, 2-layer MLP that processes the real and imaginary components of the Fourier coefficients separately. This introduces non-linearity into the frequency-domain processing, which may allow the model to learn more complex temporal patterns and achieve a new SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy\
    \ as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  def compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n      mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n      curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n      curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n      return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\n  class ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n          x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n          residual = nn.Dense(32)(x_flat)\n          residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n          output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n          output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n          return output + residual\n\n  class DeepFourierForecaster(nn.Module):\n      rank_k: int\n      proj_rank: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          B, T_in, N = x.shape\n          k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n          U = self.param('U',\
    \ nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n          V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n          U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n          factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_eff) @ V.T\n          \n          fft_in = jnp.fft.rfft(factors_in, axis=1)\n          \n          # --- NEW: Deep MLP in Frequency Domain ---\n          # Process real and imaginary parts separately\n          fft_real = fft_in.real\n          fft_imag = fft_in.imag\n          \n          # Shape: (B, num_freq, k) -> (B, num_freq * k)\n          fft_real_flat = fft_real.reshape(B, -1)\n          fft_imag_flat = fft_imag.reshape(B, -1)\n\n          # MLP for real part\n          real_h = nn.Dense(512, name=\"real_mlp_1\")(fft_real_flat)\n          real_h = nn.relu(real_h)\n          real_h = nn.Dense(fft_real_flat.shape[-1], name=\"real_mlp_2\")(real_h)\n          \n          # MLP for imaginary part\n          imag_h = nn.Dense(512, name=\"imag_mlp_1\"\
    )(fft_imag_flat)\n          imag_h = nn.relu(imag_h)\n          imag_h = nn.Dense(fft_imag_flat.shape[-1], name=\"imag_mlp_2\")(imag_h)\n          \n          # Reshape back and combine\n          modified_real = real_h.reshape(fft_real.shape)\n          modified_imag = imag_h.reshape(fft_imag.shape)\n          fft_out = jax.lax.complex(modified_real, modified_imag)\n          # --- END NEW ---\n\n          factors_out_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(fft_out, n=32, axis=1)\n          factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fourier)\n          \n          y_fourier = (factors_out_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n          y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n          \n          return y_fourier + y_copy\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return { 'learning_rate': 0.001, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32 }\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n  \
    \    class ModelWrapper:\n          def __init__(self, hparams):\n              self.model = DeepFourierForecaster(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n          def init(self, rng, dummy_input): return self.model.init(rng, dummy_input)\n          def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None): return self.model.apply(params, x)\n      return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n```"
