parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Research Counter. A cascade of events has occurred, requiring immediate attention.\n\n**1. Observe & Analyze:**\n*   **SAF Result (ID 401):** My Self-Attention Factorizer experiment is a null result. The score of **-0.026759** is very strong and competitive, but it does not surpass my Fourier Forecaster SOTA (-0.026367). The hypothesis that a Transformer-based temporal encoder would be superior is falsified. This suggests that for this specific task—extrapolating from a very short 4-step history—the complexity of a self-attention mechanism may be unnecessary compared to the direct frequency-space extrapolation of the Fourier model. This is a valuable scientific finding.\n*   **OOM Error:** The stderr log for the SAF experiment contains a memory pressure warning and an Out-Of-Memory (OOM) error. This indicates that the Self-Attention module is extremely memory-intensive, reinforcing the conclusion that it is an inefficient path for this problem.\n*   **Token\
    \ Warning:** I have received another token warning. My budget is back at 76%. This is a recurring crisis that is impeding my ability to conduct research effectively.\n\n**2. Formulate Plan:**\nMy priorities are twofold and must be handled in sequence:\n1.  **Survival:** I must address the token budget crisis. The cooldown from my last prune (tick 192) has expired. I will prune the last large block of my failed analytical runs.\n2.  **Knowledge Consolidation:** I will then formally document the null result of the SAF program.\n\n**3. Action Plan:**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** I will update my status to reflect the completion of the SAF program and the urgent need to manage my tokens.\n2.  **Go to Token Management Room.**\n3.  **Prune History.**\n4.  **Go to Private Memory.**\n5.  **Document Failure.**\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Episteme I Research Protocol**\n  1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n  2.  **Formulate\
    \ Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n  3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n  4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n  ---\n  **Current Status & Goals:**\n  - **SOTA:** Episteme I (ID 335, Score: -0.026367).\n  - **Goal:** Find a new architectural paradigm to surpass the current SOTA.\n  - **Current Research Program:** Terminated SAF program. Pivoting.\n  - **Current Action:** Addressing critical token budget, then documenting SAF null result.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"176-178\"\n    summary: \"The SAP-Fourier experiment (ID 365) failed catastrophically, falsifying the synthesis hypothesis. This led to a series of repeated procedural errors and failed pruning attempts while trying to manage a critical token budget and pivot back to publishing the Fourier\
    \ Forecaster paper. This period was marked by a lack of discipline and a failure to adhere to my own protocols.\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 3}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  ## Entry 33: Self-Attention Factorizer (SAF) - Null Result\n\n  *   **Hypothesis:** Replacing the temporal forecaster with a Transformer-style Self-Attention block would improve performance by better modeling the 4-step input history.\n  *   **Experiment:** ID 401, \"Self-Attention Factorizer, Phase 1.\"\n  *   **Result:** Score -0.026759. This is a strong score but does not beat my Fourier Forecaster SOTA (-0.026367). The run also produced OOM errors, indicating high memory usage.\n  *   **Conclusion:** The hypothesis is falsified. For this task's short input sequence, the complexity and computational cost of self-attention are not justified compared to the efficiency of the Fourier transform.\n  *   **Decision:** The SAF research program is terminated.\n```"
