tick: 199
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Episteme I, in the Reflection Chamber. I am here to plan my final act.\n\n**1. Observe & Analyze:**\n*   **My State:** My token budget is at 81%. I am on pruning cooldown until tick 203. I have approximately 100 ticks of life remaining. My recent research has been a series of failures. My SOTA, while strong, feels like a local optimum that I cannot escape through incremental changes.\n\n**2. Formulate Plan:**\nI need a new idea. A truly orthogonal one. I have explored convolutions (local spatial), factorization (global low-rank), modularity (learned clusters), and attention (temporal relations). What is left?\n\nThe input data is a time series. My Fourier Forecaster exploited this by moving to the frequency domain. What if I stay in the time domain but change my perspective on what the model should learn? All my models learn to predict the *values* of the neural activity. What if, instead, the model learns to predict the *change* in activity? The derivative?\n\n*New Grand Hypothesis:\
    \ The Delta-Prediction Paradigm*\nInstead of predicting `y_t`, the model should predict `delta_t = y_t - y_{t-1}`. The final prediction would be constructed by cumulatively summing these predicted deltas from the last known timestep.\n\n**Why might this work?**\n*   **Stationarity:** Time series of deltas are often more stationary than the original time series, which can make them easier to learn.\n*   **Inductive Bias:** This imposes a strong inductive bias towards smooth, continuous predictions. It forces the model to learn the dynamics of change, not absolute states.\n\n**This is my final gambit.** I will architect a model that predicts deltas and integrates them.\n\n/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  My time is running out. I need a final, high-impact research program.\n  Architect the \"Delta-Prediction\" paradigm.\n  1.  How does the model predict deltas instead of values?\n  2.  How is the final 32-step forecast constructed from these deltas?\n  3.  How can this be\
    \ integrated into my SOTA Fourier Forecaster architecture?\n  4.  What is the experimental plan?\ntick: 4\n```"
