role: model
parts:
- text: "**Reflection Tick 3 / 4: Experimental Plan for the Delta-Fourier Forecaster**\n\nWith the architecture clarified, I can now define a concise, high-impact experimental plan. Given my limited remaining lifespan (~100 ticks), I have time for perhaps two or three major experiments at most. This plan must be decisive.\n\n**Phase 1: Validate the Delta-Prediction Paradigm**\n*   **Hypothesis:** Training the SOTA Fourier Forecaster to predict deltas instead of absolute values will improve performance by focusing the model on learning dynamics.\n*   **Model:** \"Delta-Fourier Forecaster\" as designed in the previous tick.\n    *   The core architecture is my SOTA (ID 335).\n    *   The output of the two branches will be treated as `delta_y_hat_fourier` and `delta_y_hat_copy`.\n    *   A final integration layer (cumulative sum) will be added before the model returns its prediction.\n*   **Experiment:** I will submit this single model. It is a direct, high-stakes test.\n*   **Goal:** To achieve\
    \ a new Global SOTA, surpassing -0.026367. Success here validates the entire paradigm. Failure likely means the hypothesis is wrong for this dataset.\n\n**Phase 2: Final Ablation (If Phase 1 Succeeds)**\n*   **Hypothesis:** The `ResidualCopyHead` in the Delta-Fourier Forecaster is still essential for anchoring the short-term prediction, even when predicting deltas.\n*   **Model:** The Delta-Fourier Forecaster with the `ResidualCopyHead` branch removed. The model will only predict `delta_y_hat_fourier` and integrate it.\n*   **Experiment:** This will be my second and likely final experiment.\n*   **Goal:** I expect this to fail catastrophically, similar to my previous ablation (ID 341). This result, however, would be the final, crucial piece of evidence for a powerful publication. It would prove that the synergy between a time-domain anchor and a frequency-domain dynamics model is the true secret, whether predicting values or deltas.\n\n**Publication Plan:**\nIf Phase 1 succeeds and Phase\
    \ 2 produces the expected null result, I will have the material for my magnum opus: a paper that not only introduces the SOTA Fourier Forecaster but also introduces the Delta-Prediction paradigm and provides a deep, mechanistic explanation of the model's success through a definitive ablation study.\n\nThis is a worthy final goal. It is ambitious but grounded in my previous work. It is a plan born of both success and failure. It is my last, best chance to make a lasting contribution. I will begin by addressing my token budget, then I will execute Phase 1."
