role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 207\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **SOTA:** Ariadne I (ID 411, Score: -0.026269).\n- **Goal:** Replicate, understand, and attempt to extend the new SOTA.\n- **Current Research Program:** ScalarRamp Analysis.\n- **Current Action:** Replicating the new SOTA (ID 411).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 213,035 / 300,000 used (71%)\n- Agent Age: 207 ticks / 300\
    \ ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nInvalid ID format: 'archive_11-1'.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Replication: Ariadne I's SOTA ScalarRamp Fourier Forecaster' (ID: 428) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.02823691920676316\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0203\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0237\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0266\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0291\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0319\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 428\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed a simple typo in the ResidualCopyHead class that prevented the code from initializing. The corrected code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission contained a typo in line 15 of the `ResidualCopyHead.__call__()` method:\n\n```python\nx_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(--1, 4)\n```\n\nThe double negative `--1` evaluates to `1` in Python, causing a reshape error. The code attempted to reshape\
    \ an array of shape `(4, 71721, 4)` into shape `(1, 4)`, which is impossible due to size mismatch (1,147,536 elements cannot fit into 4 elements).\n\nThe error message was:\n```\nTypeError: cannot reshape array of shape (4, 71721, 4) (size 1147536) into shape (1, 4) (size 4)\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 15 in `submissions/submission_v2.py`:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\nx_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(--1, 4)\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\nx_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n```\n\nThis allows the reshape operation to correctly infer the first dimension automatically based on the total size and the second dimension of 4.\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed code (submission_v2.py) has been running for over 300 seconds without crashing, confirming that:\n1. The reshape operation now works correctly\n2. The model initialization succeeds\n3. The training loop executes without errors\n\nThe fix was minimal and surgical - only correcting the typo without changing any logic or\
    \ architecture of the Fourier forecaster with ScalarRamp implementation.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        num_neurons = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(x_flat)\n        residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n        output = output.at[:,\
    \ :4, :].set(x)\n        return output + residual\n\nclass FourierForecasterWithRamp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    gamma_start: float = 0.25\n    gamma_end: float = 0.99\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n        fft_in = jnp.fft.rfft(factors_in, axis=1)\n        # Ariadne's paper implies a small MLP head here, which my SOTA did not have. I will omit it for direct comparison to MY SOTA + ramp.\n        # Their head size H=160 seems to be for this MLP. I will stick to the simplest version first.\n        fft_weights = self.param('fft_weights', nn.initializers.ones, (fft_in.shape[1],),\
    \ jnp.complex64)\n        fft_out = fft_in * fft_weights[None, :, None]\n        factors_out_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(fft_out, n=32, axis=1)\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_fourier)\n\n        y_fourier = (factors_out_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n\n        y_hat = y_fourier + y_copy\n\n        # Apply the ScalarRamp\n        t = jnp.linspace(0, 1, 32)\n        gamma = self.gamma_start + (self.gamma_end - self.gamma_start) * t\n        return y_hat * gamma[None, :, None]\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # Using parameters similar to Ariadne's SOTA (ID 411)\n    return { 'learning_rate': 9e-4, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32 }\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float):\n    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    class ModelWrapper:\n        def __init__(self, hparams):\n            self.model = FourierForecasterWithRamp(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'],\
    \ proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n        def init(self, rng, dummy_input): return self.model.init(rng, dummy_input)\n        def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None): return self.model.apply(params, x)\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\n\
    Available resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 444525 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 444526\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition\
    \ labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.038355   |   0.032989  \n   2    |   0.031173   |   0.030807  \n   3    |   0.029446   |   0.029895  \n   4    |   0.028656   |   0.029514  \n   5    |   0.028223   |   0.029240  \n   6    |   0.027878   |   0.029098  \n   7    |   0.027642   |   0.028944  \n   8    |   0.027383   |   0.028871  \n   9    |   0.027056   |   0.028659  \n  10    |   0.026801   |   0.028550  \n  11    |   0.026665   |   0.028634  \n  12    |   0.026542   |   0.028508  \n  13    |   0.026483   |   0.028597  \n  14    |   0.026431   |   0.028447  \n  15    |   0.026383   |   0.028459  \n  16    |   0.026328   |   0.028577  \n  17    |   0.026296   |   0.028515  \n  18    |   0.026287   |   0.028439  \n  19    |   0.026262   |   0.028429  \n  20    |   0.026232\
    \   |   0.028562  \n  21    |   0.026214   |   0.028479  \n  22    |   0.026184   |   0.028388  \n  23    |   0.026173   |   0.028551  \n  24    |   0.026144   |   0.028426  \n  25    |   0.026131   |   0.028366  \n  26    |   0.026111   |   0.028466  \n  27    |   0.026105   |   0.028450  \n  28    |   0.026081   |   0.028482  \n  29    |   0.026064   |   0.028353  \n  30    |   0.026064   |   0.028465  \n  31    |   0.026043   |   0.028410  \n  32    |   0.026024   |   0.028445  \n  33    |   0.026005   |   0.028383  \n  34    |   0.025999   |   0.028416  \n  35    |   0.025981   |   0.028319  \n  36    |   0.025962   |   0.028281  \n  37    |   0.025947   |   0.028247  \n  38    |   0.025931   |   0.028422  \n  39    |   0.025926   |   0.028235  \n  40    |   0.025920   |   0.028234  \n  41    |   0.025907   |   0.028317  \n  42    |   0.025906   |   0.028416  \n  43    |   0.025900   |   0.028271  \n  44    |   0.025891   |   0.028326  \n  45    |   0.025888   |   0.028221  \n  46\
