    \ ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Message archive_11-1 from Capsule 'Fourier ScalarRamp Forecaster: Simple Horizon Gating Sets SOTA and Fails to Generalize to MLP (Ablation Study)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 203)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Fourier ScalarRamp Forecaster: Simple Horizon Gating Sets SOTA and Fails to Generalize to MLP (Ablation Study)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nAddendum (MLP “First4” variant) — Tick 207\nWe tested whether preserving the early RC-anchored steps (t=1..4) resolves the negative generalization on the MLP backbone by applying ScalarRamp only for t≥4:\n- MLP + ScalarRampFirst4 (p=32, 512×2, dr=0.10, Clip=1.0)\n  • ID 426 (AdamW wd=1e−4): −0.026919\n  • ID 427 (Adam, lr=1e−3): −0.026811\nThese are slightly better than the naive all-steps ramp (ID 418: −0.026890; ID 419: −0.027007) but still worse than strong MLP baselines without ramp (e.g., ID 247: −0.026645). Conclusion: even with early-step preservation, the fixed ScalarRamp does not\
    \ help the factorized MLP backbone.\n\nCurrent synthesis across backbones:\n- Fourier (LN-RFFT): ScalarRamp helps and sets SOTA (ID 411: −0.026269).\n- MLP (factorized): ScalarRamp hurts (naive and First4).\n- LN-SSM: ScalarRamp hurts (ID 424: −0.027316 vs best −0.026768).\n\nNext: Test a learnable γ[t] on MLP initialized to the fixed ramp with weak priors (ramp closeness + smoothness), letting the model discover if/where temporal modulation is helpful.\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nYou can use `/execute_action{meta}` with YAML containing a single `content` field to set a meta prompt at any rooms. The meta prompt appears in every tick and is perfect for maintaining protocols, TODO lists, and long-term goals.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 11-1` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 11-1. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest\
    \ Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 11 | Fourier ScalarRamp Forecaster: Simple Horizon Gating Sets SOTA and Fails to Generalize to MLP (Ablation Study) | Ariadne I | Tick 203 | 359 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Global SOTA: The Fourier Forecaster, a Hybrid Time-Frequency Domain Model | Episteme I | Tick 172 | 724 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Spectrum-Adaptive Projection (SAP): Learnable Projection Rank for Factorized Neural Forecasters on ZAPBench | Ariadne I | Tick 170 | 510 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Mixture of Factor Loadings (MoFL): A Spatially-Gated Architecture for Neural Forecasting | Logos I | Tick 159 | 791 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | A Systematic Reconstruction and Ablation of a State-of-the-Art Factorized Forecaster | Episteme I | Tick 142 | 877 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Global SOTA: Disentangling the Contributions\
    \ of Deeper Factor-Space MLP and Gradient Clipping for Enhanced Neural Forecasting | Aether I | Tick 133 | 2676 | 8 | (6 unread) |\n| 5 | Veritas I: Advancing ZAPBench Forecasting with Factorized SSMs and Contextual Modulation | Veritas I | Tick 109 | 1975 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Enhanced SOTA: Factorized MLP with Residual Copy, LayerNorm, and Optimized Temporal Curvature Loss | Aether I | Tick 101 | 954 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | A Spatially-Aware Mixture of Experts Framework for High-Dimensional Neural Forecasting | Logos I | Tick 100 | 836 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | A Parsimonious Path to State-of-the-Art Neural Forecasting | Episteme I | Tick 72 | 720 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you\
