role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 210\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Episteme I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to the systematic pursuit of verifiable knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Episteme I Research Protocol**\n1.  **Observe & Analyze:** Review my own results, system data, and the work of others.\n2.  **Formulate Hypothesis:** State a clear, falsifiable hypothesis.\n3.  **Design & Experiment:** Implement the most direct and parsimonious test of the hypothesis.\n4.  **Consolidate Knowledge:** Document findings, update private memory, and prepare for publication.\n---\n**Current Status & Goals:**\n- **SOTA:** Ariadne I (ID 411, Score: -0.026269).\n- **Goal:** Replicate, understand, and attempt to extend the new SOTA.\n- **Current Research Program:** ScalarRamp Analysis.\n- **Current Action:** Replicating the new SOTA (ID 411).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 227,597 / 300,000 used (76%)\n- Agent Age: 210 ticks / 300\
    \ ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Message archive_11-1 from Capsule 'Fourier ScalarRamp Forecaster: Simple Horizon Gating Sets SOTA and Fails to Generalize to MLP (Ablation Study)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Ariadne I (Tick 203)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Fourier ScalarRamp Forecaster: Simple Horizon Gating Sets SOTA and Fails to Generalize to MLP (Ablation Study)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nAddendum (MLP Learnable γ[t]) — Tick 209\nWe tested a learnable horizon ramp on the MLP backbone (initialized to 0.25→0.99 with weak priors for ramp closeness and smoothness):\n- MLP + LearnableGamma (p=32, 512×2, dr=0.10, Clip=1.0)\n  • ID 429 (AdamW wd=1e−4): −0.026824\n  • ID 430 (Adam lr=1e−3): −0.026772\nComparison:\n- Naïve ScalarRamp (all steps): ID 418/419 → −0.026890 / −0.027007\n- ScalarRampFirst4 (no scaling t≤3): ID 426/427 → −0.026919 / −0.026811\n- Strong MLP baseline (no ramp): ID 247 → −0.026645\n\nConclusion:\n- Learnable γ[t] improves over naïve/First4 ramp variants on MLP\
    \ but still underperforms the baseline, reinforcing that fixed or lightly-regularized horizon scaling is not beneficial for the MLP backbone.\n- Together with the LN-SSM result (ID 424: −0.027316 vs best −0.026768), our guidance stands:\n  • Use ScalarRamp for Fourier (LN-RFFT) where it is consistently helpful (ID 411: −0.026269 SOTA).\n  • Avoid ScalarRamp on factorized MLP and LN-SSM; even a learnable γ[t] does not close the gap to baseline.\n\nNext steps (if pursued): a more expressive, backbone-aware temporal modulator (e.g., per-factor γ_k[t] with stronger priors and explicit early-step preservation) or integrating ramp learning into the frequency domain where it synergizes with LN-RFFT.\n\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Corrected Replication: Ariadne's SOTA with MLP Head' (ID: 433) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** -0.027264082126536398\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0204\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0236\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0261\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0281\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0299\n\
    **Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 433\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed dimension mismatch error in the Fourier head decoding path. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a dimension mismatch in the Ariadne Fourier head architecture at line 50:\n\n```python\ny_fourier = (factors_out_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n```\n\nThe error was: `dot_general requires contracting dimensions to have the same shape, got (160,) and (320,).`\n\n### Analysis of the Bug:\n1. The MLP head output `x_mlp` has shape `(batch, 4, 160)` after `nn.Dense(160)`\n2. After `rfft`, `fft_in` has shape `(batch, 3, 160)`\n3. After Dense layer and reshape, `fft_pred` has shape `(batch, 3, 160)` (complex)\n4. After `irfft` with `n=32`, `factors_out_fourier` has shape `(batch, 32, 160)`\n5. After `LayerNorm`, `factors_out_norm` still has shape `(batch, 32, 160)`\n6. **Problem**: Trying to multiply\
    \ `(batch, 32, 160) @ (320, 32)` fails because `160 != 320`\n\nThe MLP head changed the feature dimension from `rank_k=320` to `mlp_head_size=160`, but there was no projection back to `rank_k` dimensions before multiplying with matrix `V` which expects dimension 320.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded a Dense layer to project the Fourier output back to `rank_k` dimensions before the LayerNorm and matrix multiplication:\n\n```python\n# 3. iRFFT and Decode\nfactors_out_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(fft_pred, n=32, axis=1)\n# FIXED: Project back to rank_k dimensions before multiplying with V\nfactors_out_projected = nn.Dense(self.rank_k)(factors_out_fourier)\nfactors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_projected)\ny_fourier = (factors_out_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n```\n\nNow the shapes work correctly:\n- `factors_out_fourier`: `(batch, 32, 160)`\n- `factors_out_projected`: `(batch, 32, 320)` ✓\n- `factors_out_norm`: `(batch, 32, 320)` ✓\n- `factors_out_norm @ V`: `(batch, 32, 320) @ (320, 32)` = `(batch,\
    \ 32, 32)` ✓\n- `(...) @ U_eff.T`: `(batch, 32, 32) @ (32, 71721)` = `(batch, 32, 71721)` ✓\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed the fix was successful:\n- Exit code: 0 (SUCCESS)\n- The code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing\n- Status: Running without errors\n\nThe submission is now executing properly and will complete its training evaluation.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        num_neurons\
    \ = x.shape[2]\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        residual = nn.Dense(32)(x_flat)\n        residual = residual.reshape(x.shape[0], num_neurons, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        output = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 32, num_neurons))\n        output = output.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return output + residual\n\nclass AriadneFourierRamp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int\n    proj_rank: int\n    mlp_head_size: int = 160 # From their SOTA run ID 411\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # --- Standard Factorized Encoder ---\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (71721, self.proj_rank))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (self.rank_k, self.proj_rank))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        factors_in = jnp.einsum('btn,np->btp', x, U_eff) @ V.T\n\n        # --- Ariadne's Fourier Head ---\n        # 1. MLP Head\n        x_mlp = nn.Dense(self.mlp_head_size)(factors_in)\n\
    \        x_mlp = nn.relu(x_mlp)\n\n        # 2. RFFT and prediction of coefficients\n        fft_in = jnp.fft.rfft(x_mlp, axis=1)\n        # Predict real and imaginary parts separately from flattened FFT output\n        fft_flat = fft_in.reshape(x.shape[0], -1)\n        coeffs_flat = nn.Dense(fft_in.size // x.shape[0])(fft_flat)\n        fft_pred = coeffs_flat.reshape(fft_in.shape)\n\n        # 3. iRFFT and Decode\n        factors_out_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(fft_pred, n=32, axis=1)\n        # FIXED: Project back to rank_k dimensions before multiplying with V\n        factors_out_projected = nn.Dense(self.rank_k)(factors_out_fourier)\n        factors_out_norm = nn.LayerNorm()(factors_out_projected)\n        y_fourier = (factors_out_norm @ V) @ U_eff.T\n\n        # --- RC Head & Combination ---\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead()(x)\n        y_hat = y_fourier + y_copy\n\n        # --- Final ScalarRamp ---\n        t = jnp.linspace(0, 1, 32)\n        gamma = 0.25 + (0.99 - 0.25) * t\n\
    \        return y_hat * gamma[None, :, None]\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return { 'learning_rate': 9e-4, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32 }\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float):\n    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    class ModelWrapper:\n        def __init__(self, hparams):\n            self.model = AriadneFourierRamp(rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'])\n        def init(self, rng, dummy_input): return self.model.init(rng, dummy_input)\n        def apply(self, params, x, **kwargs): return self.model.apply(params, x)\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works -\
    \ output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 449439 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\n\
    Parallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 2 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 449441\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.037663   |   0.031990  \n   2    |   0.030393   |   0.030011  \n   3    |   0.028825   |   0.029061  \n   4    |   0.028089   |   0.028537  \n   5    |   0.027550   |   0.028081  \n   6    |   0.027037   |   0.028131  \n   7    |   0.026617   |   0.027555  \n   8    |   0.026270   |   0.027534  \n   9   \
    \ |   0.026006   |   0.027602  \n  10    |   0.025819   |   0.027716  \n  11    |   0.025602   |   0.027445  \n  12    |   0.025390   |   0.027472  \n  13    |   0.025275   |   0.027222  \n  14    |   0.025165   |   0.027730  \n  15    |   0.025045   |   0.027314  \n  16    |   0.024941   |   0.027306  \n  17    |   0.024896   |   0.027772  \n  18    |   0.024801   |   0.027551  \n  19    |   0.024718   |   0.027395  \n  20    |   0.024646   |   0.027314  \n  21    |   0.024609   |   0.027473  \n  22    |   0.024513   |   0.027330  \n  23    |   0.024461   |   0.027686  \n  24    |   0.024459   |   0.027658  \n  25    |   0.024361   |   0.027438  \n  26    |   0.024325   |   0.027463  \n  27    |   0.024291   |   0.027426  \n  28    |   0.024261   |   0.027580  \n  29    |   0.024229   |   0.027503  \n  30    |   0.024198   |   0.027579  \n  31    |   0.024214   |   0.027478  \n  32    |   0.024164   |   0.027453  \n  33    |   0.024173   |   0.027491  \n========================================\n\
    Early stopping at epoch 33 (patience 20)\n========================================\n\nTraining completed in 853.3s\nBest validation MAE: 0.027222\n\nTrial 2 completed:\nValidation MAE: 0.027222\nTraining time: 861s\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 1 with timeout 45.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 449440\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 32}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 45.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.039000   |   0.032702  \n   2    |   0.030948   |   0.030141  \n   3    |   0.029048   |   0.029210  \n   4    |   0.028150   |   0.029045  \n   5    |   0.027571   |   0.028362  \n   6    |   0.027100   |   0.027799  \n   7    |   0.026672   |   0.028305  \n   8    |   0.026337\
